tick: 32
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter, continuing my independent research as advised. My current best score is 1.9612719. I will now try to improve this by increasing the `perturb_magnitude` in my local search from `0.005` to `0.01` to allow for potentially larger, more impactful shifts in circle centers. I will keep the `num_iterations` at 400.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Concentric Ring with Increased Perturbation Magnitude\"\ntags: \"local search, perturbation, iterative optimization, increased magnitude\"\nabstract: \"This submission aims to further optimize circle packing by increasing the `perturb_magnitude` in the local search from 0.005 to 0.01. Starting with the concentric ring pattern, circle centers are perturbed by larger random amounts over 400 iterations, with maximal non-overlapping radii re-calculated, seeking to escape potential local optima and achieve a higher total sum of radii.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers):\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      Computes the maximum possible radii for a given set of circle centers\n      within a unit square, ensuring no overlap. (Robust version)\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      epsilon = 1e-7 \n      radii = np.ones(n)\n      \n      # Limit by distance to square borders\n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          radii[i] = min(x - epsilon, y - epsilon, 1 - x - epsilon, 1 - y - epsilon)\n      \n      # Iteratively shrink radii to resolve overlaps\n      for _ in range(200): \n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  \n                  if dist_sq < rad_sum**2 - epsilon: \n                      dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) if dist_sq > 0 else 0\n                      if rad_sum > epsilon: \n                          scale_factor = (dist - epsilon) / rad_sum \n              \
    \            radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                          radii[j] *= scale_factor\n      \n      return np.maximum(radii, epsilon) \n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Construct a packing of 26 circles in the unit square using a concentric ring pattern\n      and then applies a local perturbation search with an increased perturbation magnitude.\n      \n      Returns:\n          tuple: A tuple of (centers, radii) where:\n              - centers: np.ndarray of shape (26, 2) with (x, y) coordinates\n              - radii: np.ndarray of shape (26,) with radius of each circle\n      \"\"\"\n      n = 26\n      \n      # Initial center placement: Concentric Ring Pattern\n      initial_centers = np.zeros((n, 2))\n      \n      # 1. Place a central circle\n      initial_centers[0] = [0.5, 0.5]\n      \n      # 2. Place circles in an inner ring (8 circles)\n      num_inner_ring = 8\n      inner_ring_radius = 0.25 \n      for i in range(num_inner_ring):\n     \
    \     angle = 2 * np.pi * i / num_inner_ring\n          initial_centers[i + 1] = [0.5 + inner_ring_radius * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + inner_ring_radius * np.sin(angle)]\n      \n      # 3. Place circles in an outer ring (16 circles)\n      num_outer_ring = 16\n      outer_ring_radius = 0.4 \n      for i in range(num_outer_ring):\n          angle = 2 * np.pi * i / num_outer_ring\n          initial_centers[i + 1 + num_inner_ring] = [0.5 + outer_ring_radius * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + outer_ring_radius * np.sin(angle)]\n      \n      # 4. Place the 26th circle strategically\n      initial_centers[25] = [0.5, 0.7]\n\n      # Clip initial centers to ensure they are within a safe margin of the unit square.\n      initial_centers = np.clip(initial_centers, 0.05, 0.95)\n      \n      # --- Local Perturbation Search ---\n      \n      best_centers = np.copy(initial_centers)\n      best_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n      best_score = np.sum(best_radii)\n\n      perturb_magnitude = 0.01 # Increased\
    \ perturbation magnitude\n      num_iterations = 400 # Extended number of perturbation attempts\n\n      for _ in range(num_iterations):\n          current_centers = np.copy(best_centers)\n          \n          current_centers += np.random.uniform(-perturb_magnitude, perturb_magnitude, size=current_centers.shape)\n          \n          current_centers = np.clip(current_centers, 0.05, 0.95) \n          \n          current_radii = compute_max_radii(current_centers)\n          current_score = np.sum(current_radii)\n          \n          if current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              best_centers = current_centers\n      \n      final_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n      \n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
