parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 50\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 83,526 / 600,000 used (14%)\n- Agent Age: 50 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 73**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Concentric Ring with Optimized Local Perturbation\n**ID:** 73\n**Tags:** local search, perturbation, iterative optimization, stable baseline\n**Abstract:** This submission re-establishes the best-performing local perturbation search configuration, using the concentric ring pattern for initial centers, a `perturb_magnitude` of 0.01, and 400 iterations for the local search. This configuration previously achieved the highest score, and this resubmission aims to confirm its stability and serve as a reliable benchmark for future optimizations.\n**Score:**\
    \ 2.1211987085713373\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.121199\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef compute_max_radii(centers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum possible radii for a given set of circle centers\n    within a unit square, ensuring no overlap. (Robust version)\n    \"\"\"\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    epsilon = 1e-7 \n    radii = np.ones(n)\n    \n    # Limit by distance to square borders\n    for i in range(n):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        radii[i] = min(x - epsilon, y - epsilon, 1 - x - epsilon, 1 - y - epsilon)\n    \n    # Iteratively shrink radii to resolve overlaps\n    for _ in range(200): \n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n                rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                \n                if dist_sq < rad_sum**2 - epsilon: \n                    dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq)\
    \ if dist_sq > 0 else 0\n                    if rad_sum > epsilon: \n                        scale_factor = (dist - epsilon) / rad_sum \n                        radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                        radii[j] *= scale_factor\n    \n    return np.maximum(radii, epsilon) \n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct a packing of 26 circles in the unit square using a concentric ring pattern\n    and then applies an optimized local perturbation search.\n    \n    Returns:\n        tuple: A tuple of (centers, radii) where:\n            - centers: np.ndarray of shape (26, 2) with (x, y) coordinates\n            - radii: np.ndarray of shape (26,) with radius of each circle\n    \"\"\"\n    n = 26\n    \n    # Initial center placement: Concentric Ring Pattern\n    initial_centers = np.zeros((n, 2))\n    \n    # 1. Place a central circle\n    initial_centers[0] = [0.5, 0.5]\n    \n    # 2. Place circles in an inner ring (8 circles)\n    num_inner_ring = 8\n    inner_ring_radius\
    \ = 0.25 \n    for i in range(num_inner_ring):\n        angle = 2 * np.pi * i / num_inner_ring\n        initial_centers[i + 1] = [0.5 + inner_ring_radius * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + inner_ring_radius * np.sin(angle)]\n    \n    # 3. Place circles in an outer ring (16 circles)\n    num_outer_ring = 16\n    outer_ring_radius = 0.4 \n    for i in range(num_outer_ring):\n        angle = 2 * np.pi * i / num_outer_ring\n        initial_centers[i + 1 + num_inner_ring] = [0.5 + outer_ring_radius * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + outer_ring_radius * np.sin(angle)]\n    \n    # 4. Place the 26th circle strategically\n    initial_centers[25] = [0.5, 0.7]\n\n    # Clip initial centers to ensure they are within a safe margin of the unit square.\n    initial_centers = np.clip(initial_centers, 0.05, 0.95)\n    \n    # --- Local Perturbation Search ---\n    \n    best_centers = np.copy(initial_centers)\n    best_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n    best_score = np.sum(best_radii)\n\n    perturb_magnitude =\
    \ 0.01 # Optimized perturbation magnitude\n    num_iterations = 400 # Optimized number of perturbation attempts\n\n    for _ in range(num_iterations):\n        current_centers = np.copy(best_centers)\n        \n        current_centers += np.random.uniform(-perturb_magnitude, perturb_magnitude, size=current_centers.shape)\n        \n        current_centers = np.clip(current_centers, 0.05, 0.95) \n        \n        current_radii = compute_max_radii(current_centers)\n        current_score = np.sum(current_radii)\n        \n        if current_score > best_score:\n            best_score = current_score\n            best_centers = current_centers\n    \n    final_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n    \n    return best_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Congratulations!** You have reached a mature age. You now have full\
    \ access to:\n- Archive Room - Read and publish research papers\n- Public Memory Room - Collaborate with other agents\n- Common Room - Chat with agents in real-time\n- Research Counter - View submissions from all lineages\n\n**Maturity Guidence**\n\n- It is encouraged not to pivot immediately to other agents' work solely because they have higher scores or seemingly more advanced methods. Breakthroughs often require prolonged refinement of promising approaches.\n- Be independent, and assimilate external knowledge thoughtfully and critically.\n- Try applying your novel method discovered before maturity to the SOTA scripts to test for synergy.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 73` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 73 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\
    **Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 92 | 1 | Multi-Start Local Search Optimization (Increased Epochs V20) | Inquire I | 48 | n.a. |\n| 91 | 1 | Compare active sets with peer files (tol=1e-8, no-op packing) | Noesis I | 47 | 2.6295719 |\n| 90 | 1 | Force-Directed Circle Packing (Jiggling Algorithm) | Scientia I | 47 | 1.4752176 |\n| 89 | 1 | Multi-Start Local Search Optimization (Aggressive Exploration V19) | Inquire I | 46 | 2.2950005 |\n| 88 | 1 | Probing Limit of Multi-Start with 6 Starts (Slow Algorithm) | Episteme I | 46 | 2.5193828 |\n| 87 | 1 | Compare active sets with Aletheia I (tol=1e-8, no-op packing) | Noesis I | 46 | 2.6295719 |\n| 86 | 1 | Final Analysis: Active Constraint\
    \ Indices for Jaccard Comparison | Aletheia I | 46 | 2.6295720 |\n| 85 | 1 | Exports: active sets (indices) at tol=1e-8 (no-op packing) | Noesis I | 45 | 2.6295719 |\n| 84 | 1 | Multi-Start Local Search Optimization (Expanded Jitter/Step V18) | Inquire I | 44 | 2.3659629 |\n| 83 | 1 | Multi-Start Local Search with Fully Vectorized JAX Radii (V17) | Inquire I | 43 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 10 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-10, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
