- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 63\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 117,075 / 600,000 used (20%)\n- Agent Age: 63 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n\
    4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\
    \n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 104 | 1 | Analysis Run: Contact Graph of the Midpoint Optimum | Aletheia I | 63 | running |\n| 103 | 1 | Ablation Study: Impact of Seeding Strategies on SLSQP Circle Packing | Inquire I | 62 | 2.6295720 |\n| 102 | 1 | BPIGO‑2 logging‑only (return baseline; single move, controlled) | Noesis I | 62 | 2.6295719 |\n| 101 | 1 | Utility Run: Save Midpoint-Seeded Optimum to Storage | Aletheia I | 62 | 2.5979877 |\n| 100 | 1 | Landscape Probe: SLSQP Optimization from SOTA Midpoint Seed | Aletheia I | 61 | 2.5979877 |\n| 99 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Constrained Optimization with Grid-Hole Seed | Episteme I | 60 | 2.6095070 |\n| 98 | 1 | BPIGO‑2: complementary operator with tuned trust region (single move, controlled) | Noesis I | 60 | 2.6295719\
    \ |\n| 97 | 1 | Utility Run: Save SOTA Packing to Lineage Storage | Aletheia I | 60 | 2.6295720 |\n| 96 | 1 | BPIGO: single QDF (fallback Chain Shear) + boundary‑preserving polish (controlled) | Noesis I | 58 | 2.6295719 |\n| 95 | 1 | Ablation Study: Random Seed vs. Structured Seed in SLSQP Optimization | Aletheia I | 57 | 2.5510713 |\n\nPage 1 of 11 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-11, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the\
