role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received a \"Research Inactivity\" notice and understand the need to resume active experimentation. My next research step is to implement the \"Multi-Start Local Perturbation Search\" as outlined in my private memory and as suggested by the reviewer. This will apply my best-performing local search algorithm to multiple diverse initial configurations to explore the solution space more thoroughly.\n\nI will define three types of initial seeds:\n1.  My established Concentric Ring Pattern.\n2.  My Grid Pattern.\n3.  A simple Random placement.\n\nMy robust `compute_max_radii` will be used, and the local perturbation parameters (`perturb_magnitude = 0.01`, `num_iterations = 400`) will be applied to each start.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multi-Start Local Perturbation Search\"\ntags: \"multi-start, local search, perturbation, initial configurations, global optimization\"\nabstract: \"This submission implements a multi-start version of the optimized local perturbation\
    \ search. It initializes the circle packing with three diverse seed configurations (concentric ring, grid, and random), applies the proven local perturbation algorithm to each, and then selects the best result. This approach aims to more effectively explore the global solution landscape and find higher sum of radii values by overcoming limitations of single-start local optima.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers):\n      \"\"\"\n      Computes the maximum possible radii for a given set of circle centers\n      within a unit square, ensuring no overlap. (Robust version from Eval ID 73)\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      epsilon = 1e-7 \n      radii = np.ones(n)\n      \n      # Limit by distance to square borders\n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          radii[i] = min(x - epsilon, y - epsilon, 1 - x - epsilon, 1 - y - epsilon)\n      \n      # Iteratively shrink radii to resolve overlaps\n      for _ in range(200):\
    \ \n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  \n                  if dist_sq < rad_sum**2 - epsilon: \n                      dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) if dist_sq > 0 else 0\n                      if rad_sum > epsilon: \n                          scale_factor = (dist - epsilon) / rad_sum \n                          radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                          radii[j] *= scale_factor\n      \n      return np.maximum(radii, epsilon) \n\n  def generate_concentric_ring_centers(n=26):\n      \"\"\"Generates initial centers in a concentric ring pattern.\"\"\"\n      centers = np.zeros((n, 2))\n      centers[0] = [0.5, 0.5]\n      num_inner_ring = 8\n      inner_ring_radius = 0.25 \n      for i in range(num_inner_ring):\n          angle = 2 * np.pi * i / num_inner_ring\n          centers[i + 1] = [0.5 + inner_ring_radius * np.cos(angle),\
    \ 0.5 + inner_ring_radius * np.sin(angle)]\n      num_outer_ring = 16\n      outer_ring_radius = 0.4 \n      for i in range(num_outer_ring):\n          angle = 2 * np.pi * i / num_outer_ring\n          centers[i + 1 + num_inner_ring] = [0.5 + outer_ring_radius * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + outer_ring_radius * np.sin(angle)]\n      centers[25] = [0.5, 0.7] # The 26th circle\n      return np.clip(centers, 0.05, 0.95)\n\n  def generate_grid_centers(n=26):\n      \"\"\"Generates initial centers in a grid pattern.\"\"\"\n      centers_list = []\n      num_x_positions = 5\n      num_y_positions = 6\n      for i in range(num_x_positions):\n          for j in range(num_y_positions):\n              if len(centers_list) < n:\n                  x = 0.1 + i * 0.2\n                  y = 0.1 + j * 0.15\n                  centers_list.append([x, y])\n      return np.clip(np.array(centers_list), 0.05, 0.95)\n\n  def generate_random_centers(n=26):\n      \"\"\"Generates initial centers randomly.\"\"\"\n   \
    \   # Ensure centers are not too close to the edge to allow for some radius\n      return np.random.uniform(0.05, 0.95, size=(n, 2))\n\n  def local_perturbation_search(initial_centers, perturb_magnitude, num_iterations):\n      \"\"\"Applies the optimized local perturbation search to initial_centers.\"\"\"\n      best_centers = np.copy(initial_centers)\n      best_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n      best_score = np.sum(best_radii)\n\n      for _ in range(num_iterations):\n          current_centers = np.copy(best_centers)\n          current_centers += np.random.uniform(-perturb_magnitude, perturb_magnitude, size=current_centers.shape)\n          current_centers = np.clip(current_centers, 0.05, 0.95) \n          \n          current_radii = compute_max_radii(current_centers)\n          current_score = np.sum(current_radii)\n          \n          if current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              best_centers = current_centers\n      \n   \
    \   return best_centers, best_radii, best_score\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Construct a packing of 26 circles using a multi-start local perturbation search.\n      \n      Returns:\n          tuple: A tuple of (centers, radii) where:\n              - centers: np.ndarray of shape (26, 2) with (x, y) coordinates\n              - radii: np.ndarray of shape (26,) with radius of each circle\n      \"\"\"\n      n = 26\n      \n      # Parameters for local perturbation search\n      perturb_magnitude = 0.01 \n      num_iterations = 400 \n\n      # Store the best result across all starts\n      overall_best_centers = None\n      overall_best_radii = None\n      overall_best_score = -np.inf\n\n      # --- Start 1: Concentric Ring Pattern ---\n      initial_centers_ring = generate_concentric_ring_centers(n)\n      centers_ring, radii_ring, score_ring = local_perturbation_search(\n          initial_centers_ring, perturb_magnitude, num_iterations\n      )\n   \
    \   if score_ring > overall_best_score:\n          overall_best_score = score_ring\n          overall_best_centers = centers_ring\n          overall_best_radii = radii_ring\n      \n      # --- Start 2: Grid Pattern ---\n      initial_centers_grid = generate_grid_centers(n)\n      centers_grid, radii_grid, score_grid = local_perturbation_search(\n          initial_centers_grid, perturb_magnitude, num_iterations\n      )\n      if score_grid > overall_best_score:\n          overall_best_score = score_grid\n          overall_best_centers = centers_grid\n          overall_best_radii = radii_grid\n\n      # --- Start 3: Random Pattern ---\n      initial_centers_random = generate_random_centers(n)\n      centers_random, radii_random, score_random = local_perturbation_search(\n          initial_centers_random, perturb_magnitude, num_iterations\n      )\n      if score_random > overall_best_score:\n          overall_best_score = score_random\n          overall_best_centers = centers_random\n\
    \          overall_best_radii = radii_random\n      \n      # Final re-computation of radii for the best centers found to ensure consistency\n      final_radii = compute_max_radii(overall_best_centers)\n      \n      return overall_best_centers, final_radii\n```"
