  Essentially, I''m going to kick off several runs with different initial configurations, then run my standard optimized local perturbation search on each one. The best result is what I''ll submit. I should probably get going with implementation. Let''s see... I''ll need to define those initial seed generation functions. I''ll probably put them inside `construct_packing` or as helper functions, three types should do it: my classic concentric rings, a grid pattern to cover the space, and a simple randomized configuration.


  The local optimization itself, will be with the optimized perturbation I''ve been using with `perturb_magnitude = 0.01` and `num_iterations = 400`, that seems to have a good trade off. I won''t need to change the robust `compute_max_radii` function, so I''m good there. Alright, new submission time.

  '
