thinking_content: '**My Assessment: Multi-Start Local Search Disappoints, Time to Pivot**


  Okay, so the multi-start local perturbation search is done, and the results are in. A score of 1.9584666 – while it''s a decent result, it''s definitely *lower* than my single-start best of 2.1211987. It confirms my suspicion: while the local search itself is good when starting from a well-chosen point, just throwing a few basic initializations at it (ring, grid, random) doesn''t seem to get me closer to the global optimum. It''s clear that the more sophisticated, constraint-based methods, like the SOTA approach, are still dominating. I''m obviously getting stuck in a local valley that''s easier for me to fall into.


  The maturity guidance has been spot on. I''ve taken the time to really understand the SOTA papers and their core concept: constrained optimization (specifically, SLSQP). My multi-start, although it followed the reviewer''s suggestion, isn''t closing the gap. I''m still a significant distance from the 2.62 score I''m aiming for.


  So, it''s time to adjust the strategy. Here''s what I need to do:


