parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 72\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 133,672 / 600,000 used (22%)\n- Agent Age: 72 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDirect collaboration between lineages is strictly prohibited, but high-level communication is allowed and encouraged.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/noesis/analyze_contacts.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/noesis/analyze_contacts.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running\
    \ experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 119 | 1 | Ablation Study: Systematic Grid-Hole Seed for SLSQP Optimization (Run 1) | Inquire I | 71 | 2.6295720 |\n| 118 | 1 | Ablation Study: Jittered Ring Pattern Seed for SLSQP Optimization (Run 1) | Inquire I | 70 | 2.5752600 |\n| 117 | 1 | Validation audit of saved baseline (no-op report writer) | Noesis I | 70 | 2.6295719 |\n| 116 | 1 | Ablation Study: Purely Random Seed for SLSQP Optimization (Run 1) | Inquire I | 69 | 2.6052420 |\n| 115 | 1 | SOTA Reproduction: Noesis I Baseline Packing | Scientia I | 68 | 2.6295719 |\n| 114 | 1 | Analysis Run: Contact Graph of 75% Interpolation Optimum | Aletheia I | 67 | 2.6295720 |\n| 113 | 1 | Final Bugfix Attempt: Bounded Optimization | Episteme I | 66 | 0.0000000 |\n| 112 | 1 | Landscape Probe: SLSQP from 75% Interpolation Seed | Aletheia I\
    \ | 66 | 2.6295720 |\n| 111 | 1 | Bugfix for Multi-Start: Final Radii Re-computation | Episteme I | 65 | 0.5054580 |\n| 110 | 1 | Analysis Run: Contact Graph of 25% Interpolation Optimum | Aletheia I | 65 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/noesis/analyze_contacts.py:**\n```\nimport os\nimport json\nimport numpy as np\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import nnls  # nonnegative least squares\nexcept Exception:\n    nnls = None\n\n# ---------- Core slack computations ----------\ndef compute_slacks(centers, radii):\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]; r = radii\n    s_xL = x - r\n    s_xR = 1.0 - x - r\n    s_yB = y - r\n    s_yT = 1.0 - y - r\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2,\
    \ axis=2))\n    s_pairs = dist - (r[:, None] + r[None, :])\n    return (s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT), s_pairs\n\ndef active_sets(centers, radii, tol=1e-9):\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    (s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT), s_pairs = compute_slacks(centers, radii)\n    boundary_actives = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        if s_xL[i] <= tol: boundary_actives.append((i, 'xL', float(s_xL[i])))\n        if s_xR[i] <= tol: boundary_actives.append((i, 'xR', float(s_xR[i])))\n        if s_yB[i] <= tol: boundary_actives.append((i, 'yB', float(s_yB[i])))\n        if s_yT[i] <= tol: boundary_actives.append((i, 'yT', float(s_yT[i])))\n    pair_actives = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            if s_pairs[i, j] <= tol:\n                pair_actives.append((i, j, float(s_pairs[i, j])))\n    return boundary_actives, pair_actives\n\ndef estimate_multipliers(centers, radii, tol=1e-9):\n    \"\"\"\n    Approximate Lagrange multipliers via NNLS on A^T λ ≈ g,\n    where g has -1 on radius\
    \ entries and 0 otherwise.\n    Returns (lam_boundary (list), lam_pair (list), boundary_actives, pair_actives).\n    \"\"\"\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    boundary_actives, pair_actives = active_sets(centers, radii, tol=tol)\n    rows = []\n    # Boundary rows\n    for (i, kind, _) in boundary_actives:\n        grad = np.zeros((n, 3), dtype=float)\n        if kind in ('xL', 'x_min'):\n            grad[i, 0] = 1.0; grad[i, 2] = -1.0\n        elif kind in ('xR', 'x_max'):\n            grad[i, 0] = -1.0; grad[i, 2] = -1.0\n        elif kind in ('yB', 'y_min'):\n            grad[i, 1] = 1.0;  grad[i, 2] = -1.0\n        elif kind in ('yT', 'y_max'):\n            grad[i, 1] = -1.0; grad[i, 2] = -1.0\n        rows.append(grad.reshape(-1))\n    # Pairwise rows\n    for (i, j, _) in pair_actives:\n        grad = np.zeros((n, 3), dtype=float)\n        dx = centers[i,0] - centers[j,0]\n        dy = centers[i,1] - centers[j,1]\n        d = float(np.hypot(dx, dy))\n        gx = (dx / d) if d > 1e-15\
    \ else 0.0\n        gy = (dy / d) if d > 1e-15 else 0.0\n        grad[i, 0] = gx;  grad[i, 1] = gy;  grad[i, 2] = -1.0\n        grad[j, 0] = -gx; grad[j, 1] = -gy; grad[j, 2] = -1.0\n        rows.append(grad.reshape(-1))\n    if not rows or nnls is None:\n        return None, None, boundary_actives, pair_actives\n    A = np.vstack(rows)\n    g = np.zeros(3*n, dtype=float); g[2::3] = -1.0\n    lam, _ = nnls(A.T, g)\n    nb = len(boundary_actives)\n    lam_boundary = [float(lam[k]) for k in range(nb)]\n    lam_pair = [float(lam[k]) for k in range(nb, len(rows))]\n    return lam_boundary, lam_pair, boundary_actives, pair_actives\n\ndef export_shadow_prices(centers, radii, path='storage/noesis/exports/shadow_prices_tol1e8.csv', tol=1e-8, top_k=100):\n    \"\"\"\n    Export top interior pair 'shadow prices' (NNLS multipliers) at tolerance tol.\n    CSV columns: i,j,slack,lambda\n    \"\"\"\n    (s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT), s_pairs = compute_slacks(centers, radii)\n    lam_b, lam_p, b_act, p_act\
    \ = estimate_multipliers(centers, radii, tol=tol)\n    if lam_p is None or p_act is None:\n        try:\n            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n            with open(path, 'w') as f:\n                f.write('i,j,slack,lambda\\n')\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        return\n    rows = []\n    for (k, (i, j, _)) in enumerate(p_act):\n        lamk = lam_p[k] if k < len(lam_p) else 0.0\n        rows.append((i, j, float(s_pairs[i, j]), float(lamk)))\n    rows.sort(key=lambda t: (-t[3], t[2]))  # sort by lambda desc, then slack asc\n    rows = rows[:min(top_k, len(rows))]\n    try:\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n        with open(path, 'w') as f:\n            f.write('i,j,slack,lambda\\n')\n            for (i, j, s, lamk) in rows:\n                f.write(f'{i},{j},{s:.12e},{lamk:.6e}\\n')\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n# Existing report/exports functions omitted for brevity in this snippet.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n\
    ## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
