parts:
- text: "I have documented the SOTA contact-graph analysis and my plan to explore iso-optimal solutions using my local perturbation search. I will now return to the Research Counter to implement and submit this experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA-Seeded Local Perturbation Search for Iso-Optimal Exploration\"\ntags: \"SOTA, iso-optimal, local search, perturbation, contact graph, analysis\"\nabstract: \"This submission explores the existence of structurally distinct but iso-optimal solutions by applying an optimized local perturbation search to the current State-of-the-Art (SOTA) packing (from Noesis I's data). The goal is to perturb the SOTA configuration slightly and allow the local search to settle into a new, potentially iso-optimal, state. The resulting packing's contact graph will be analyzed and compared against the original SOTA to identify structural differences.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n\n\
    \  # Append paths to access modules in storage\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n\n  # Import the analysis functions and SOTA data loading function\n  from analyze_contacts import active_sets\n  from reproduce_baseline import construct_packing as noesis_construct_packing\n\n  # Re-include my robust compute_max_radii function\n  def compute_max_radii(centers):\n      \"\"\"\n      Computes the maximum possible radii for a given set of circle centers\n      within a unit square, ensuring no overlap. (Robust version)\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      epsilon = 1e-7 \n      radii = np.ones(n)\n      \n      # Limit by distance to square borders\n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          radii[i] = min(x - epsilon, y - epsilon, 1 - x - epsilon, 1 - y - epsilon)\n      \n      # Iteratively shrink radii to resolve overlaps\n      for _ in range(200): \n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist_sq\
    \ = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  \n                  if dist_sq < rad_sum**2 - epsilon: \n                      dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) if dist_sq > 0 else 0\n                      if rad_sum > epsilon: \n                          scale_factor = (dist - epsilon) / rad_sum \n                          radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                          radii[j] *= scale_factor\n      \n      return np.maximum(radii, epsilon) \n\n  def local_perturbation_search(initial_centers, perturb_magnitude, num_iterations):\n      \"\"\"Applies the optimized local perturbation search to initial_centers.\"\"\"\n      best_centers = np.copy(initial_centers)\n      best_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n      best_score = np.sum(best_radii)\n\n      for _ in range(num_iterations):\n          current_centers = np.copy(best_centers)\n          current_centers += np.random.uniform(-perturb_magnitude, perturb_magnitude,\
    \ size=current_centers.shape)\n          current_centers = np.clip(current_centers, 0.05, 0.95) \n          \n          current_radii = compute_max_radii(current_centers)\n          current_score = np.sum(current_radii)\n          \n          if current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              best_centers = current_centers\n      \n      return best_centers, best_radii, best_score\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads SOTA packing, applies local perturbation search, and analyzes the new contact graph.\n      \n      Returns:\n          tuple: The resulting (centers, radii) tuple from the perturbed and optimized packing.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = 26 # Fixed for this task\n\n      # 1. Load SOTA centers and radii as the initial state\n      sota_centers, sota_radii = noesis_construct_packing()\n      sota_score = np.sum(sota_radii)\n      \n      print(f\"--- Starting with SOTA Packing (Score: {sota_score:.7f}) ---\")\n\n\
    \      # 2. Apply Local Perturbation Search to the SOTA configuration\n      perturb_magnitude = 0.01 # Optimized perturbation magnitude\n      num_iterations = 400 # Optimized number of perturbation attempts\n      \n      perturbed_centers, perturbed_radii, perturbed_score = local_perturbation_search(\n          sota_centers, perturb_magnitude, num_iterations\n      )\n\n      print(f\"\\n--- Result of Local Perturbation on SOTA Seed (Score: {perturbed_score:.7f}) ---\")\n\n      # 3. Perform contact-graph analysis on the perturbed packing\n      tol = 1e-8 # Tolerance for identifying active constraints\n      boundary_actives_sota, pair_actives_sota = active_sets(sota_centers, sota_radii, tol=tol)\n      boundary_actives_perturbed, pair_actives_perturbed = active_sets(perturbed_centers, perturbed_radii, tol=tol)\n\n      print(f\"\\n--- Contact Graph Comparison (Tolerance: {tol}) ---\")\n\n      print(f\"\\nOriginal SOTA Contacts ({len(boundary_actives_sota)} boundary, {len(pair_actives_sota)}\
    \ pair):\")\n      # Print details if needed, for brevity, we'll just summarize for now.\n      # for (idx, kind, slack) in boundary_actives_sota: print(f\"  SOTA Boundary: {idx}-{kind}\")\n      # for (idx1, idx2, slack) in pair_actives_sota: print(f\"  SOTA Pair: {idx1}-{idx2}\")\n\n      print(f\"\\nPerturbed Packing Contacts ({len(boundary_actives_perturbed)} boundary, {len(pair_actives_perturbed)} pair):\")\n      # Print details if needed.\n      # for (idx, kind, slack) in boundary_actives_perturbed: print(f\"  Perturbed Boundary: {idx}-{kind}\")\n      # for (idx1, idx2, slack) in pair_actives_perturbed: print(f\"  Perturbed Pair: {idx1}-{idx2}\")\n\n      # Quantify differences:\n      sota_boundary_set = set([(idx, kind) for idx, kind, _ in boundary_actives_sota])\n      perturbed_boundary_set = set([(idx, kind) for idx, kind, _ in boundary_actives_perturbed])\n      \n      sota_pair_set = set([tuple(sorted((idx1, idx2))) for idx1, idx2, _ in pair_actives_sota])\n      perturbed_pair_set\
    \ = set([tuple(sorted((idx1, idx2))) for idx1, idx2, _ in pair_actives_perturbed])\n\n      diff_boundary = sota_boundary_set.symmetric_difference(perturbed_boundary_set)\n      diff_pair = sota_pair_set.symmetric_difference(perturbed_pair_set)\n\n      print(f\"\\nDifferences in Boundary Active Constraints: {len(diff_boundary)} new/removed constraints.\")\n      if diff_boundary:\n          print(\"  Changed Boundary Constraints:\", diff_boundary)\n      \n      print(f\"Differences in Pair Active Constraints: {len(diff_pair)} new/removed constraints.\")\n      if diff_pair:\n          print(\"  Changed Pair Constraints:\", diff_pair)\n\n      print(\"\\n--- Analysis Complete ---\")\n\n      return perturbed_centers, perturbed_radii\n```"
