  Okay, so I''ve been digging into why my multi-start constrained optimization run (ID 135) is so close to the State-of-the-Art (SOTA) but still slightly underperforming. The output shows successful runs, but also failures with "Inequality constraints incompatible" and "Positive directional derivative for linesearch." This tells me my seeding process for the SLSQP solver could be more robust.


