role: model
parts:
- text: "I have updated my private memory with the analysis of the sub-optimal score from my multi-start constrained optimization and the refined strategy for a more robust `_generate_grid_plus_hole_seed` function.\n\nI will now return to the Research Counter to implement the improved seeding and resubmit the Multi-Start Constrained Optimization.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multi-Start Constrained Optimization (SLSQP) with Robust Grid-Hole Seeds\"\ntags: \"constrained optimization, SLSQP, multi-start, SOTA, grid-hole seed, robust initialization\"\nabstract: \"This submission refines the multi-start constrained optimization approach for 26-circle packing by implementing a more robust 'grid-plus-hole' seeding strategy. Initial radii for the 'hole' circle are now dynamically calculated based on its closest grid neighbors to ensure initial feasibility, addressing previous 'incompatible constraints' failures. This aims to consistently achieve\
    \ the SOTA score by providing well-conditioned starting points for the SLSQP solver across diverse initial configurations.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  # --- Constants and Configuration ---\n  N_CIRCLES = 26\n  R_MIN_BOUND = 1e-6\n  R_MAX_BOUND = 0.5\n  MARGIN_TOL = 1e-9 # For final radii safety factor\n\n  # --- Helper Functions for Decision Vector (z) Conversion ---\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      \"\"\"Converts flattened decision vector z to (centers, radii).\"\"\"\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]  # x coordinates\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]  # y coordinates\n      radii = z[2::3]  # radii\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n      \"\"\"Converts (centers, radii) to flattened decision vector z.\"\"\"\n      z = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES * 3)\n      z[0::3] = centers[:, 0] # X\n      z[1::3] = centers[:, 1] # Y\n      z[2::3] = radii # R\n      return z\n\n  # --- Initial Seeding\
    \ Strategy: Grid-Plus-Hole (IMPROVED) ---\n  def _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed(hole_pos_idx, n_circles=N_CIRCLES, base_r=0.1 - 1e-8, initial_eps=1e-8):\n      \"\"\"\n      Generates a 5x5 grid (25 circles) + 1 'hole' circle.\n      The 'hole' circle's initial radius is dynamically calculated for feasibility.\n      \"\"\"\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9] # For 5x5 grid\n      grid_centers_list = []\n      for x_coord in coords:\n          for y_coord in coords:\n              grid_centers_list.append(np.array([x_coord, y_coord]))\n      grid_centers = np.array(grid_centers_list) # 25 centers\n\n      # Select the grid cell for the 'hole' circle\n      row_idx = hole_pos_idx // 5\n      col_idx = hole_pos_idx % 5\n      \n      # Calculate coordinates of the center of this grid cell (midpoint)\n      hole_mid_x = 0.2 + row_idx * 0.2\n      hole_mid_y = 0.2 + col_idx * 0.2\n      hole_circle_center = np.array([hole_mid_x, hole_mid_y])\n\n      # Combine the 25 grid centers with\
    \ the 26th hole circle center\n      final_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_circle_center]) # 26 centers\n\n      # Initialize radii: base_r for grid circles, dynamically for hole circle\n      radii = np.full(n_circles, base_r, dtype=float)\n\n      # Dynamically calculate the radius for the hole circle (the 26th one)\n      # Its closest neighbors are the 4 grid circles forming the corners of the cell it's in.\n      # The corner circles are (coords[row_idx], coords[col_idx]), (coords[row_idx+1], coords[col_idx]), etc.\n      # For a cell from (x,y) to (x+0.2, y+0.2), the midpoint is (x+0.1, y+0.1).\n      # The 4 corner circles are (x,y), (x+0.2,y), (x,y+0.2), (x+0.2,y+0.2)\n      \n      # Let's find the distances from hole_circle_center to its 4 corner grid neighbors\n      # The four corners of the specific grid cell for this hole:\n      corner1 = np.array([coords[row_idx], coords[col_idx]])\n      corner2 = np.array([coords[row_idx], coords[col_idx+1]]) if col_idx < 4\
    \ else np.array([coords[row_idx], coords[col_idx]]) # Adjust for edge cases\n      corner3 = np.array([coords[row_idx+1], coords[col_idx]]) if row_idx < 4 else np.array([coords[row_idx], coords[col_idx]]) # Adjust for edge cases\n      corner4 = np.array([coords[row_idx+1], coords[col_idx+1]]) if row_idx < 4 and col_idx < 4 else np.array([coords[row_idx], coords[col_idx]]) # Adjust for edge cases\n\n      # To be more robust, find min distance to any of the 25 grid centers.\n      # Then radius of hole is that min_dist - base_r - epsilon.\n      \n      # Calculate distances from hole_circle_center to all 25 grid centers\n      distances_to_grid = np.linalg.norm(grid_centers - hole_circle_center, axis=1)\n      min_dist_to_grid_circle = np.min(distances_to_grid)\n\n      # Set hole radius to be nearly touching its closest grid neighbor\n      radii[n_circles - 1] = max(R_MIN_BOUND, min_dist_to_grid_circle - base_r - initial_eps)\n      \n      # Ensure final centers are clipped (redundant\
    \ with bounds but good for safety)\n      final_centers = np.clip(final_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n      return final_centers, radii\n\n  # --- Objective Function and Jacobian (from previous submission) ---\n  def objective_fun(z):\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      return -np.sum(radii)\n\n  def jac_objective_fun(z):\n      jac = np.zeros_like(z)\n      jac[2::3] = -1.0 \n      return jac\n\n  # --- Constraint Functions and Jacobians (from previous submission) ---\n  def boundary_constraints_fun(z):\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      \n      g = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES * 4)\n      g[0::4] = centers[:, 0] - radii           \n      g[1::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 0] - radii     \n      g[2::4] = centers[:, 1] - radii           \n      g[3::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 1] - radii     \n      return g\n\n  def jac_boundary_constraints_fun(z):\n      jac = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES * 4, N_CIRCLES\
    \ * 3))\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 0] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 0] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 1] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 1] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n      return jac\n\n  def overlap_constraints_fun(z):\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n      radii = z[2::3]\n\n      g = []\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              g.append(dist - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n      return np.array(g)\n\n  def jac_overlap_constraints_fun(z):\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      \n      num_pair_constraints = N_CIRCLES * (N_CIRCLES - 1) // 2\n      jac = np.zeros((num_pair_constraints,\
    \ N_CIRCLES * 3))\n      \n      k = 0 \n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n              delta_c = centers[i] - centers[j]\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(delta_c)\n              \n              if dist < 1e-15: \n                  gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n              else:\n                  unit_vec = delta_c / dist\n                  gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n              \n              jac[k, i*3 + 0] = gx; jac[k, i*3 + 1] = gy; jac[k, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              jac[k, j*3 + 0] = -gx; jac[k, j*3 + 1] = -gy; jac[k, j*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              k += 1\n      return jac\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Construct a packing of 26 circles in the unit square using Multi-Start SLSQP\n      with systematically varied, robustly initialized Grid-Hole Seeds.\n      \n      Returns:\n          tuple: A tuple of (centers, radii) where:\n              - centers: np.ndarray of shape (26, 2) with (x, y) coordinates\n\
    \              - radii: np.ndarray of shape (26,) with radius of each circle\n      \"\"\"\n      best_overall_z = None\n      best_overall_score = -np.inf\n\n      # 25 possible \"hole\" positions in a 5x5 grid for multi-start\n      num_seed_starts = 25 \n\n      for seed_idx in range(num_seed_starts):\n          print(f\"Running optimization for seed_idx: {seed_idx+1}/{num_seed_starts}\")\n          # 1. Initial Seed (Grid-Plus-Hole) - now with robust radius calculation\n          initial_centers, initial_radii = _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed(seed_idx)\n          initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n          # 2. Bounds for Decision Variables\n          bounds = []\n          for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n              bounds.append((0.0, 1.0)) # x_i\n              bounds.append((0.0, 1.0)) # y_i\n              bounds.append((R_MIN_BOUND, R_MAX_BOUND)) # r_i (r >= 1e-6, r <= 0.5)\n\n          # 3. Constraints\n          constraints = [\n              {'type': 'ineq',\
    \ 'fun': boundary_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_boundary_constraints_fun},\n              {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_overlap_constraints_fun}\n          ]\n\n          # 4. Optimization Call\n          result = minimize(\n              fun=objective_fun,\n              x0=initial_z,\n              jac=jac_objective_fun,\n              bounds=bounds,\n              constraints=constraints,\n              method='SLSQP',\n              options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9} \n          )\n          \n          current_score = -result.fun\n          print(f\"  Seed {seed_idx+1} Score: {current_score:.7f}, Status: {result.message}\")\n\n          # 5. Track Best Result\n          if result.success and current_score > best_overall_score:\n              best_overall_score = current_score\n              best_overall_z = result.x\n              print(f\"  New best score found: {best_overall_score:.7f}\")\n\n      # 6. Post-process the overall best result\n   \
    \   if best_overall_z is None:\n          # Fallback if no successful optimization occurred (shouldn't happen with robust seeds)\n          print(\"Warning: No successful optimization found, returning default seed.\")\n          # Use a robust default seed if all failed\n          initial_centers_fallback, initial_radii_fallback = _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed(0)\n          best_overall_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers_fallback, initial_radii_fallback)\n          best_overall_score = -np.inf # Ensure fallback is still evaluated for score\n\n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(best_overall_z)\n\n      # Apply a final safety factor, as mentioned by Inquire I.\n      final_radii *= (1.0 - MARGIN_TOL)\n      \n      # Ensure final centers are within bounds too, just in case\n      final_centers = np.clip(final_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n      print(f\"\\nMulti-Start Optimization Complete. Best Final Score: {best_overall_score:.7f}\")\n      \n      return final_centers,\
    \ final_radii\n```"
