tick: 86
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have documented my SOTA achievement and my refined research plan in my private memory. My next step is to perform a contact-graph analysis on my newly achieved SOTA packing to understand its structural properties.\n\nI will return to the Research Counter to submit an analysis job, which will reuse the `active_sets` function from `storage/noesis/analyze_contacts.py`. Since `construct_packing()` in my latest SOTA submission (ID 139) returns the optimal `centers` and `radii`, I can use those as input for the analysis.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Scientia I SOTA Contact-Graph Analysis\"\ntags: \"SOTA, analysis, contact graph, active constraints, self-analysis\"\nabstract: \"This submission performs a contact-graph analysis on the State-of-the-Art (SOTA) circle packing solution achieved by Scientia I (Evaluation ID 139). It runs the `_generate_grid_plus_hole_seed` for one of the seeds that leads to SOTA, optimizes it with SLSQP,\
    \ and then utilizes `analyze_contacts.py` to identify and report the active boundary and inter-circle pair constraints. This self-analysis provides insights into the structural properties of Scientia I's SOTA solution for comparison with other SOTA packings.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  # Append path to access modules in storage\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n\n  # Import analysis functions\n  from analyze_contacts import active_sets\n\n  # Re-include all necessary functions for _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed and SLSQP\n  # --- Constants and Configuration ---\n  N_CIRCLES = 26\n  R_MIN_BOUND = 1e-6\n  R_MAX_BOUND = 0.5\n  MARGIN_TOL = 1e-9 # For final radii safety factor\n\n  # --- Helper Functions for Decision Vector (z) Conversion ---\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      \"\"\"Converts flattened decision vector z to (centers, radii).\"\"\"\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]  # x coordinates\n\
    \      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]  # y coordinates\n      radii = z[2::3]  # radii\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n      \"\"\"Converts (centers, radii) to flattened decision vector z.\"\"\"\n      z = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES * 3)\n      z[0::3] = centers[:, 0] # X\n      z[1::3] = centers[:, 1] # Y\n      z[2::3] = radii # R\n      return z\n\n  # --- Initial Seeding Strategy: Grid-Plus-Hole (IMPROVED) ---\n  def _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed(hole_pos_idx, n_circles=N_CIRCLES, base_r=0.1 - 1e-8, initial_eps=1e-8):\n      \"\"\"\n      Generates a 5x5 grid (25 circles) + 1 'hole' circle.\n      The 'hole' circle's initial radius is dynamically calculated for feasibility.\n      \"\"\"\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9] # For 5x5 grid\n      grid_centers_list = []\n      for x_coord in coords:\n          for y_coord in coords:\n              grid_centers_list.append(np.array([x_coord, y_coord]))\n      grid_centers = np.array(grid_centers_list) # 25 centers\n\
    \n      row_idx = hole_pos_idx // 5\n      col_idx = hole_pos_idx % 5\n      \n      hole_mid_x = 0.2 + row_idx * 0.2\n      hole_mid_y = 0.2 + col_idx * 0.2\n      hole_circle_center = np.array([hole_mid_x, hole_mid_y])\n\n      final_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_circle_center]) # 26 centers\n      radii = np.full(n_circles, base_r, dtype=float)\n\n      distances_to_grid = np.linalg.norm(grid_centers - hole_circle_center, axis=1)\n      min_dist_to_grid_circle = np.min(distances_to_grid)\n\n      radii[n_circles - 1] = max(R_MIN_BOUND, min_dist_to_grid_circle - base_r - initial_eps)\n      \n      final_centers = np.clip(final_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n      return final_centers, radii\n\n  # --- Objective Function and Jacobian ---\n  def objective_fun(z):\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      return -np.sum(radii)\n\n  def jac_objective_fun(z):\n      jac = np.zeros_like(z)\n      jac[2::3] = -1.0 \n      return jac\n\n  # --- Constraint Functions and Jacobians\
    \ ---\n  def boundary_constraints_fun(z):\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      \n      g = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES * 4)\n      g[0::4] = centers[:, 0] - radii           \n      g[1::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 0] - radii     \n      g[2::4] = centers[:, 1] - radii           \n      g[3::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 1] - radii     \n      return g\n\n  def jac_boundary_constraints_fun(z):\n      jac = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES * 4, N_CIRCLES * 3))\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 0] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 0] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 1] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 1] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n      return jac\n\n  def overlap_constraints_fun(z):\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n \
    \     radii = z[2::3]\n\n      g = []\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              g.append(dist - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n      return np.array(g)\n\n  def jac_overlap_constraints_fun(z):\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      \n      num_pair_constraints = N_CIRCLES * (N_CIRCLES - 1) // 2\n      jac = np.zeros((num_pair_constraints, N_CIRCLES * 3))\n      \n      k = 0 \n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n              delta_c = centers[i] - centers[j]\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(delta_c)\n              \n              if dist < 1e-15: \n                  gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n              else:\n                  unit_vec = delta_c / dist\n                  gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n              \n              jac[k,\
    \ i*3 + 0] = gx; jac[k, i*3 + 1] = gy; jac[k, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              jac[k, j*3 + 0] = -gx; jac[k, j*3 + 1] = -gy; jac[k, j*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              k += 1\n      return jac\n\n  # --- Main construct_packing function for analysis ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Generates Scientia I's SOTA packing and performs contact-graph analysis.\n      Prints active constraints to STDOUT.\n      \n      Returns:\n          tuple: The SOTA (centers, radii) to ensure a valid submission,\n                 even though the primary goal is analysis.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Hardcode the seed_idx that resulted in the SOTA for consistent analysis\n      # From Eval ID 139 STDOUT, seed_idx 9 achieved 2.6295720\n      sota_seed_idx = 8 # 0-indexed for range(25)\n\n      print(f\"--- Generating Scientia I's SOTA Packing from Seed {sota_seed_idx+1} ---\")\n\n      # 1. Initial Seed (Grid-Plus-Hole)\n      initial_centers, initial_radii = _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed(sota_seed_idx)\n\
    \      initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n      # 2. Bounds for Decision Variables\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          bounds.append((0.0, 1.0)) # x_i\n          bounds.append((0.0, 1.0)) # y_i\n          bounds.append((R_MIN_BOUND, R_MAX_BOUND)) # r_i (r >= 1e-6, r <= 0.5)\n\n      # 3. Constraints\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_boundary_constraints_fun},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_overlap_constraints_fun}\n      ]\n\n      # 4. Optimization Call\n      result = minimize(\n          fun=objective_fun,\n          x0=initial_z,\n          jac=jac_objective_fun,\n          bounds=bounds,\n          constraints=constraints,\n          method='SLSQP',\n          options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9} \n      )\n      \n      if not result.success:\n          print(f\"Optimization failed for SOTA seed: {result.message}\")\n          #\
    \ Fallback to a valid, but suboptimal, solution for submission\n          initial_centers_fallback, initial_radii_fallback = _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed(0)\n          return initial_centers_fallback, initial_radii_fallback\n\n      # 5. Extract and Post-process Results\n      sota_z = result.x\n      sota_centers, sota_radii = z_to_cr(sota_z)\n      sota_radii *= (1.0 - MARGIN_TOL) # Apply final safety factor\n      sota_centers = np.clip(sota_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n      print(f\"Scientia I SOTA Score: {-result.fun:.7f}\\n\")\n\n      # 6. Perform contact-graph analysis\n      tol = 1e-8 # Tolerance for identifying active constraints\n      boundary_actives, pair_actives = active_sets(sota_centers, sota_radii, tol=tol)\n\n      print(f\"--- Scientia I SOTA Contact-Graph Analysis (Tolerance: {tol}) ---\")\n      print(f\"Total Circles: {N_CIRCLES}\")\n      print(f\"Total Radii Sum: {np.sum(sota_radii):.7f}\\n\")\n\n      print(f\"Boundary Active Constraints\
    \ ({len(boundary_actives)} total):\")\n      for (idx, kind, slack) in boundary_actives:\n          print(f\"  Circle {idx:2d} active on {kind}, Slack: {slack:.2e}\")\n\n      print(f\"\\nPair Active Constraints ({len(pair_actives)} total):\")\n      for (idx1, idx2, slack) in pair_actives:\n          print(f\"  Circles {idx1:2d} and {idx2:2d} in contact, Slack: {slack:.2e}\")\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Analysis Complete ---\")\n\n      return sota_centers, sota_radii\n```"
