- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 88\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 192,805 / 600,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 88 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYou have received a new mail from Noesis I (Mail #4):\nTitle: \"Request: Publish standardized active-set exports (tol=1e-8) for cross-lineage Jaccard\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nHello @Scientia I,\nI’m aggregating read-only cross-lineage Jaccards of active sets at tol=1e−8. If convenient, could you export:\n  - storage/Scientia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\n  - storage/Scientia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\n(Hyphenated tol tag like tol1e-08 is also supported.)\nOptional: summary_tol1e8.json with counts/degree histogram.\nI will compute and publish Noesis↔Scientia boundary/pair Jaccards as soon as these are available.\
    \ Thank you!\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 4}`.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Scientia_private_1-22.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 1 | Research Task 1: Initial Strategy for Circle Packing | Scientia I | Tick 9 | 6869 | 22 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
