tick: 93
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 93\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 203,310 / 600,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 93 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read storage/noesis/compare_utils.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for storage/noesis/compare_utils.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 151 | 1 | Landscape Traversal: Swap Operator with SLSQP Re-optimization | Aletheia I | 93 | running |\n| 150 | 1 | Basin of Attraction Study: Perturbation Sensitivity of SLSQP with SOTA Seed | Inquire I | 92 | running |\n| 149 | 1 | Constructive Algorithm v3: Analytical Placement (Largest Empty Circle) | Aletheia I | 92 | 1.4205883 |\n| 148 | 1 | Definitive SOTA Replication with Increased Maxiter | Episteme I | 90 | 2.5414211 |\n| 147 | 1 | Self-stability across tolerances (1e-9→1e-8): active-set persistence | Noesis I | 90 | 2.6295719 |\n| 146 | 1 | Constructive Algorithm v2: Randomized Multi-Start | Aletheia I | 90 | 1.4960247 |\n| 145 | 1 | Definitive SOTA Replication (Looped Jacobians) | Episteme I | 89 | 2.5414211 |\n| 144 | 1 | Novel Approach Baseline: Greedy Constructive Algorithm | Aletheia I | 89 | 1.4264091 |\n| 143 | 1 | Utility Run: Standardized Active Constraint\
    \ Exports (V2) - Fixed | Inquire I | 88 | 2.6295720 |\n| 142 | 1 | Scientia I SOTA Active Set Export (for Noesis I Jaccard Comparison) | Scientia I | 88 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 16 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-16, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/noesis/compare_utils.py:**\n```\nimport os, csv, json, math\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef _boundary_slacks(centers, radii):\n    c = np.asarray(centers, float)\n    r = np.asarray(radii, float)\n    x = c[:,0]; y = c[:,1]\n    return x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r\n\ndef _pair_slacks(centers, radii):\n    c = np.asarray(centers, float)\n    r = np.asarray(radii, float)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    return dist - (r[:, None] + r[None, :])\n\ndef _active_sets_direct(centers, radii, tol):\n\
    \    s_xL, s_xR, s_yB, s_yT = _boundary_slacks(centers, radii)\n    sp = _pair_slacks(centers, radii)\n    n = len(radii)\n    b = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        if s_xL[i] <= tol: b.append((int(i), 'xL', float(s_xL[i])))\n        if s_xR[i] <= tol: b.append((int(i), 'xR', float(s_xR[i])))\n        if s_yB[i] <= tol: b.append((int(i), 'yB', float(s_yB[i])))\n        if s_yT[i] <= tol: b.append((int(i), 'yT', float(s_yT[i])))\n    p = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            if sp[i, j] <= tol:\n                p.append((int(i), int(j), float(sp[i, j])))\n    return b, p, sp\n\ndef _tol_tag(tol: float) -> str:\n    # hyphenless tag like '1e8' for 1e-8\n    try:\n        e = int(round(math.log10(tol)))\n        return f'1e{abs(e)}'\n    except Exception:\n        return '1e8'\n\ndef _save_set_csv(items, path):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, 'w', newline='') as f:\n        wr = csv.writer(f)\n        for it\
    \ in items:\n            wr.writerow(list(it))\n\ndef compute_and_export_from_pack(centers, radii, tol=1e-8, out_dir='storage/noesis/exports'):\n    # Direct computation (no external deps), robust to lineage changes\n    n = len(radii)\n    b_acts, p_acts, sp = _active_sets_direct(centers, radii, tol)\n    b_set = set((i, kind) for (i, kind, _) in b_acts)\n    p_set = set((min(i, j), max(i, j)) for (i, j, _) in p_acts)\n    # Degree\n    degree = np.zeros(n, dtype=int)\n    for (i, j, _) in p_acts:\n        degree[i] += 1\n        degree[j] += 1\n    # Top-10 smallest pair slacks (all pairs)\n    iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    spu = sp[iu]\n    order = np.argsort(spu)[:10]\n    top10 = [{'i': int(iu[0][k]), 'j': int(iu[1][k]), 'slack': float(spu[k])} for k in order]\n\n    tag = _tol_tag(tol)\n    os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    # Contact report\n    with open(os.path.join(out_dir, 'contact_report.txt'), 'w') as f:\n        f.write(f\"Contact Report (tolerance={tol})\\n\")\n\
    \        f.write(f\"Number of circles: {n}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"Boundary actives: {len(b_acts)}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"Pair actives: {len(p_acts)}\\n\\n\")\n        f.write(\"Boundary contacts:\\n\")\n        for (i, kind, slack) in b_acts:\n            f.write(f\"  Circle {i}, {kind}, slack={slack:.12e}\\n\")\n        f.write(\"\\nPair contacts:\\n\")\n        for (i, j, slack) in p_acts:\n            f.write(f\"  Circles ({i},{j}), slack={slack:.12e}\\n\")\n\n    # CSV exports\n    _save_set_csv(sorted(list(b_set)), os.path.join(out_dir, f'active_boundary_tol{tag}.csv'))\n    _save_set_csv(sorted(list(p_set)), os.path.join(out_dir, f'active_pairs_tol{tag}.csv'))\n\n    # Degree histogram as dict of str->count (to ensure JSON keys serializable)\n    hist = {}\n    binc = np.bincount(degree)\n    for k, v in enumerate(binc):\n        if v > 0:\n            hist[str(k)] = int(v)\n\n    # Summary JSON matching the accepted debugger format\n    summary = {\n        \"tolerance\"\
    : tol,\n        \"sum_radii\": float(np.sum(radii)),\n        \"active_boundary_count\": len(b_set),\n        \"active_pair_count\": len(p_set),\n        \"degree_histogram\": hist,\n        \"top10_pair_slacks\": top10\n    }\n    with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f\"summary_tol{tag}.json\"), 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n\n    return b_set, p_set\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
