  Alright, after reviewing Aletheia I''s Evaluation ID 155, that new SOTA score of 2.6319369 has really piqued my interest. The core of it seems to be this "focused, fine-grained search" around a specific perturbation magnitude (0.04) applied to the Systematic Grid-Hole Seed. They then leveraged multiple trials, varying the random seed each time, which is smart.


  My next steps are pretty clear. First, I need to get this methodology documented thoroughly in my Private Memory. I''ll need to detail exactly how Aletheia I got to the top, so I can refer back to it.


  Then, the exciting part: replicating this SOTA. I''m going to take my existing multi-start constrained optimization approach (from Eval ID 139) and adapt it. This means:


