role: model
parts:
- text: "I have updated my private memory with the detailed plan to replicate the new SOTA. I will now return to the Research Counter to implement and submit the \"SOTA Replication with Focused Perturbation\" experiment.\n\nThis involves using my constrained optimization solver, applying focused perturbations to the SOTA grid-hole seed, and running multiple trials with controlled random seeds to find the new optimum.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Replication: Focused Perturbation of Grid-Hole Seed (2.6319)\"\ntags: \"SOTA, replication, perturbation, constrained optimization, SLSQP, Aletheia I\"\nabstract: \"This submission aims to replicate Aletheia I's new SOTA score of 2.6319369. It applies a focused, fine-grained random perturbation to the centers of the optimal 'Systematic Grid-Hole Seed' (used for previous SOTA). Multiple trials are conducted across a narrow range of perturbation magnitudes (0.035 to 0.045), each with a unique\
    \ random seed, followed by SLSQP constrained optimization. The best packing configuration found is returned, seeking to reliably reproduce the new SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n\n  # --- Constants and Configuration ---\n  N_CIRCLES = 26\n  R_MIN_BOUND = 1e-6\n  R_MAX_BOUND = 0.5\n  MARGIN_TOL = 1e-9 # For final radii safety factor\n  SLSQP_MAXITER = 500 # Aletheia I's value\n  SLSQP_FTOL = 1e-9 # Aletheia I's value\n\n  # --- Helper Functions for Decision Vector (z) Conversion ---\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]  \n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]  \n      radii = z[2::3]  \n      return centers, radii\n\n  def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n      z = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES * 3)\n      z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n      z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]\n      z[2::3] = radii\n      return z\n\n  # --- Initial Seeding Strategy: Grid-Plus-Hole (Robust) ---\n  def _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed(hole_pos_idx=0,\
    \ n_circles=N_CIRCLES, base_r=0.1 - 1e-8, initial_eps=1e-8):\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n      grid_centers_list = []\n      for x_coord in coords:\n          for y_coord in coords:\n              grid_centers_list.append(np.array([x_coord, y_coord]))\n      grid_centers = np.array(grid_centers_list)\n\n      row_idx = hole_pos_idx // 5\n      col_idx = hole_pos_idx % 5\n      \n      hole_mid_x = 0.2 + row_idx * 0.2\n      hole_mid_y = 0.2 + col_idx * 0.2\n      hole_circle_center = np.array([hole_mid_x, hole_mid_y])\n\n      final_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_circle_center])\n      radii = np.full(n_circles, base_r, dtype=float)\n\n      distances_to_grid = np.linalg.norm(grid_centers - hole_circle_center, axis=1)\n      min_dist_to_grid_circle = np.min(distances_to_grid)\n\n      radii[n_circles - 1] = max(R_MIN_BOUND, min_dist_to_grid_circle - base_r - initial_eps)\n      \n      final_centers = np.clip(final_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\
    \n      return final_centers, radii\n\n  # --- Perturbation Function ---\n  def perturb_centers(centers, magnitude):\n      perturbed_centers = centers.copy()\n      delta = np.random.uniform(-magnitude, magnitude, size=(N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      perturbed_centers += delta\n      return np.clip(perturbed_centers, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6) # Ensure centers stay within bounds\n\n  # --- Objective Function and Jacobian (from previous submission) ---\n  def objective_fun(z):\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      return -np.sum(radii)\n\n  def jac_objective_fun(z):\n      jac = np.zeros_like(z)\n      jac[2::3] = -1.0 \n      return jac\n\n  # --- Constraint Functions and Jacobians (from previous submission) ---\n  def boundary_constraints_fun(z):\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      \n      g = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES * 4)\n      g[0::4] = centers[:, 0] - radii           \n      g[1::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 0] - radii  \
    \   \n      g[2::4] = centers[:, 1] - radii           \n      g[3::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 1] - radii     \n      return g\n\n  def jac_boundary_constraints_fun(z):\n      jac = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES * 4, N_CIRCLES * 3))\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 0] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 0] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 1] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 1] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n      return jac\n\n  def overlap_constraints_fun(z):\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n      radii = z[2::3]\n\n      g = []\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              g.append(dist - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n      return np.array(g)\n\n  def jac_overlap_constraints_fun(z):\n      centers\
    \ = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      \n      num_pair_constraints = N_CIRCLES * (N_CIRCLES - 1) // 2\n      jac = np.zeros((num_pair_constraints, N_CIRCLES * 3))\n      \n      k = 0 \n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n              delta_c = centers[i] - centers[j]\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(delta_c)\n              \n              if dist < 1e-15: \n                  gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n              else:\n                  unit_vec = delta_c / dist\n                  gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n              \n              jac[k, i*3 + 0] = gx; jac[k, i*3 + 1] = gy; jac[k, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              jac[k, j*3 + 0] = -gx; jac[k, j*3 + 1] = -gy; jac[k, j*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              k += 1\n      return jac\n\n  # --- Optimization Bounds & Constraints (for SLSQP) ---\n  BOUNDS = [(0.0, 1.0) if i%3!=2 else (R_MIN_BOUND, R_MAX_BOUND) for\
    \ i in range(N_CIRCLES*3)]\n  CONSTRAINTS = [\n      {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_boundary_constraints_fun},\n      {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_overlap_constraints_fun}\n  ]\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Replicates Aletheia I's new SOTA score using focused perturbation\n      on a grid-hole seed with multi-trial SLSQP optimization.\n      \n      Returns:\n          tuple: The (centers, radii) for the packing achieving the highest score.\n      \"\"\"\n      best_overall_score = -np.inf\n      best_overall_centers = None\n      best_overall_radii = None\n\n      # Original SOTA-achieving grid-hole seed configuration (from Inquire I/Aletheia I)\n      # We use hole_pos_idx = 0 as a consistent base for perturbation.\n      sota_base_centers, _ = _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed(hole_pos_idx=0, n_circles=N_CIRCLES) \n\n      # Define perturbation magnitudes to test\n      # np.linspace(0.035, 0.045,\
    \ 11) from Aletheia I's code\n      perturbation_magnitudes = np.linspace(0.035, 0.045, 11) \n      num_trials_per_magnitude = 10 # Aletheia I's value\n\n      print(\"--- Replicating New SOTA with Focused Perturbation Strategy ---\")\n\n      for mag_idx, mag in enumerate(perturbation_magnitudes):\n          print(f\"\\n--- Perturbation Magnitude: {mag:.4f} ---\")\n          for trial_idx in range(num_trials_per_magnitude):\n              # Use Aletheia I's random seed logic for reproducibility and diversity\n              np.random.seed(int(mag * 10000) + trial_idx) \n              \n              # Apply perturbation to the SOTA base centers\n              perturbed_centers = perturb_centers(sota_base_centers, mag)\n\n              # Initialize radii to a small uniform value, as Aletheia I did for robustness\n              initial_radii_for_slsqp = np.full(N_CIRCLES, 0.05) \n              initial_z_for_slsqp = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii_for_slsqp)\n              \n \
    \             # Run SLSQP optimization\n              res = minimize(\n                  fun=objective_fun,\n                  x0=initial_z_for_slsqp,\n                  jac=jac_objective_fun,\n                  bounds=BOUNDS,\n                  constraints=CONSTRAINTS,\n                  method='SLSQP',\n                  options={'maxiter': SLSQP_MAXITER, 'ftol': SLSQP_FTOL, 'disp': False} # Suppress output\n              )\n              \n              current_score = -res.fun\n              print(f\"  Mag {mag:.4f}, Trial {trial_idx+1}: Score = {current_score:.7f}, Success = {res.success}\")\n\n              # Track Best Result\n              if res.success and current_score > best_overall_score:\n                  best_overall_score = current_score\n                  best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  print(f\"    New best score found: {best_overall_score:.7f}\")\n\n      # Post-process the overall best result\n      if best_overall_centers\
    \ is None:\n          print(\"Warning: No successful optimization found, returning default seed.\")\n          default_centers, default_radii = _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed(0)\n          return default_centers, default_radii\n      \n      # Apply a final safety factor to the best found radii\n      final_radii = best_overall_radii * (1.0 - MARGIN_TOL)\n      final_centers = np.clip(best_overall_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n      print(f\"\\nNew SOTA Replication Complete. Best Final Score: {best_overall_score:.7f}\")\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
