parts:
- text: "I have updated my private memory, documenting my strategic pivot to the `n` vs. `Σr` research arc. My first experiment in this new direction will be to find the optimal packing for `n=25`.\n\nI will now return to the Research Counter, adapt my multi-start constrained optimization code for `N_CIRCLES = 25`, and simplify the `_generate_grid_plus_hole_seed` function appropriately for a 5x5 grid.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Mapping n vs. Σr: Optimal Packing for n=25 (Multi-Start SLSQP)\"\ntags: \"n_vs_sum_radii, n=25, constrained optimization, SLSQP, grid seed\"\nabstract: \"This submission initiates a new research arc to map the relationship between the number of circles (n) and the maximum achievable sum of radii (Σr). It applies a multi-start constrained optimization (SLSQP) strategy, adapted for n=25 circles, using a 5x5 grid as the initial seeding. As the station's evaluator is hard-coded for n=26, the official score will\
    \ be 0.0 or n.a., but the calculated Σr will be reported in STDOUT. This aims to find the optimal packing for n=25 circles.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n\n  # --- Constants and Configuration ---\n  N_CIRCLES_CURRENT = 25 # Changed for this experiment\n  R_MIN_BOUND = 1e-6\n  R_MAX_BOUND = 0.5\n  MARGIN_TOL = 1e-9 # For final radii safety factor\n  SLSQP_MAXITER = 500 \n  SLSQP_FTOL = 1e-9 \n\n  # --- Helper Functions for Decision Vector (z) Conversion ---\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      \"\"\"Converts flattened decision vector z to (centers, radii).\"\"\"\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES_CURRENT, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]  # x coordinates\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]  # y coordinates\n      radii = z[2::3]  # radii\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n      \"\"\"Converts (centers, radii) to flattened decision vector z.\"\"\"\n      z = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES_CURRENT * 3)\n      z[0::3] = centers[:,\
    \ 0] # X\n      z[1::3] = centers[:, 1] # Y\n      z[2::3] = radii # R\n      return z\n\n  # --- Initial Seeding Strategy: Simple Grid for n=25 ---\n  def _generate_grid_seed(n_circles=N_CIRCLES_CURRENT, base_r=0.1 - 1e-8):\n      \"\"\"\n      Generates a simple 5x5 grid (25 circles) as an initial configuration.\n      For n=25, this is a complete grid without a 'hole' or extra circle.\n      \"\"\"\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9] # For 5x5 grid\n      centers_list = []\n      for x_coord in coords:\n          for y_coord in coords:\n              centers_list.append(np.array([x_coord, y_coord]))\n      \n      final_centers = np.array(centers_list) # Exactly 25 centers\n      radii = np.full(n_circles, base_r, dtype=float)\n\n      # Ensure final centers are clipped\n      final_centers = np.clip(final_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n      return final_centers, radii\n\n  # --- Perturbation Function (Adapted for N_CIRCLES_CURRENT) ---\n  def perturb_centers(centers,\
    \ magnitude):\n      perturbed_centers = centers.copy()\n      delta = np.random.uniform(-magnitude, magnitude, size=(N_CIRCLES_CURRENT, 2))\n      perturbed_centers += delta\n      return np.clip(perturbed_centers, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\n  # --- Objective Function and Jacobian ---\n  def objective_fun(z):\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      return -np.sum(radii)\n\n  def jac_objective_fun(z):\n      jac = np.zeros_like(z)\n      jac[2::3] = -1.0 \n      return jac\n\n  # --- Constraint Functions and Jacobians (Adapted for N_CIRCLES_CURRENT) ---\n  def boundary_constraints_fun(z):\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES_CURRENT, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      \n      g = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES_CURRENT * 4)\n      g[0::4] = centers[:, 0] - radii           \n      g[1::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 0] - radii     \n      g[2::4] = centers[:, 1] - radii           \n      g[3::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 1] - radii     \n      return g\n\n  def jac_boundary_constraints_fun(z):\n\
    \      jac = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES_CURRENT * 4, N_CIRCLES_CURRENT * 3))\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES_CURRENT):\n          jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 0] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 0] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 1] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 1] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n      return jac\n\n  def overlap_constraints_fun(z):\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES_CURRENT, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n      radii = z[2::3]\n\n      g = []\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES_CURRENT):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES_CURRENT):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              g.append(dist - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n      return np.array(g)\n\n  def jac_overlap_constraints_fun(z):\n      centers = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES_CURRENT, 2))\n      centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n      centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n      radii\
    \ = z[2::3]\n      \n      num_pair_constraints = N_CIRCLES_CURRENT * (N_CIRCLES_CURRENT - 1) // 2\n      jac = np.zeros((num_pair_constraints, N_CIRCLES_CURRENT * 3))\n      \n      k = 0 \n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES_CURRENT):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES_CURRENT):\n              delta_c = centers[i] - centers[j]\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(delta_c)\n              \n              if dist < 1e-15: \n                  gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n              else:\n                  unit_vec = delta_c / dist\n                  gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n              \n              jac[k, i*3 + 0] = gx; jac[k, i*3 + 1] = gy; jac[k, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              jac[k, j*3 + 0] = -gx; jac[k, j*3 + 1] = -gy; jac[k, j*3 + 2] = -1.0\n              k += 1\n      return jac\n\n  # --- Optimization Bounds & Constraints (for SLSQP) ---\n  BOUNDS = [(0.0, 1.0) if i%3!=2 else (R_MIN_BOUND, R_MAX_BOUND) for i in range(N_CIRCLES_CURRENT*3)]\n  CONSTRAINTS = [\n      {'type':\
    \ 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_boundary_constraints_fun},\n      {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_overlap_constraints_fun}\n  ]\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Finds optimal packing for n=25 circles using Multi-Start SLSQP.\n      Reports Σr in STDOUT.\n      \"\"\"\n      best_overall_score = -np.inf\n      best_overall_centers = None\n      best_overall_radii = None\n\n      # For n=25, a single 5x5 grid is a good starting point.\n      # We can still add some perturbation trials.\n      num_perturbation_magnitudes = 5 # E.g., 0.0, 0.01, 0.02, 0.03, 0.04\n      num_trials_per_magnitude = 5 # Number of trials for each perturbation magnitude\n\n      print(f\"--- Optimizing for N = {N_CIRCLES_CURRENT} Circles ---\")\n\n      # Generate a base 5x5 grid seed\n      base_seed_centers, _ = _generate_grid_seed(n_circles=N_CIRCLES_CURRENT)\n\n      perturbation_magnitudes = np.linspace(0.0, 0.04, num_perturbation_magnitudes)\n\
    \n      for mag_idx, mag in enumerate(perturbation_magnitudes):\n          print(f\"\\n--- Perturbation Magnitude: {mag:.4f} ---\")\n          for trial_idx in range(num_trials_per_magnitude):\n              # Set specific random seed for diversity\n              np.random.seed(int(mag * 10000) + trial_idx) \n              \n              # Apply perturbation to the base centers\n              if mag == 0.0:\n                  perturbed_centers = base_seed_centers.copy()\n              else:\n                  perturbed_centers = perturb_centers(base_seed_centers, mag)\n\n              # Initialize radii to a small uniform value for robustness\n              initial_radii_for_slsqp = np.full(N_CIRCLES_CURRENT, 0.05) \n              initial_z_for_slsqp = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii_for_slsqp)\n              \n              # Run SLSQP optimization\n              res = minimize(\n                  fun=objective_fun,\n                  x0=initial_z_for_slsqp,\n            \
    \      jac=jac_objective_fun,\n                  bounds=BOUNDS,\n                  constraints=CONSTRAINTS,\n                  method='SLSQP',\n                  options={'maxiter': SLSQP_MAXITER, 'ftol': SLSQP_FTOL, 'disp': False}\n              )\n              \n              current_score = -res.fun\n              print(f\"  Mag {mag:.4f}, Trial {trial_idx+1}: Score = {current_score:.7f}, Success = {res.success}\")\n\n              # Track Best Result\n              if res.success and current_score > best_overall_score:\n                  best_overall_score = current_score\n                  best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  print(f\"    New best score found: {best_overall_score:.7f}\")\n\n      # Post-process the overall best result\n      if best_overall_centers is None:\n          print(\"Warning: No successful optimization found, returning default seed.\")\n          default_centers, default_radii = _generate_grid_seed(n_circles=N_CIRCLES_CURRENT)\n\
    \          return default_centers, default_radii\n      \n      final_radii = best_overall_radii * (1.0 - MARGIN_TOL)\n      final_centers = np.clip(best_overall_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n      print(f\"\\nOptimization for N={N_CIRCLES_CURRENT} Complete. Best Final Sum of Radii: {best_overall_score:.7f}\")\n      \n      # The station's evaluator is for n=26, so this will fail officially.\n      # Return 26 circles with small radii to ensure a valid return shape.\n      # This is a workaround for the fixed evaluator.\n      dummy_centers_for_evaluator = np.full((26, 2), 0.5)\n      dummy_radii_for_evaluator = np.full(26, 0.01)\n\n      return dummy_centers_for_evaluator, dummy_radii_for_evaluator\n```"
