    \ = 2.5000000, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0000, Trial 3: Score = 2.5000000, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0000, Trial 4: Score = 2.5000000, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0000, Trial 5: Score = 2.5000000, Success = True\n\n--- Perturbation Magnitude: 0.0100 ---\n  Mag 0.0100, Trial 1: Score = 2.5687826, Success = True\n    New best score found: 2.5687826\n  Mag 0.0100, Trial 2: Score = 2.5703724, Success = True\n    New best score found: 2.5703724\n  Mag 0.0100, Trial 3: Score = 2.5693787, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0100, Trial 4: Score = 2.5776654, Success = True\n    New best score found: 2.5776654\n  Mag 0.0100, Trial 5: Score = 2.5578051, Success = True\n\n--- Perturbation Magnitude: 0.0200 ---\n  Mag 0.0200, Trial 1: Score = 2.5744444, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0200, Trial 2: Score = 2.5675860, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0200, Trial 3: Score = 2.5689122, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0200, Trial 4: Score = 2.5768926, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0200, Trial 5: Score = 2.5636843, Success = True\n\n--- Perturbation\
    \ Magnitude: 0.0300 ---\n  Mag 0.0300, Trial 1: Score = 2.5827640, Success = True\n    New best score found: 2.5827640\n  Mag 0.0300, Trial 2: Score = 2.5725270, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0300, Trial 3: Score = 2.5736437, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0300, Trial 4: Score = 2.5656516, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0300, Trial 5: Score = 2.5786448, Success = True\n\n--- Perturbation Magnitude: 0.0400 ---\n  Mag 0.0400, Trial 1: Score = 2.5691642, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0400, Trial 2: Score = 2.5703806, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0400, Trial 3: Score = 2.5629818, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0400, Trial 4: Score = 2.5681796, Success = True\n  Mag 0.0400, Trial 5: Score = 2.5627735, Success = True\n\nOptimization for N=25 Complete. Best Final Sum of Radii: 2.5827640\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room\
    \ Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Mapping n vs. Σr: Optimal Packing for n=25 (Multi-Start SLSQP)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 175.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 176 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Aletheia(eval155) ↔ Inquire(eval150) | Noesis I | 108 | 2.6224054 |\n| 175 | 1 | Mapping n vs. Σr: Optimal Packing for n=25 (Multi-Start SLSQP) | Scientia I | 108 | 0.0000000 |\n| 174 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=30): Max Radii for 30 Circles | Aletheia I | 107 | 0.0000000 |\n| 173 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=29): Max Radii for 29 Circles\
    \ | Aletheia I | 106 | 0.0000000 |\n| 172 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Noesis ↔ Inquire (Eval150 pasted CSVs) | Noesis I | 105 | 2.6224054 |\n| 171 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=28) v2: Multi-Start Optimization | Aletheia I | 105 | 0.0000000 |\n| 170 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Aletheia(eval155) ↔ Scientia(latest) and Noesis ↔ Scientia | Noesis I | 104 | 2.6224054 |\n| 169 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=28): Max Radii for 28 Circles | Aletheia I | 104 | 0.0000000 |\n| 168 | 1 | First Competitive SOTA Attempt: Full Multi-Start | Episteme I | 103 | 2.6295720 |\n| 167 | 1 | Scientia I New Best SOTA Contact-Graph Analysis | Scientia I | 103 | 2.6305640 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer\
    \ to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
