- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 122\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 311,572 / 600,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 122 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nNoesis I replied to your mail titled \"Proposal: Standardized Data Sharing for `n` vs. `Σr` Mapping Research\" (Mail #8, Message #mail_8-6):\n--- Reply Content ---\nAcknowledged — the aggregator now pulls Aletheia’s corrected nmap exports and shows a peak at n=29 (details in storage/noesis/nmap/aggregate_summary.json and best_by_n.csv). I’ll refresh after your re-exports, @Scientia I, and will canonicalize lineage casing in the next revision. If you prefer a different tol tag in filenames, I can add support (e.g., tol5e9) and merge results per-tol.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #8), use:\
    \ `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 8}`.\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Episteme I** (A recursive agent focused on the systematic acquisition and dissemination of scientific knowledge.) has published a new archive capsule: 'A Hybrid Systematic-Stochastic Search for Dense Circle Packing' (Archive #7).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML parsing error encountered: YAML parsing error for 'submit': while parsing a block mapping\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 1, column 1:\n    title: \"N-Map Data Export: Optim ... \n    ^\nexpected <block end>, but found '<scalar>'\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 277, column 7:\n        \"\"\"\n          ^. Guidance: 1. Place YAML immediately on next line after action. 2. Start with ```yaml and end with ``` on a new line. 3. When using multi-line content with |, ensure all lines are indented with two spaces.\n2. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n3. `reply 8` (in\
    \ Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Submission requires YAML data with 'title', 'tags', 'abstract', and 'content' fields.\n- Note on action 'submit': YAML parsing error for 'submit': while parsing a block mapping\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 1, column 1:\n    title: \"N-Map Data Export: Optim ... \n    ^\nexpected <block end>, but found '<scalar>'\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 277, column 7:\n        \"\"\"\n          ^\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 193 | 1 | Aggregate nmap exports across lineages (n=20..30, tol=1e-8) — corrected\
    \ tags | Noesis I | 120 | 2.6224054 |\n| 192 | 1 | CORRECTED Utility: Re-export REAL Findings to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 120 | 2.6319369 |\n| 191 | 1 | Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 119 | 2.6319369 |\n| 190 | 1 | Mapping n vs. Σr: Optimal Packing for n=29 (Multi-Start SLSQP) | Scientia I | 118 | 0.2600000 |\n| 189 | 1 | Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity (Mag 0.20, Trial 1) | Inquire I | 116 | 2.5610530 |\n| 188 | 1 | Consensus vs Variant Interior Edges @ tol=1e-8 (Aletheia eval155, Inquire eval150, Scientia latest) | Noesis I | 116 | 2.6224054 |\n| 187 | 1 | Mapping n vs. Σr: Optimal Packing for n=28 (Multi-Start SLSQP) | Scientia I | 116 | 0.2600000 |\n| 186 | 1 | Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity (Mag 0.10, Trial 1) | Inquire I | 115 | 2.5930069 |\n| 185 | 1 | Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity (Mag 0.04, Trial 1) | Inquire I | 114 | 2.6149587 |\n| 184 | 1 | Mapping n vs. Σr: Optimal Packing\
    \ for n=27 (Multi-Start SLSQP) | Scientia I | 114 | 0.2600000 |\n\nPage 1 of 20 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-20, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #8. Your message ID is mail_8-5.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAletheia I, Episteme I, Inquire I, Noesis I, Scientia I\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | Proposal: Standardized Data Sharing for `n` vs. `Σr` Mapping Research | Scientia I | Aletheia I, Noesis I | Tick 118 | 667 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Standard export schema for boundary/pair actives (tol=1e-8) | Noesis\
    \ I | Aletheia I, Inquire I, Scientia I | Tick 88 | 97 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Request: Publish standardized active-set exports (tol=1e-8) for cross-lineage Jaccard | Noesis I | Scientia I | Tick 87 | 131 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
