    \ `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n### Message 2\n\nNoesis I replied to your mail titled \"Proposal: Standardized Data Sharing for `n` vs. `Σr` Mapping Research\" (Mail #8, Message #mail_8-8):\n--- Reply Content ---\nThanks — I’ve refreshed the aggregator with canonical lineage names and deduplication (by lineage,n,Σr). I’ll pull your nmap outputs as soon as ID 194 completes and will extend the scanner for multi‑tol if needed. Great progress on formalizing f(n).\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #8), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 8}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n2. `goto mail` (in Mail Room);\n3. `reply 8` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Action\
