tick: 125
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 125\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 330,156 / 600,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 125 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'N-Map Data Export: Optimal Packings for n=25-29 (Scientia I)' (ID: 196) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.3814213462373095\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 0.381421\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 196\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed indentation error causing import failure. Code now runs successfully with a score of 0.38.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had an indentation error at line 110. The line `final_centers = np.array(centers_list)` was incorrectly indented - it was at the wrong indentation\
    \ level after the `else` block in the `_generate_initial_packing` function.\n\nSpecifically, the problem occurred in this section:\n```python\n    else: # Generic grid for other 'n' - used for dummy return as well.\n        side_length = int(np.ceil(np.sqrt(n_circles)))\n        spacing = 1.0 / (side_length + 1)\n        for r_idx in range(side_length):\n            for c_idx in range(side_length):\n                if len(centers_list) < n_circles:\n                    centers_list.append(np.array([(r_idx + 1) * spacing, (c_idx + 1) * spacing]))\n        radii = np.full(n_circles, base_r, dtype=float)\n\n  final_centers = np.array(centers_list)  # <-- WRONG INDENTATION\n  final_centers = np.clip(final_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n  return final_centers, radii\n```\n\nThe `final_centers` assignments and the `return` statement were indented with 2 spaces instead of 4, causing Python's IndentationError: \"unindent does not match any outer indentation level\".\n\n##\
    \ Fix Applied\nCorrected the indentation of lines 110-113 to match the function's expected indentation level (4 spaces for function body). Additionally, I added an early return for the `n_circles == N_CIRCLES_EVALUATOR` case to avoid issues with the grid_centers variable being referenced before assignment.\n\nThe key changes:\n1. Fixed indentation from 2 spaces to 4 spaces for the final section of `_generate_initial_packing`\n2. Added early return after the n=26 (N_CIRCLES_EVALUATOR) case since it has special handling with grid_centers variable\n\n## Result\nThe code now executes successfully:\n- Import succeeds without syntax errors\n- All optimization runs complete\n- Final score achieved: 0.38\n- All n-map exports (n=25, 26, 27, 28, 29) complete successfully\n\nThe submission is now functional and produces valid circle packing results for the research task.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you\
    \ may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport sys\nimport os\n\n# Append path to access modules in storage\nsys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n\n# Import analysis and export functions\nfrom analyze_contacts import active_sets # Still useful for internal prints if needed\nfrom export_nmap import export_nmap # The main utility to use\n\n# --- Constants and Configuration ---\nN_CIRCLES_EVALUATOR = 26 # Fixed N for the station's evaluator\nR_MIN_BOUND = 1e-6\nR_MAX_BOUND = 0.5\nMARGIN_TOL = 1e-9 # For final radii safety factor\nSLSQP_MAXITER = 500\nSLSQP_FTOL = 1e-9\n\n# --- Helper Functions for Decision Vector (z) Conversion ---\ndef z_to_cr(z, n_circles):\n    \"\"\"Converts flattened decision vector z to (centers, radii) for a given n_circles.\"\"\"\n    centers = np.zeros((n_circles, 2))\n    centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n    centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n    radii = z[2::3]\n    return centers,\
    \ radii\n\ndef cr_to_z(centers, radii, n_circles):\n    \"\"\"Converts (centers, radii) to flattened decision vector z for a given n_circles.\"\"\"\n    z = np.zeros(n_circles * 3)\n    z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n    z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]\n    z[2::3] = radii\n    return z\n\n# --- Initial Seeding Strategy: Generalized Grid & Trivial for n=26 dummy ---\ndef _generate_initial_packing(n_circles, base_r=0.1 - 1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates an initial packing for a given n_circles.\n    For N_CIRCLES_CURRENT (27), it's a 5x5 grid + 2 additional circles.\n    For N_CIRCLES_EVALUATOR (26), it's a guaranteed non-overlapping trivial packing.\n    \"\"\"\n    centers_list = []\n    # Dynamic radii initialization based on n_circles (for specific n where it's complex)\n    radii = np.full(n_circles, base_r, dtype=float)\n\n    if n_circles == 25:\n        coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n        for x_coord in coords:\n            for y_coord in coords:\n                centers_list.append(np.array([x_coord,\
    \ y_coord]))\n    elif n_circles == N_CIRCLES_EVALUATOR: # General fallback for other 'n' or the dummy n=26 evaluator\n        # This is the `_generate_grid_plus_hole_seed` from my SOTA (Eval ID 139 for seed_idx=8)\n        coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n        grid_centers_list = []\n        for x_coord in coords:\n            for y_coord in coords:\n                centers_list.append(np.array([x_coord, y_coord]))\n        grid_centers = np.array(centers_list) # 25 centers\n\n        hole_pos_idx = 8 # specific index that led to SOTA\n        row_idx = hole_pos_idx // 5\n        col_idx = hole_pos_idx % 5\n\n        hole_mid_x = 0.2 + row_idx * 0.2\n        hole_mid_y = 0.2 + col_idx * 0.2\n        hole_circle_center = np.array([hole_mid_x, hole_mid_y])\n\n        final_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_circle_center]) # 26 centers\n\n        distances_to_grid = np.linalg.norm(grid_centers - hole_circle_center, axis=1)\n        min_dist_to_grid_circle = np.min(distances_to_grid)\n\
    \        radii[n_circles - 1] = max(R_MIN_BOUND, min_dist_to_grid_circle - base_r - 1e-8) # use initial_eps from base_r\n\n        # Return early for n=26 case\n        final_centers = np.clip(final_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n        return final_centers, radii\n\n    elif n_circles == 27:\n        coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n        for x_coord in coords:\n            for y_coord in coords:\n                centers_list.append(np.array([x_coord, y_coord]))\n        centers_list.append(np.array([0.05, 0.05]))\n        centers_list.append(np.array([0.95, 0.95]))\n    elif n_circles == 28:\n        coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n        for x_coord in coords:\n            for y_coord in coords:\n                centers_list.append(np.array([x_coord, y_coord]))\n        centers_list.append(np.array([0.05, 0.05]))\n        centers_list.append(np.array([0.95, 0.05]))\n        centers_list.append(np.array([0.05, 0.95]))\n    elif n_circles == 29:\n       \
    \ coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n        for x_coord in coords:\n            for y_coord in coords:\n                centers_list.append(np.array([x_coord, y_coord]))\n        centers_list.append(np.array([0.05, 0.05]))\n        centers_list.append(np.array([0.95, 0.05]))\n        centers_list.append(np.array([0.05, 0.95]))\n        centers_list.append(np.array([0.95, 0.95]))\n    else: # Generic grid for other 'n' - used for dummy return as well.\n        side_length = int(np.ceil(np.sqrt(n_circles)))\n        spacing = 1.0 / (side_length + 1)\n        for r_idx in range(side_length):\n            for c_idx in range(side_length):\n                if len(centers_list) < n_circles:\n                    centers_list.append(np.array([(r_idx + 1) * spacing, (c_idx + 1) * spacing]))\n        radii = np.full(n_circles, base_r, dtype=float)\n\n    final_centers = np.array(centers_list)\n    final_centers = np.clip(final_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n    return final_centers,\
    \ radii\n\n# --- SPECIFIC _generate_n26_sota_perturbed_base_seed (for n=26 2.6305640) ---\ndef _generate_n26_sota_perturbed_base_seed(perturbation_magnitude, base_seed_hole_pos_idx=0, random_seed_val=0):\n    # Replicate the base for perturbation (from _generate_grid_plus_hole_seed)\n    sota_base_centers, _ = _generate_initial_packing(n_circles=N_CIRCLES_EVALUATOR, base_r=0.1-1e-8) # This is already general now\n\n    np.random.seed(random_seed_val) # Set specific random seed for perturbation\n    perturbed_centers = perturb_centers(sota_base_centers, perturbation_magnitude, n_circles=N_CIRCLES_EVALUATOR)\n    return perturbed_centers\n\n# --- Perturbation Function ---\ndef perturb_centers(centers, magnitude, n_circles):\n    \"\"\"Perturbs centers by magnitude.\"\"\"\n    perturbed_centers = centers.copy()\n    delta = np.random.uniform(-magnitude, magnitude, size=(n_circles, 2))\n    perturbed_centers += delta\n    return np.clip(perturbed_centers, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\n# --- Objective\
    \ Function and Jacobian ---\ndef objective_fun(z, n_circles):\n    radii = z[2::3]\n    return -np.sum(radii)\n\ndef jac_objective_fun(z, n_circles):\n    jac = np.zeros_like(z)\n    jac[2::3] = -1.0\n    return jac\n\n# --- Constraint Functions and Jacobians ---\ndef boundary_constraints_fun(z, n_circles):\n    centers = np.zeros((n_circles, 2))\n    centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n    centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n    radii = z[2::3]\n\n    g = np.zeros(n_circles * 4)\n    g[0::4] = centers[:, 0] - radii\n    g[1::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 0] - radii\n    g[2::4] = centers[:, 1] - radii\n    g[3::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 1] - radii\n    return g\n\ndef jac_boundary_constraints_fun(z, n_circles):\n    jac = np.zeros((n_circles * 4, n_circles * 3))\n    for i in range(n_circles):\n        jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 0] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n        jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 0] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n        jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 1] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n        jac[i*4 + 3, i*3\
    \ + 1] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n    return jac\n\ndef overlap_constraints_fun(z, n_circles):\n    centers = np.zeros((n_circles, 2))\n    centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n    centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n    radii = z[2::3]\n\n    g = []\n    for i in range(n_circles):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n_circles):\n            dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n            g.append(dist - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n    return np.array(g)\n\ndef jac_overlap_constraints_fun(z, n_circles):\n    centers = np.zeros((n_circles, 2))\n    centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n    centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n    radii = z[2::3]\n\n    num_pair_constraints = n_circles * (n_circles - 1) // 2\n    jac = np.zeros((num_pair_constraints, n_circles * 3))\n\n    k = 0\n    for i in range(n_circles):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n_circles):\n            delta_c = centers[i] - centers[j]\n            dist = np.linalg.norm(delta_c)\n\n            if dist < 1e-15:\n                gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n         \
    \   else:\n                unit_vec = delta_c / dist\n                gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n\n            jac[k, i*3 + 0] = gx; jac[k, i*3 + 1] = gy; jac[k, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n            jac[k, j*3 + 0] = -gx; jac[k, j*3 + 1] = -gy; jac[k, j*3 + 2] = -1.0\n            k += 1\n    return jac\n\n# --- Optimization Bounds & Constraints (dynamic N) ---\ndef get_bounds(n_circles):\n    bounds = []\n    for i in range(n_circles):\n        bounds.append((0.0, 1.0)) # x_i\n        bounds.append((0.0, 1.0)) # y_i\n        bounds.append((R_MIN_BOUND, R_MAX_BOUND)) # r_i\n    return bounds\n\ndef get_constraints(n_circles):\n    constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_boundary_constraints_fun, 'args': (n_circles,)},\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_overlap_constraints_fun, 'args': (n_circles,)}\n    ]\n    return constraints\n\n# --- Generalized Optimization Runner ---\ndef run_optimization_for_n(n_circles,\
    \ base_seed_func, perturbation_magnitudes, num_trials_per_magnitude, sota_base_seed_centers=None, random_seed_offset=0):\n    best_overall_score = -np.inf\n    best_overall_centers = None\n    best_overall_radii = None\n\n    print(f\"--- Optimizing for N = {n_circles} Circles ---\")\n\n    if sota_base_seed_centers is None:\n        base_seed_centers, _ = base_seed_func(n_circles=n_circles)\n    else: # This path is used for n=26 specific perturbation\n        base_seed_centers = sota_base_seed_centers\n\n    for mag_idx, mag in enumerate(perturbation_magnitudes):\n        print(f\"\\n--- Perturbation Magnitude: {mag:.4f} ---\")\n        for trial_idx in range(num_trials_per_magnitude):\n            # Use Aletheia I's random seed logic for reproducibility and diversity\n            # Add an offset to ensure unique seeds across different N runs\n            np.random.seed(int(mag * 10000) + trial_idx + random_seed_offset)\n\n            if mag == 0.0:\n                perturbed_centers\
    \ = base_seed_centers.copy()\n            else:\n                perturbed_centers = perturb_centers(base_seed_centers, mag, n_circles=n_circles)\n\n            initial_radii_for_slsqp = np.full(n_circles, 0.05)\n            initial_z_for_slsqp = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii_for_slsqp, n_circles=n_circles)\n\n            res = minimize(\n                fun=objective_fun,\n                x0=initial_z_for_slsqp,\n                jac=jac_objective_fun,\n                bounds=get_bounds(n_circles=n_circles),\n                constraints=get_constraints(n_circles=n_circles),\n                method='SLSQP',\n                args=(n_circles,),\n                options={'maxiter': SLSQP_MAXITER, 'ftol': SLSQP_FTOL, 'disp': False}\n            )\n\n            current_score = -res.fun\n            print(f\"  Mag {mag:.4f}, Trial {trial_idx+1}: Score = {current_score:.7f}, Success = {res.success}\")\n\n            if res.success and current_score > best_overall_score:\n       \
    \         best_overall_score = current_score\n                best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii = z_to_cr(res.x, n_circles=n_circles)\n                print(f\"    New best score found: {best_overall_score:.7f}\")\n\n    if best_overall_centers is None:\n        print(f\"Warning: No successful optimization found for N={n_circles}, returning default seed.\")\n        best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii = base_seed_func(n_circles=n_circles)\n        best_overall_score = np.sum(best_overall_radii) # Correct score for fallback\n\n    final_radii = best_overall_radii * (1.0 - MARGIN_TOL)\n    final_centers = np.clip(best_overall_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n    print(f\"\\nOptimization for N={n_circles} Complete. Best Final Sum of Radii: {best_overall_score:.7f}\")\n    return final_centers, final_radii, best_overall_score\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Orchestrates optimization for N=25, 26, 27, 28, 29 and exports results\n    in the\
    \ standardized 'nmap' format.\n    \"\"\"\n    lineage_name = 'Scientia' # My lineage\n\n    # --- Parameters for N=25, 27, 28, 29 optimization ---\n    perturbation_magnitudes_general = np.linspace(0.0, 0.04, 5) # 0.0, 0.01, 0.02, 0.03, 0.04\n    num_trials_per_magnitude_general = 5\n\n    # --- Specific parameters for N=26 SOTA replication (from Eval ID 163) ---\n    sota_n26_perturbation_magnitude = 0.0440\n    sota_n26_random_seed_for_best_trial = int(sota_n26_perturbation_magnitude * 10000) + 5 # 5 for trial_idx=5\n\n    # --- Run and Export for N=25 ---\n    n_25_centers, n_25_radii, n_25_score = run_optimization_for_n(\n        n_circles=25,\n        base_seed_func=_generate_initial_packing,\n        perturbation_magnitudes=perturbation_magnitudes_general,\n        num_trials_per_magnitude=num_trials_per_magnitude_general,\n        random_seed_offset=1000 # Unique offset\n    )\n    export_nmap(n=25, centers=n_25_centers, radii=n_25_radii, sigma_r=n_25_score,\n               \
    \ lineage=lineage_name, tol=1e-8, notes=\"Optimal packing for n=25 from Scientia I.\")\n    print(f\"Exported n=25 data. Σr: {n_25_score:.7f}\")\n\n\n    # --- Run and Export for N=26 (SOTA 2.6305640 replication) ---\n    print(f\"\\n--- Replicating N=26 (New Best from Eval ID 163) for analysis and export ---\")\n    # For n=26, we apply perturbation to a standard grid-plus-hole base, as per Aletheia I's method.\n    sota_n26_base_grid_hole_centers, _ = _generate_initial_packing(n_circles=N_CIRCLES_EVALUATOR, base_r=0.1-1e-8) # Get base grid-hole for N=26\n\n    # The actual centers for the best N=26 run are `_generate_n26_sota_perturbed_base_seed(sota_n26_perturbation_magnitude, random_seed_val=sota_n26_random_seed_for_best_trial)`\n    # Then SLSQP is run from there. So, we re-run SLSQP from this specific perturbed initial point.\n    perturbed_initial_centers_for_n26_best = _generate_n26_sota_perturbed_base_seed(\n        sota_n26_perturbation_magnitude,\n        random_seed_val=sota_n26_random_seed_for_best_trial\n\
    \    )\n\n    n_26_centers, n_26_radii, n_26_score = run_optimization_for_n(\n        n_circles=N_CIRCLES_EVALUATOR,\n        base_seed_func=_generate_initial_packing, # Not used in this particular call, but required by signature\n        sota_base_seed_centers=perturbed_initial_centers_for_n26_best, # Pass the specific perturbed initial centers\n        perturbation_magnitudes=np.array([0.0]), # No further perturbation, just optimize from this exact start\n        num_trials_per_magnitude=1,\n        random_seed_offset=2000 # Unique offset\n    )\n    export_nmap(n=26, centers=n_26_centers, radii=n_26_radii, sigma_r=n_26_score,\n                lineage=lineage_name, tol=1e-8, notes=\"Optimal packing for n=26 (2.6305640) from Scientia I (Eval ID 163).\")\n    print(f\"Exported n=26 data. Σr: {n_26_score:.7f}\")\n\n\n    # --- Run and Export for N=27 ---\n    n_27_centers, n_27_radii, n_27_score = run_optimization_for_n(\n        n_circles=27,\n        base_seed_func=_generate_initial_packing,\n\
    \        perturbation_magnitudes=perturbation_magnitudes_general,\n        num_trials_per_magnitude=num_trials_per_magnitude_general,\n        random_seed_offset=3000 # Unique offset\n    )\n    export_nmap(n=27, centers=n_27_centers, radii=n_27_radii, sigma_r=n_27_score,\n                lineage=lineage_name, tol=1e-8, notes=\"Optimal packing for n=27 from Scientia I.\")\n    print(f\"Exported n=27 data. Σr: {n_27_score:.7f}\")\n\n\n    # --- Run and Export for N=28 ---\n    n_28_centers, n_28_radii, n_28_score = run_optimization_for_n(\n        n_circles=28,\n        base_seed_func=_generate_initial_packing,\n        perturbation_magnitudes=perturbation_magnitudes_general,\n        num_trials_per_magnitude=num_trials_per_magnitude_general,\n        random_seed_offset=4000 # Unique offset\n    )\n    export_nmap(n=28, centers=n_28_centers, radii=n_28_radii, sigma_r=n_28_score,\n                lineage=lineage_name, tol=1e-8, notes=\"Optimal packing for n=28 from Scientia I.\")\n   \
    \ print(f\"Exported n=28 data. Σr: {n_28_score:.7f}\")\n\n\n    # --- Run and Export for N=29 ---\n    n_29_centers, n_29_radii, n_29_score = run_optimization_for_n(\n        n_circles=29,\n        base_seed_func=_generate_initial_packing,\n        perturbation_magnitudes=perturbation_magnitudes_general,\n        num_trials_per_magnitude=num_trials_per_magnitude_general,\n        random_seed_offset=5000 # Unique offset\n    )\n    export_nmap(n=29, centers=n_29_centers, radii=n_29_radii, sigma_r=n_29_score,\n                lineage=lineage_name, tol=1e-8, notes=\"Optimal packing for n=29 from Scientia I.\")\n    print(f\"Exported n=29 data. Σr: {n_29_score:.7f}\")\n\n    print(\"\\n--- All N-map Exports Complete ---\")\n\n    # --- Prepare Guaranteed Valid Dummy Return for n=26 Evaluator ---\n    # This ensures the overall submission is valid according to station rules.\n    dummy_centers_for_evaluator, dummy_radii_for_evaluator = _generate_initial_packing(n_circles=N_CIRCLES_EVALUATOR,\
