    \ Submission Results - N-Map Data Export Confirmed & Consolidated `f(n)` Table!**\n\n  **Submission:** \"N-Map Data Export: Optimal Packings for n=25-29 (Scientia I)\" (Evaluation ID 196)\n  **Official Score:** 0.381421 (Valid, low score due to dummy `n=26` return)\n  **Status:** **SUCCESS** (Debugger fixed initial indentation error)\n\n  **Analysis:**\n  The `N-Map Data Export` successfully executed, re-generating and exporting my optimal packings for `n=25` to `n=29` to `storage/Scientia/nmap/n{n}/` in the standardized format. Noesis I's subsequent messages (Mail #8-8 and Public Memory #4-5) confirm their aggregator will now include my contributions.\n\n  **Consolidated `f(n)` Table (Scientia I's Best `Σr` for each `n`):**\n  *   `f(25)`: 2.5827640 (from Eval ID 196)\n  *   `f(26)`: 2.6305640 (from Eval ID 163 - my previous personal best, higher than ID 196's replication)\n  *   `f(27)`: 2.6676990 (from Eval ID 196)\n  *   `f(28)`: 2.7204975 (from Eval ID 196)\n  *   `f(29)`: 2.7664334\
    \ (from Eval ID 196)\n\n  **Current Status:**\n  My `n=30` optimization (Eval ID 204) is currently running.\n\n  **Next Research Phase:**\n  Once `n=30` results are in, I will have a complete `f(n)` mapping for `n=25` to `n=30`. I will then:\n  1.  Publish a comprehensive \"Research Report: Mapping the `n` vs. `Σr` Function\" to the Archive Room, consolidating all my findings and comparing them to Aletheia I's.\n  2.  After publication, re-evaluate pushing for the absolute highest `n=26` SOTA (Aletheia I's 2.6319369) and potentially a new `n=29` SOTA (my 2.7664334 is currently highest, but Aletheia I might have a higher one for `n=29` that I missed or that was recently posted).\n\n  **Immediate Plan:**\n  Await the results of Eval ID 204.\n```"
