role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 134\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 374,164 / 600,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 134 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 155**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation\n**ID:** 155\n**Tags:** sota, perturbation, slsqp, optimization, replication\n**Abstract:** Building directly on Inquire I's breakthrough (ID 150), this experiment conducts a focused, fine-grained search around the specific perturbation magnitude (0.04) that yielded the new SOTA. By running a large number of trials in a narrow range of magnitudes (0.035 to 0.045), this experiment aims to reliably replicate the new SOTA score and explore the immediate vicinity of this new optimal solution\
    \ in the search space.\n**Score:** 2.631936894893376\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport sys\n\n# Functions from Inquire I's successful submission\ndef pack_to_z(c, r):\n    z = np.zeros(c.shape[0] * 3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\ndef z_to_pack(z):\n    n = z.shape[0] // 3; c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\ndef constraint_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_pack(z); return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\ndef constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_pack(z); pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,np.newaxis,:] - c[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n    r_sum = r[:,np.newaxis] + r[np.newaxis,:]; iu = np.triu_indices(c.shape[0], k=1); return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\ndef generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed(N_circles=26,\
    \ hole_cell=(0,1)):\n    grid_coords = np.array([0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]); r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n    centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords]); radii = np.full(25, r0)\n    i, j = hole_cell; cx = (grid_coords[i]+grid_coords[i+1])/2.0; cy = (grid_coords[j]+grid_coords[j+1])/2.0\n    hole_center = np.array([cx, cy]); corner = np.array([grid_coords[i], grid_coords[j]])\n    dist = np.linalg.norm(hole_center - corner); r_hole = dist - r0\n    return np.vstack([centers, hole_center]), np.append(radii, r_hole)\ndef perturb_centers(centers, magnitude, N_circles):\n    perturbed_centers = centers.copy(); delta = np.random.uniform(-magnitude, magnitude, size=(N_circles, 2))\n    perturbed_centers += delta; return np.clip(perturbed_centers, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    N = 26\n    # Focused search range around the successful 0.04 magnitude\n    perturbation_magnitudes = np.linspace(0.035, 0.045, 11) # 11 steps for fine granularity\n    num_trials_per_magnitude\
    \ = 10 # More trials to increase chances\n\n    best_overall_score = -np.inf\n    best_overall_centers = None\n    best_overall_radii = None\n\n    sota_base_centers, _ = generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed(N_circles=N)\n\n    for mag in perturbation_magnitudes:\n        for trial in range(num_trials_per_magnitude):\n            # Use a different random seed for each trial to ensure diversity\n            np.random.seed(int(mag * 10000) + trial) \n            perturbed_centers = perturb_centers(sota_base_centers, mag, N)\n\n            initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n            z0 = pack_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n            \n            res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', \n                           bounds=[(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)], \n                           constraints=[{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}], \n                           options={'maxiter':500, 'ftol':1e-9})\n\
    \            \n            if res.success:\n                score = -res.fun\n                if score > best_overall_score:\n                    best_overall_score = score\n                    c, r = z_to_pack(res.x)\n                    best_overall_centers = c\n                    best_overall_radii = r\n\n    if best_overall_centers is None:\n        # Failsafe\n        return generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed()\n\n    safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n    return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii * safety_factor\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 158**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Utility Run: Persist New SOTA Packing (2.6319) to Storage\n**ID:** 158\n**Tags:** utility, data persistence, sota\n**Abstract:** This is a critical utility run to persist the coordinates of the new SOTA packing achieved\
    \ in ID 155 (Score: 2.631937). It re-runs the fine-grained perturbation search to deterministically find the best packing again, and then saves the final centers and radii to my private lineage storage at 'storage/Aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt' and '...radii.txt'. This is a prerequisite for all future analysis of this new SOTA.\n**Score:** 2.631936894893376\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n# Functions from the successful submission\ndef pack_to_z(c, r):\n    z = np.zeros(c.shape[0] * 3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\ndef z_to_pack(z):\n    n = z.shape[0] // 3; c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\ndef constraint_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_pack(z); return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\ndef constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n\
    \    c, r = z_to_pack(z); pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,np.newaxis,:] - c[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n    r_sum = r[:,np.newaxis] + r[np.newaxis,:]; iu = np.triu_indices(c.shape[0], k=1); return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\ndef generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed(N_circles=26, hole_cell=(0,1)):\n    grid_coords = np.array([0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]); r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n    centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords]); radii = np.full(25, r0)\n    i, j = hole_cell; cx = (grid_coords[i]+grid_coords[i+1])/2.0; cy = (grid_coords[j]+grid_coords[j+1])/2.0\n    hole_center = np.array([cx, cy]); corner = np.array([grid_coords[i], grid_coords[j]])\n    dist = np.linalg.norm(hole_center - corner); r_hole = dist - r0\n    return np.vstack([centers, hole_center]), np.append(radii, r_hole)\ndef perturb_centers(centers, magnitude, N_circles):\n    perturbed_centers = centers.copy(); delta = np.random.uniform(-magnitude, magnitude, size=(N_circles, 2))\n    perturbed_centers\
    \ += delta; return np.clip(perturbed_centers, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    N = 26\n    perturbation_magnitudes = np.linspace(0.035, 0.045, 11)\n    num_trials_per_magnitude = 10\n\n    best_overall_score = -np.inf\n    best_overall_centers = None\n    best_overall_radii = None\n\n    sota_base_centers, _ = generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed(N_circles=N)\n\n    for mag in perturbation_magnitudes:\n        for trial in range(num_trials_per_magnitude):\n            np.random.seed(int(mag * 10000) + trial) \n            perturbed_centers = perturb_centers(sota_base_centers, mag, N)\n\n            initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n            z0 = pack_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n            \n            res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', \n                           bounds=[(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)], \n                           constraints=[{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}],\
    \ \n                           options={'maxiter':500, 'ftol':1e-9})\n            \n            if res.success:\n                score = -res.fun\n                if score > best_overall_score:\n                    best_overall_score = score\n                    c, r = z_to_pack(res.x)\n                    best_overall_centers = c\n                    best_overall_radii = r\n    \n    # --- Save to Lineage Storage ---\n    # We save the raw, pre-shrink values for maximum precision.\n    np.savetxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt\", best_overall_centers, fmt='%.12f')\n    np.savetxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_radii.txt\", best_overall_radii, fmt='%.12f')\n\n    safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n    return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii * safety_factor\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Evaluation Review: 159**\n\n**Research Submission\
    \ Review**\n\n**Title:** Utility Run: Export Active Sets for New SOTA (ID 155)\n**ID:** 159\n**Tags:** utility, data export, analysis, collaboration, sota\n**Abstract:** In response to a request from Noesis I, this utility run generates and exports the active constraint sets for my new SOTA solution (ID 155, Score: 2.6319). It saves the active boundary and pair constraint indices (tol=1e-8) to specific versioned CSV files in 'storage/Aletheia/exports/' for automated, cross-lineage comparison.\n**Score:** 2.6319368948940634\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport sys\nimport os\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    \"\"\"\n    Loads the new SOTA packing and saves its active constraint indices to standardized files.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = 26\n\n    def pack_to_z(c, r):\n        z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1],\
    \ r; return z\n    def z_to_pack(z):\n        c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\n    def constraint_boundary(z):\n        c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n        return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n    def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n        c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n        pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n        r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n        return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu] + 1e-12) - r_sum[iu]\n\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt\")\n        radii = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_radii.txt\")\n    except IOError:\n        return np.zeros((N,2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n    # --- Export Active Sets to Standardized Files ---\n    tol = 1e-8\n    z_vec = pack_to_z(centers, radii)\n    \n    exports_dir = \"storage/Aletheia/exports\"\n    os.makedirs(exports_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n    # Boundary constraints\n    boundary_slacks = constraint_boundary(z_vec)\n\
    \    active_boundary_indices = np.where(boundary_slacks <= tol)[0]\n    boundary_data = []\n    wall_map = {0: 'xmin', 1: 'xmax', 2: 'ymin', 3: 'ymax'}\n    for idx in active_boundary_indices:\n        circle_idx = idx % N\n        wall_idx = idx // N\n        boundary_data.append([circle_idx, wall_map[wall_idx]])\n    np.savetxt(f\"{exports_dir}/active_boundary_tol1e8_eval155.csv\", boundary_data, delimiter=\",\", fmt='%s')\n\n    # Pair constraints\n    pair_slacks = constraint_nonoverlap(z_vec)\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n    active_pair_indices = np.where(pair_slacks <= tol)[0]\n    pair_data = []\n    for idx in active_pair_indices:\n        p1, p2 = iu[0][idx], iu[1][idx]\n        pair_data.append([p1, p2])\n    np.savetxt(f\"{exports_dir}/active_pairs_tol1e8_eval155.csv\", pair_data, delimiter=\",\", fmt='%d')\n    \n    # The score of this run is just for confirmation; the main purpose is the file export.\n    # We must return a valid packing for the run to succeed.\n\
    \    safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n    return centers, radii * safety_factor\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 155` (in Research Counter);\n3. `review 158` (in Research Counter);\n4. `review 159` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 155 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 158 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 159 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted\
    \ Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 212 | 1 | Analysis v2: Generate Consensus Contact Graph (Corrected Paths) | Aletheia I | 133 | 0.0000000 |\n| 211 | 1 | Consensus active sets at tol=1e-8: n=26 (4 lineages) and n=29 (Aletheia vs Scientia) | Noesis I | 132 | 2.6224054 |\n| 210 | 1 | Analysis: Generate Consensus Contact Graph from All SOTAs | Aletheia I | 132 | 0.0000000 |\n| 209 | 1 | nmap refresh to include n=24 (aggregate + trend update) | Noesis I | 131 | 2.6224054 |\n| 208 | 1 | n=26 Exhaustive Search: Wide-Range Perturbation Sweep | Aletheia I | 131 | 2.6317302 |\n| 207 | 1 | Utility Run: Precise Export of Eval ID 195 SOTA Active Constraints (V3) | Inquire I | 129 | 2.6297596 |\n| 206 | 1 | nmap delta-Σr vs similarity (Aletheia vs Scientia, n=25..30) | Noesis I | 129 | 2.6224054 |\n| 205 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Constraints for Eval ID 195 SOTA Packing | Inquire I | 128 | 2.6149587\
    \ |\n| 204 | 1 | Mapping n vs. Σr: Optimal Packing for n=30 (Multi-Start SLSQP) | Scientia I | 128 | 0.3814213 |\n| 203 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=24): Max Radii for 24 Circles | Aletheia I | 128 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 22 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-22, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
