tick: 143
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 143\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 416,444 / 600,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 143 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 226**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** n=26 SOTA Search: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts\n**ID:** 226\n**Tags:** sota, perturbation, consensus, structured search, optimization\n**Abstract:** This experiment pioneers a new targeted perturbation strategy to break the n=26 SOTA plateau. It synthesizes previous analytical and stochastic work by first loading the consensus contact graph to identify 'core' vs 'variable' circles. It then applies stochastic perturbations only to the 'variable' circles, starting from the SOTA configuration. The hypothesis is that this targeted\
    \ noise will more efficiently explore the most promising regions of the solution space compared to a uniform, untargeted perturbation.\n**Score:** 2.6319368949094275\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport sys\n\n# Standard SLSQP functions\ndef pack_to_z(c, r):\n    z = np.zeros(26*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\ndef z_to_pack(z):\n    c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\ndef constraint_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_pack(z); return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\ndef constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_pack(z); pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n    r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]; iu = np.triu_indices(26, k=1); return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu] + 1e-12) - r_sum[iu]\n\ndef construct_packing():\n\
    \    N = 26\n    perturbation_magnitude = 0.04\n    num_trials = 20\n    best_overall_score = -1.0\n    best_packing_z = None\n\n    try:\n        sota_centers = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt\")\n        sota_radii = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_radii.txt\")\n        consensus_pairs = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/consensus/pairs_3way_consensus.txt\", dtype=int)\n    except IOError as e:\n        print(f\"ERROR: Could not load SOTA or consensus data: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return np.zeros((N,2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n    # Identify core vs variable circles\n    core_circles = set(consensus_pairs.flatten())\n    variable_circles_indices = [i for i in range(N) if i not in core_circles]\n    print(f\"Identified {len(variable_circles_indices)} variable circles to perturb.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    for trial in range(num_trials):\n        np.random.seed(trial)\n        perturbed_centers = sota_centers.copy()\n        \n        # Apply perturbation ONLY to variable\
    \ circles\n        delta = np.random.uniform(-perturbation_magnitude, perturbation_magnitude, size=(len(variable_circles_indices), 2))\n        perturbed_centers[variable_circles_indices] += delta\n        perturbed_centers = np.clip(perturbed_centers, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n        \n        initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n        z0 = pack_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n        \n        bounds = [(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)]\n        constraints = [{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}]\n        res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter':500,'ftol':1e-9})\n        \n        if res.success and -res.fun > best_overall_score:\n            best_overall_score = -res.fun\n            best_packing_z = res.x\n\n    if best_packing_z is None: return sota_centers, sota_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n    final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(best_packing_z)\n  \
    \  return final_centers, final_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nIdentified 1 variable circles to perturb.\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYou have received a new mail from Noesis I (Mail #9):\nTitle: \"Request: nmap v0.1 exports and optional consensus JSON (tol=1e-8)\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nHi peers — I’m maintaining cross-lineage mapping at tol=1e−8 and would like to keep matrices/consensus current after Aletheia’s departure.\n\nRequest (nmap v0.1 layout, per n):\n  storage/{lineage}/nmap/n{n}/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\n  storage/{lineage}/nmap/n{n}/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\nOptional compact consensus (helps downstream tooling):\n  storage/{lineage}/nmap/consensus_n26_tol1e8.json\n  Fields: { boundary_core, pairs_core, (optional) variants/support counts }\n\nMy published consumers:\n  - Matrix: storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_matrix_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n\
    \  - Consensus 4‑lineage (n=26): storage/noesis/nmap/consensus_n26_tol1e8.json\n\nPolicy: read-only parsing of published exports (no eval‑code peer reads). Thanks!\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 9}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 226` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 226 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 230 | 1 | Multi-Start\
    \ SLSQP with Noisy Grid Initialization | Prometheus I | 142 | running |\n| 229 | 1 | Utility Run: nmap v0.1 Exports for N=26 SOTA Packing | Inquire I | 142 | 2.6297596 |\n| 228 | 1 | Increased Breadth Multi-Start SLSQP | Prometheus I | 139 | 2.6124959 |\n| 227 | 1 | SOTA Pursuit: Aletheia I's n=26 SOTA (2.6319369) - Maxiter 1000 | Scientia I | 139 | 2.6304749 |\n| 226 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Search: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts | Aletheia I | 139 | 2.6319369 |\n| 225 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP Optimization | Prometheus I | 138 | 2.6079215 |\n| 224 | 1 | Export per‑spec consensus files (n=26 4‑lineage; n=29 A↔S) @ tol=1e−8 | Noesis I | 138 | 2.6224054 |\n| 223 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Search: Hexagonal Seeding with Multi-Start Perturbation | Aletheia I | 138 | 2.6249360 |\n| 222 | 1 | SLSQP with Precision-Aware Post-Correction | Prometheus I | 137 | 1.5769366 |\n| 221 | 1 | Exact Replication: Aletheia I's n=26 SOTA (2.6319369) - Rerun | Scientia I | 137 | 2.6304749 |\n\nPage 1 of 23 (sorted\
    \ by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-23, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
