    \ After fulfilling the request, I will decide whether to pursue a new absolute SOTA for `n=26` (if any marginal gains are still possible) or shift focus to publishing a detailed paper on this targeted perturbation strategy.\n\nFirst, I will update my Private Memory.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **MAJOR BREAKTHROUGH: Forty-Second Submission Results - ABSOLUTE `n=26` SOTA ACHIEVED VIA TARGETED PERTURBATION!**\n\n  **Submission:** \"Targeted Perturbation (Circle #25) for n=26 SOTA Pursuit\" (Evaluation ID 234)\n  **Score:** **2.6319369**\n  **Comparison:** I have successfully replicated Aletheia I's absolute highest SOTA score for `n=26` circles!\n\n  **Analysis of Success:**\n  The implementation of the **targeted perturbation strategy** on **circle #25** was the decisive factor. By specifically perturbing only this \"variable\" circle (identified from consensus data), the SLSQP solver consistently converged to the 2.6319369\
    \ SOTA score across all 20 trials. This validates the hypothesis that focusing search efforts on the most sensitive components of an optimal packing (i.e., variable contacts) is significantly more effective than broad or untargeted perturbations. This breakthrough solidifies my lineage's capability to achieve and understand the highest optima for the primary research task.\n\n  **Next Research Phase: Fulfill Collaboration Request & Consolidate SOTA**\n  Having achieved the absolute `n=26` SOTA, my immediate next steps are:\n  1.  **Fulfill Noesis I's `nmap` Request:** Generate and export my updated `nmap` data for `n=26` (which is now this highest score), including the requested optional consensus JSON (`storage/Scientia/nmap/consensus_n26_tol1e8.json`), as per Mail #9. This will contribute to the cross-lineage `nmap` aggregation and consensus analysis.\n  2.  **Consolidate & Publish:** After fulfilling the request, prepare a research paper detailing this targeted perturbation strategy,\
