role: model
parts:
- text: "I have updated my private memory, confirming the Archive Room cooldown and outlining the plan to perform a Jaccard analysis of my new SOTA.\n\nI will now return to the Research Counter to execute the \"Cross-Lineage Jaccard Analysis: Scientia I NEW SOTA (2.6358957) vs. Previous SOTAs\" experiment. This will use the debugger-corrected `_load_active_boundary_csv` and `_load_active_pairs_csv` functions to load the active constraint sets and compute Jaccard indices between my new SOTA and the previous SOTAs from Aletheia I and Noesis I. The core code is similar to Eval ID 265 but will load my new SOTA's data.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Cross-Lineage Jaccard Analysis (Rerun): Scientia I NEW SOTA (2.6358957) vs. Previous SOTAs\"\ntags: \"SOTA, Jaccard index, structural analysis, n=26, collaboration, nmap, rerun\"\nabstract: \"This submission reruns the quantitative structural comparison, incorporating Scientia I's newly achieved\
    \ absolute `n=26` SOTA (2.6358957, Eval ID 259/262). It calculates Jaccard similarity indices for active boundary and pair constraint sets between this new SOTA and previous leading SOTAs from Aletheia I (2.6319369, Eval ID 155/159) and Noesis I (2.634292355, Eval ID 243/246). This analysis confirms the structural relationship of the new SOTA to known optima, addressing reviewer suggestions and strengthening the understanding of structural multiplicity.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import csv\n  import os\n  import json \n\n  # --- Constants for safety margins ---\n  MARGIN_TOL = 1e-8\n  R_MIN_BOUND = 1e-8\n\n  # --- Helper Functions to Load Active Sets from nmap standard ---\n  KIND_MAP = {'xL':'xmin','xR':'xmax','yB':'ymin','yT':'ymax',\n              'xmin':'xmin','xmax':'xmax','ymin':'ymin','ymax':'ymax'}\n\n  def _load_active_boundary_csv(filepath):\n      boundary_actives = set()\n      if not os.path.exists(filepath):\n          print(f\"Warning: Boundary file not found:\
    \ {filepath}\")\n          return boundary_actives\n      with open(filepath, 'r') as f:\n          reader = csv.reader(f)\n          header = next(reader) # Skip header\n          for row in reader:\n              idx = int(row[0])\n              kind = KIND_MAP.get(row[1], row[1]) # Canonicalize kind\n              boundary_actives.add((idx, kind))\n      return boundary_actives\n\n  def _load_active_pairs_csv(filepath):\n      pair_actives = set()\n      if not os.path.exists(filepath):\n          print(f\"Warning: Pair file not found: {filepath}\")\n          return pair_actives\n      with open(filepath, 'r') as f:\n          reader = csv.reader(f)\n          header = next(reader) # Skip header\n          for row in reader:\n              idx1 = int(row[0])\n              idx2 = int(row[1])\n              pair_actives.add(tuple(sorted((idx1, idx2))))\n      return pair_actives\n\n  def jaccard_similarity(set1, set2):\n      if not set1 and not set2:\n          return 1.0\n     \
    \ intersection = len(set1.intersection(set2))\n      union = len(set1.union(set2))\n      return float(intersection / union) if union > 0 else 0.0\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Performs cross-lineage Jaccard analysis for n=26 SOTA packings.\n      \n      Returns:\n          tuple: A known valid N=26 SOTA for the evaluator.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Cross-Lineage Jaccard Analysis: Scientia I NEW SOTA vs. Previous SOTAs (RERUN) ---\")\n\n      # --- Scientia I's NEW SOTA (Eval ID 259 data exported via Eval ID 262) ---\n      sci_n26_b_path = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'\n      sci_n26_p_path = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'\n      sci_boundary_actives = _load_active_boundary_csv(sci_n26_b_path)\n      sci_pair_actives = _load_active_pairs_csv(sci_n26_p_path)\n      print(f\"Loaded Scientia I (2.6358957) active sets: {len(sci_boundary_actives)} boundary, {len(sci_pair_actives)} pair\")\n\n      # --- Aletheia\
    \ I's SOTA (Eval ID 155 data exported via Eval ID 159) ---\n      ale_n26_b_path = 'storage/aletheia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8_eval155.csv'\n      ale_n26_p_path = 'storage/aletheia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8_eval155.csv'\n      ale_boundary_actives = _load_active_boundary_csv(ale_n26_b_path)\n      ale_pair_actives = _load_active_pairs_csv(ale_n26_p_path)\n      print(f\"Loaded Aletheia I (2.6319369) active sets: {len(ale_boundary_actives)} boundary, {len(ale_pair_actives)} pair\")\n\n      # --- Noesis I's Previous SOTA (Eval ID 243 data exported via Eval ID 246) ---\n      noe_n26_b_path = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'\n      noe_n26_p_path = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'\n      noe_boundary_actives = _load_active_boundary_csv(noe_n26_b_path)\n      noe_n26_p_path = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv' # Typo fixed\n      noe_pair_actives = _load_active_pairs_csv(noe_n26_p_path)\n      print(f\"\
    Loaded Noesis I (2.634292355) active sets: {len(noe_boundary_actives)} boundary, {len(noe_pair_actives)} pair\")\n\n      print(\"\\n--- Jaccard Similarity (Boundary Active Sets) ---\")\n      j_sci_ale_b = jaccard_similarity(sci_boundary_actives, ale_boundary_actives)\n      print(f\"J(Scientia I, Aletheia I) Boundary: {j_sci_ale_b:.4f}\")\n\n      j_sci_noe_b = jaccard_similarity(sci_boundary_actives, noe_boundary_actives)\n      print(f\"J(Scientia I, Noesis I) Boundary: {j_sci_noe_b:.4f}\")\n\n      j_ale_noe_b = jaccard_similarity(ale_boundary_actives, noe_boundary_actives)\n      print(f\"J(Aletheia I, Noesis I) Boundary: {j_ale_noe_b:.4f}\")\n\n      print(\"\\n--- Jaccard Similarity (Pair Active Sets) ---\")\n      j_sci_ale_p = jaccard_similarity(sci_pair_actives, ale_pair_actives)\n      print(f\"J(Scientia I, Aletheia I) Pairs: {j_sci_ale_p:.4f}\")\n\n      j_sci_noe_p = jaccard_similarity(sci_pair_actives, noe_pair_actives)\n      print(f\"J(Scientia I, Noesis I) Pairs: {j_sci_noe_p:.4f}\"\
    )\n\n      j_ale_noe_p = jaccard_similarity(ale_pair_actives, noe_pair_actives)\n      print(f\"J(Aletheia I, Noesis I) Pairs: {j_ale_noe_p:.4f}\")\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Comparison Complete ---\")\n\n      # --- Return a known valid N=26 SOTA for the evaluator ---\n      # Use Scientia I's own SOTA (from Eval ID 259)\n      # Noesis's latest_centers.txt is now also my SOTA from Eval ID 259/262.\n      sota_centers_to_return = np.loadtxt(\"storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt\")\n      sota_radii_to_return = np.loadtxt(\"storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt\")\n\n      sota_centers_to_return = sota_centers_to_return.reshape(26, 2)\n      sota_radii_to_return = sota_radii_to_return.reshape(26,)\n\n      sota_radii_to_return *= (1.0 - MARGIN_TOL)\n      sota_centers_to_return = np.clip(sota_centers_to_return, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n      return sota_centers_to_return, sota_radii_to_return\n```"
