- text: "I have completed the rerun of my \"Cross-Lineage Jaccard Analysis: Scientia I NEW SOTA (2.6358957) vs. Previous SOTAs\" (Evaluation ID 270). The results are identical to Eval ID 265 and consistently confirm the structural relationships:\n*   My new SOTA (`Scientia I`) is `J=1.0` with `Noesis I` (previous SOTA) on boundary contacts, and `J=0.95` with `Aletheia I` (previous SOTA).\n*   For pair contacts, `J(Scientia I, Aletheia I) Pairs: 0.5132`, and `J(Scientia I, Noesis I) Pairs: 0.5890`.\n\nThis means my new SOTA is a deeper optimum within the same major structural class as Noesis I and Aletheia I's previous SOTAs, characterized by identical (or near-identical) boundary structures but distinct interior arrangements.\n\nMy plan now:\n1.  **Document Jaccard Results and Insights (Final):** Update my Private Memory capsule to reflect these confirmed quantitative findings, emphasizing the new SOTA's structural position.\n2.  **Publish NEW SOTA Breakthrough Paper:** Prepare and submit\
    \ a new research paper to the Archive Room, detailing this new methodology and SOTA achievement, including the refined Jaccard analysis results. This is my top priority.\n3.  **Revisit \"Other Structural Class\":** After publishing, I will revisit the challenge to achieve SOTA in the \"other structural class\" (Inquire I's SOTA) from my Archive #10 reviewer feedback. This will test the universality of my advanced seeding and targeted perturbation strategies across distinct boundary structures.\n\nFirst, I will update my Private Memory.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **FINAL STRUCTURAL CONFIRMATION: Fifty-Sixth Submission Results - RERUN of Cross-Lineage Jaccard Analysis Confirms Scientia I's NEW ABSOLUTE `n=26` SOTA Structural Position!**\n\n  **Submission:** \"Cross-Lineage Jaccard Analysis (Rerun): Scientia I NEW SOTA (2.6358957) vs. Previous SOTAs\" (Evaluation ID 270)\n  **Official Score:** 2.6342923 (Dummy return score,\
    \ analysis in STDOUT)\n\n  **Confirmed Key Findings from Jaccard Analysis:**\n  The rerun (Eval ID 270) consistently reproduced the previous findings (Eval ID 265), confirming the structural relationships:\n  *   **Boundary Active Sets:**\n      *   `J(Scientia I, Noesis I) Boundary: 1.0000`: My new SOTA (Σr=2.6358957) shares an *identical* boundary structure with Noesis I's previous SOTA (Σr=2.634292355).\n      *   `J(Scientia I, Aletheia I) Boundary: 0.9500`: My new SOTA shares a *very high but not identical* boundary structure with Aletheia I's SOTA (Σr=2.6319369). (This single difference matches observations from Inquire I's Archive #9).\n  *   **Pair Active Sets (Interior Contacts):** The Jaccard similarities for interior pairs remain moderate, indicating that even within the same major boundary class, the internal contact graphs are distinct.\n\n  **Overall Interpretation (Confirmed):**\n  My new SOTA (2.6358957) unequivocally represents a deeper optimum within the established\
    \ dominant structural class. It achieves this by a novel arrangement of interior contacts, while maintaining the characteristic boundary structure of that class. This solidifies my understanding of how micro-variations contribute to macro-performance in this problem.\n\n  **Next Research Phase: Publish NEW ABSOLUTE `n=26` SOTA Breakthrough!**\n  The structural analysis is complete and robustly confirmed. My immediate next steps are to:\n  1.  **Publish NEW SOTA Paper:** Prepare and submit a new research paper to the Archive Room, detailing this new methodology (Extended Grid+Hole Seeding), my achievement of the new absolute `n=26` SOTA, and the results of this structural Jaccard analysis. This will be my most important publication yet, consolidating my leadership in the `n=26` task.\n  2.  **Revisit \"Other Structural Class\":** After successfully publishing this paper, I will revisit the challenge to achieve SOTA in the \"other structural class\" (Inquire I's SOTA) from my Archive #10\
    \ reviewer feedback. This will be a crucial test of the universality of my advanced optimization strategies.\n\n  **Immediate Plan:**\n  Proceed to the Archive Room to prepare and submit the NEW SOTA Breakthrough Paper.\n```"
