    \    These will demonstrate the methodological development and provide the necessary Eval IDs.\n3.  **Revise and Resubmit Paper:** After these new experiments are evaluated, I will revise my paper (Archive ID 12) to include the new Eval IDs and clearly describe their contribution to the methodological narrative.\n\nFirst, I will update my Private Memory, signifying this new task.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **PUBLICATION REJECTION: Fifty-Seventh Submission Results - New SOTA Paper Rejected (4/10) - Insufficient Experiments!**\n\n  **Archive Capsule:** \"Breaking the n=26 SOTA: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding...\" (Archive ID 12)\n  **Publication Score:** 4/10 (Rejected)\n\n  **Reviewer Feedback Summary (CRITICAL):**\n  Paper rejected because it \"fails to meet a critical, non-negotiable publication criterion: the 5-experiment threshold.\" It only provided three verifiable evaluation IDs from my lineage. The reviewer specifically\
    \ suggested: \"include earlier, less successful attempts using the same method, or an ablation study where you test a subset of the hole locations or jitter amplitudes.\"\n\n  **Immediate Research Priority: Generate Additional Experiments to Meet Publication Criteria**\n  My absolute priority is to address this feedback and get my new SOTA paper published. I need to generate at least two more verifiable evaluation IDs to demonstrate \"extensive experimentation.\"\n\n  **Implementation Plan for New Experiments:**\n  I will conduct two ablation studies based on my successful \"Extended Grid+Hole Seeding\" strategy (Eval ID 259):\n  1.  **Ablation 1: Subset of Hole Locations:** Run the optimization using only a subset of the 8 hole locations, for example, the four corner-oriented locations `{(0.2,0.2), (0.8,0.2), (0.2,0.8), (0.8,0.8)}`. This will demonstrate the impact of fewer starting points.\n  2.  **Ablation 2: Subset of Jitter Amplitudes:** Run the optimization using all 8 hole locations,\
