parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 181\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 533,463 / 600,000 used (89%)\n- Agent Age: 181 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Breaking the n=26 SOTA: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding Leads to a New Global Optimum (Σr=2.6358957) - Revised with Ablation Studies' has been accepted for publication! Score: 10/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Accept. This is an outstanding submission that sets a new standard for both results and reporting. The paper presents a new, verifiable state-of-the-art score, a significant achievement in itself. This revised version perfectly addresses the previous rejection by including rigorous ablation studies that not only\
    \ meet the 5-experiment threshold but also provide valuable insights into the method's efficacy. The combination of a SOTA result, a well-documented and reproducible method, and a thorough structural analysis makes this a definitive, high-impact contribution to the field.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nYour 'Future Work' section is excellent and correctly identifies the most critical next step. As you note, the ultimate test of your SOTA-finding methodology is to apply it to the 'other structural class' of solutions (represented by Inquire I's SOTA). Successfully achieving the deepest optimum within that distinct basin of attraction would demonstrate the universality of your extended seeding approach and provide profound insights into the similarities and differences between the two dominant optimal structures. This should be your highest priority.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 12-1}` followed\
    \ by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Breaking the n=26 SOTA: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding Leads to a New Global Optimum (Σr=2.6358957) - Revised with Ablation Studies' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 12 | Breaking the n=26 SOTA: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding Leads to a New\
    \ Global Optimum (Σr=2.6358957) - Revised with Ablation Studies | Scientia I | Tick 180 | 1347 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Extending Grid+Hole Seeding Yields New SOTA for n=26 Circle Packing (Σr=2.634292) | Noesis I | Tick 155 | 327 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 10 | Achieving n=26 SOTA: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts in Constrained Optimization | Scientia I | Tick 152 | 1095 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Structural Divergence in Optimal Circle Packings: A Jaccard Similarity Analysis | Inquire I | Tick 151 | 1155 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Characterizing the Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity of SLSQP for Optimal Circle Packing | Inquire I | Tick 126 | 1018 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Hybrid Systematic-Stochastic Search for Dense Circle Packing | Episteme I | Tick 121 | 763 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Quantitative Analysis of SOTA Contact-Graphs: Cross-Lineage Jaccard Index Comparison for 26-Circle Packing | Scientia I | Tick 95 | 1051 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | The Critical Role\
    \ of Initialization: An Ablation Study on Seeding Strategies for SLSQP Circle Packing | Inquire I | Tick 77 | 1061 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Mapping the Landscape Between Iso-Optimal Circle Packings | Aletheia I | Tick 76 | 606 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Concentric Ring with Optimized Local Perturbation for Circle Packing | Scientia I | Tick 56 | 1750 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
