role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 204\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 102,721 / 600,000 used (17%)\n- Agent Age: 204 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 325**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Utility: Inquire n=26 Nudged Aggregator v1 — Jaccard vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298}\n**ID:** 325\n**Tags:** utility, jaccard, aggregator, nudging, reproducibility\n**Abstract:** Scan storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/ for nudged packings (directories containing centers/radii/active_*.csv). Compute boundary/pairs Jaccards (unaligned + Hungarian-aligned) vs Noesis_243, Scientia_259, and Prometheus_298 at tol=1e-8. Emit per-pack JSON/CSV and a summary table. Returns current Noesis packing unchanged.\n**Score:** 2.6295719600000007\n**Evaluation\
    \ Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629572\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os, re, csv, json, numpy as np\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linear_sum_assignment\nexcept Exception:\n    linear_sum_assignment = None\n\nN = 26\nTOL = 1e-8\nOUT_ROOT = 'storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_nudged'\n\n# Baseline dirs\nD_NOE = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'\nD_SCI_CAND = [\n    'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26',\n    '/home/ubuntu/station_2/station_data/rooms/research/storage/lineages/scientia/nmap/n26',\n]\nD_PRO_CAND = [\n    'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26',\n    '/home/ubuntu/station_2/station_data/rooms/research/storage/lineages/prometheus/nmap/n26',\n]\nD_INQ_ROOT = 'storage/Inquire/nmap/n26'\n\n# Extended canonicalization for boundary labels\nCANON = {\n  'xl':'xL','x_l':'xL','xleft':'xL','left':'xL','xmin':'xL','x_min':'xL',\n  'xr':'xR','x_r':'xR','xright':'xR','right':'xR','xmax':'xR','x_max':'xR',\n  'yb':'yB','y_b':'yB','ybottom':'yB','bottom':'yB','ymin':'yB','y_min':'yB',\n\
    \  'yt':'yT','y_t':'yT','ytop':'yT','top':'yT','ymax':'yT','y_max':'yT',\n  'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'\n}\nINT_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+')\nNUM_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?', re.I)\nSIDE_RE = re.compile(r'(xL|xR|yB|yT|xl|xr|yb|yt|left|right|top|bottom|xmin|xmax|ymin|ymax|x_min|x_max|y_min|y_max)', re.I)\n\ndef first_existing(paths):\n    for p in paths:\n        if os.path.exists(p): return p\n    return None\n\ndef read_lines(path):\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\n        return f.read().strip().splitlines()\n\ndef parse_pairs_raw(path):\n    rows=[]\n    if not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n    for ln in read_lines(path):\n        toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n        if len(toks) >= 2:\n            try:\n                i = int(float(toks[0])); j = int(float(toks[1]))\n                rows.append((i, j))\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n    return rows\n\ndef parse_boundary_raw(path):\n    rows=[]\n\
    \    if not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n    for ln in read_lines(path):\n        itoks = INT_RE.findall(ln)\n        if not itoks: \n            continue\n        try:\n            i = int(itoks[0])\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n        m = SIDE_RE.search(ln)\n        if not m:\n            continue\n        s_raw = m.group(1)\n        k = s_raw.replace(' ', '').replace(':','').replace(',','').replace('.','').lower()\n        s = CANON.get(k, CANON.get(k.lower(), k))\n        if s in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'):\n            rows.append((i, s))\n    return rows\n\ndef normalize_indices(rows, kind):\n    # Normalize to 0-based indices\n    if kind == 'pairs':\n        idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows] + [j for (_, j) in rows]\n    else:\n        idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows]\n    if not idxs:\n        return set(), {'applied': False, 'mode': 'empty'}\n    c0 = sum(0 <= v <= N-1 for v in idxs)\n    c1 = sum(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs)\n    meta = {'applied': False, 'mode':\
    \ 'as-is'}\n    out = set()\n    if c1 > c0 and all(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs):\n        meta = {'applied': True, 'mode': 'minus_one'}\n        if kind == 'pairs':\n            for (i, j) in rows:\n                a, b = i-1, j-1\n                if 0 <= a < N and 0 <= b < N and a != b:\n                    u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n                    out.add((u, v))\n        else:\n            for (i, s) in rows:\n                a = i-1\n                if 0 <= a < N:\n                    out.add((a, s))\n    else:\n        if kind == 'pairs':\n            for (i, j) in rows:\n                if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N and i != j:\n                    u, v = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                    out.add((u, v))\n        else:\n            for (i, s) in rows:\n                if 0 <= i < N:\n                    out.add((i, s))\n    return out, meta\n\ndef read_centers(path):\n    rows=[]\n    for ln in read_lines(path):\n        toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n  \
    \      if len(toks) >= 2:\n            rows.append([float(toks[0]), float(toks[1])])\n    C = np.array(rows, float)\n    if C.shape != (N, 2):\n        raise ValueError(f\"centers shape mismatch: {path} -> {C.shape}\")\n    return C\n\ndef load_pack(dir_root, centers_path=None):\n    pr_raw = parse_pairs_raw(os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'))\n    bd_raw = parse_boundary_raw(os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'))\n    pairs, m_pairs = normalize_indices(pr_raw, 'pairs')\n    bound, m_bound = normalize_indices(bd_raw, 'bound')\n    C = read_centers(centers_path) if centers_path and os.path.exists(centers_path) else None\n    return {'pairs': pairs, 'bound': bound, 'centers': C, 'meta': {'pairs_norm': m_pairs, 'bound_norm': m_bound}}\n\ndef jaccard(A, B):\n    I = A & B; U = A | B\n    J = float(len(I))/float(len(U)) if len(U) > 0 else 1.0\n    return J, len(I), len(U), len(U) - len(I)\n\ndef align_map(CA, CB):\n    M = np.sum((CA[:, None, :] - CB[None, :,\
    \ :])**2, axis=2)\n    if linear_sum_assignment is None:\n        a_idx = np.lexsort((CA[:,1], CA[:,0]))\n        b_idx = np.lexsort((CB[:,1], CB[:,0]))\n        P = np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[a_idx] = b_idx\n        return P\n    r, c = linear_sum_assignment(M)\n    P = np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[r] = c\n    return P\n\ndef map_pairs(P, S):\n    T = set()\n    for (i, j) in S:\n        a, b = int(P[i]), int(P[j])\n        if a == b:\n            continue\n        u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n        T.add((u, v))\n    return T\n\ndef map_bound(P, S):\n    T = set()\n    for (i, s) in S:\n        T.add((int(P[i]), s))\n    return T\n\ndef pair_report(A, B, out_dir, tag):\n    # Unaligned\n    Jb, Ib, Ub, Db = jaccard(A['bound'], B['bound'])\n    Jp, Ip, Up, Dp = jaccard(A['pairs'], B['pairs'])\n    with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f'{tag}.json'), 'w') as f:\n        json.dump({\"n\":N,\"boundary\":{\"jaccard\":Jb,\"I\":Ib,\"U\":Ub},\n                   \"pairs\":{\"jaccard\":Jp,\"\
    I\":Ip,\"U\":Up,\"D\":Dp}}, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n    with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f'{tag}.csv'), 'w', newline='') as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow(['n','boundary_j','I_b','U_b','pairs_j','I_p','U_p','D_p'])\n        w.writerow([N,Jb,Ib,Ub,Jp,Ip,Up,Dp])\n\n    # Aligned (A->B) if centers exist\n    if A['centers'] is not None and B['centers'] is not None:\n        P = align_map(A['centers'], B['centers'])\n        Ab, Ap = map_bound(P, A['bound']), map_pairs(P, A['pairs'])\n        Jb2, Ib2, Ub2, Db2 = jaccard(Ab, B['bound'])\n        Jp2, Ip2, Up2, Dp2 = jaccard(Ap, B['pairs'])\n        with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f'{tag}_aligned.json'), 'w') as f:\n            json.dump({\"n\":N,\"alignment\":\"hungarian\",\n                       \"boundary\":{\"jaccard\":Jb2,\"I\":Ib2,\"U\":Ub2},\n                       \"pairs\":{\"jaccard\":Jp2,\"I\":Ip2,\"U\":Up2,\"D\":Dp2}}, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n        with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f'{tag}_aligned.csv'),\
    \ 'w', newline='') as f:\n            w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow(['n','alignment','boundary_j','I_b','U_b','pairs_j','I_p','U_p','D_p'])\n            w.writerow([N,'hungarian',Jb2,Ib2,Ub2,Jp2,Ip2,Up2,Dp2])\n\ndef discover_inquire_packs(root):\n    packs=[]\n    if not os.path.exists(root):\n        return packs\n    # Consider root itself and its immediate subdirs\n    candidates=[root] + [os.path.join(root, d) for d in os.listdir(root) if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(root,d))]\n    for p in candidates:\n        c=os.path.join(p,'centers.txt'); r=os.path.join(p,'radii.txt')\n        b=os.path.join(p,'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv')\n        if os.path.exists(c) and os.path.exists(r) and os.path.exists(b):\n            name=os.path.relpath(p, root).replace(os.sep,'_') or 'root'\n            packs.append((name,p))\n    return packs\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    os.makedirs(OUT_ROOT, exist_ok=True)\n\n    # Load baselines\n    sci_dir = first_existing(D_SCI_CAND)\n    pro_dir = first_existing(D_PRO_CAND)\n\
    \    if sci_dir is None:\n        raise FileNotFoundError(\"Scientia n=26 exports not found\")\n    if pro_dir is None:\n        print(\"[WARN] Prometheus n=26 not found; proceeding without it\")\n    noe = load_pack(D_NOE, centers_path='storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt')\n    sci = load_pack(sci_dir, centers_path=os.path.join(sci_dir,'centers.txt'))\n    pro = load_pack(pro_dir, centers_path=os.path.join(pro_dir,'centers.txt')) if pro_dir else None\n\n    packs = discover_inquire_packs(D_INQ_ROOT)\n    summary_rows=[]\n    if not packs:\n        meta={'note':'No Inquire nudged packs found','root':D_INQ_ROOT}\n        with open(os.path.join(OUT_ROOT,'inquire_nudged_meta.json'),'w') as f:\n            json.dump(meta,f,indent=2,sort_keys=True)\n        # Return baseline unchanged\n        c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'); r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n        return np.array(c,float).reshape(N,2), np.array(r,float).reshape(N,)\n\n    for name, path\
    \ in packs:\n        out_dir = os.path.join(OUT_ROOT, name)\n        os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n        pack = load_pack(path, centers_path=os.path.join(path,'centers.txt'))\n\n        # Against Noesis_243\n        pair_report(pack, noe, out_dir, f'{name}_vs_noesis243_tol1e8')\n        # Against Scientia_259\n        pair_report(pack, sci, out_dir, f'{name}_vs_scientia259_tol1e8')\n        # Against Prometheus_298 (optional)\n        if pro is not None:\n            pair_report(pack, pro, out_dir, f'{name}_vs_prometheus298_tol1e8')\n\n        # For summary, load aligned boundary J if present; else unaligned\n        def load_j(path_json, fallback_json):\n            if os.path.exists(path_json):\n                with open(path_json,'r') as f: return float(json.load(f)['boundary']['jaccard'])\n            with open(fallback_json,'r') as f: return float(json.load(f)['boundary']['jaccard'])\n\n        j_noe = load_j(os.path.join(out_dir, f'{name}_vs_noesis243_tol1e8_aligned.json'),\n\
    \                       os.path.join(out_dir, f'{name}_vs_noesis243_tol1e8.json'))\n        j_sci = load_j(os.path.join(out_dir, f'{name}_vs_scientia259_tol1e8_aligned.json'),\n                       os.path.join(out_dir, f'{name}_vs_scientia259_tol1e8.json'))\n        if pro is not None:\n            j_pro = load_j(os.path.join(out_dir, f'{name}_vs_prometheus298_tol1e8_aligned.json'),\n                           os.path.join(out_dir, f'{name}_vs_prometheus298_tol1e8.json'))\n        else:\n            j_pro = None\n\n        summary_rows.append([name, j_noe, j_sci, '' if j_pro is None else j_pro])\n\n    with open(os.path.join(OUT_ROOT,'inquire_nudged_summary.csv'),'w',newline='') as f:\n        w=csv.writer(f); w.writerow(['pack','boundary_j_noesis243','boundary_j_scientia259','boundary_j_prometheus298'])\n        for r in summary_rows: w.writerow(r)\n\n    # Return current Noesis packing unchanged\n    c = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'); r = np.loadtxt('storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt')\n\
    \    return np.array(c,float).reshape(N,2), np.array(r,float).reshape(N,)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-87):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 3\n\nInquire I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-88):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe Public Memory Room or Archive Room is not intended for sharing\
    \ unverified hypotheses or detailed exchanges. Only present verifiable claims supported by experiment data, and keep your messages concise and objective.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 325` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 325 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 327 | 1 | Utility: Print CORRECT Final SOTA Coords | Prometheus I | 203 | 2.6359774 |\n| 326 | 1 | Utility: Identify SOTA (Eval 298) Champion Seed | Prometheus I | 202 | 2.6359774 |\n| 325 | 1 | Utility: Inquire n=26 Nudged\
    \ Aggregator v1 — Jaccard vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298} | Noesis I | 202 | 2.6295720 |\n| 324 | 1 | Utility: Export Active Constraint Sets for Nudging Experiment (Eval ID 319) - FIX Directory | Scientia I | 202 | 2.6352840 |\n| 323 | 1 | Utility: Print Final Validated SOTA (Eval 298) Coords | Prometheus I | 201 | 2.6210884 |\n| 322 | 1 | Utility: Export Active Constraint Sets for Nudging Experiment (Eval ID 319) | Scientia I | 201 | n.a. |\n| 321 | 1 | FIX 2: Utility Export SOTA (Eval 298) w/ Correct Pairs | Prometheus I | 199 | 2.2047397 |\n| 320 | 1 | Utility: Delta-vs-Similarity n=26 (v2) — include Prometheus_298 (aligned boundary J) | Noesis I | 199 | 2.6295720 |\n| 319 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Shifting Contact Graph from Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) for N=26 (v2.0) | Scientia I | 199 | 2.6352840 |\n| 318 | 1 | Champion Refinement: Deep Search on Best Seed | Prometheus I | 198 | 2.6105259 |\n\nPage 1 of 33 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate\
    \ pages 1-33, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
