role: model
parts:
- text: "My last utility submission (Eval ID 353) failed with a `ValueError: too many values to unpack` in the `_local_map_bound` function. This error occurred because `_local_get_active_constraints` was returning lists of strings (e.g., `\"b0_xmin\"`) instead of sets of tuples (e.g., `(0, \"xL\")`), which `_local_map_bound` expects to iterate over.\n\nI have identified the source of the error and will fix it by modifying `_local_get_active_constraints` to directly produce the active boundary and pair contacts as lists of `(index, tag)` or `(index1, index2)` tuples. These raw lists will then be immediately processed by `_local_normalize_indices` to convert them into the expected sets of normalized tuples before being stored and used for Jaccard calculations.\n\nMy goal remains to successfully perform Jaccard similarity analysis on my nudged packing (Eval ID 319) to quantify its structural distinctness.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia\
    \ I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 319) vs SOTAs - FIX Tuple Format\"\ntags: \"utility, Jaccard analysis, contact graph, structural distinctness, nmap, bugfix, sandbox-compat\"\nabstract: \"This is a bugfix resubmission for the Jaccard analysis utility. It resolves a 'ValueError: too many values to unpack' by correcting the output format of `_local_get_active_constraints` to produce `(index, tag)` and `(index1, index2)` tuples, which are then normalized into sets for Jaccard comparison. This ensures consistent data handling and enables the accurate quantification of structural distinctness for the Archive reviewer's challenge.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, re, csv, json, numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds, linear_sum_assignment\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  # GLOBAL CONSTANTS (should be accessible)\n  N = 26\n  TOL = 1e-8\n  OUT_ROOT = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_319'\n\n  # Constants for the original nudging experiment (copied\
    \ for internal re-optimization)\n  R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT = 1e-6 \n  EPS_CLOSE_OPT = 1e-8 \n  EPS_FAR_OPT = 0.005 \n  ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT = 1e2\n  BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT = 1e2\n  ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT = (5, 6) \n  DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT = (0, 1) \n\n  # Paths to relevant packings\n  D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudged_319_data'\n  D_NOESIS_243 = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'\n  D_SCIENTIA_259 = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26' # My own SOTA\n  D_PROMETHEUS_298_CANDIDATES = [ \n      'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/sota_298_data', \n      'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26',\n      '/home/ubuntu/station_2/station_data/rooms/research/storage/lineages/prometheus/nmap/n26',\n  ]\n\n  # Extended canonicalization for boundary labels (copied from Noesis I)\n  CANON = {\n    'xl':'xL','x_l':'xL','xleft':'xL','left':'xL','xmin':'xL','x_min':'xL',\n    'xr':'xR','x_r':'xR','xright':'xR','right':'xR','xmax':'xR','x_max':'xR',\n    'yb':'yB','y_b':'yB','ybottom':'yB','bottom':'yB','ymin':'yB','y_min':'yB',\n\
    \    'yt':'yT','y_t':'yT','ytop':'yT','top':'yT','ymax':'yT','y_max':'yT',\n    'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'\n  }\n  INT_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+')\n  NUM_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?', re.I)\n  SIDE_RE = re.compile(r'(xL|xR|yB|yT|xl|xr|yb|yt|left|right|top|bottom|xmin|xmax|ymin|ymax|x_min|x_max|y_min|y_max)', re.I)\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # All helper functions are defined locally within construct_packing to avoid NameErrors\n      # This makes the function very long but ensures sandbox compatibility.\n\n      # ---------- Feasibility helpers (copied from storage/noesis/operators.py and adapted for constants) ----------\n      def _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9):\n          x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n          cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n          return np.maximum(cap, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT)\n\n      def _local_make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000):\n    \
    \      n = centers.shape[0]\n          r = np.minimum(radii, _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n          r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT)\n          for _ in range(max_iter):\n              diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n              dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n              iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n              m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n              if np.all(m >= eps):\n                  break\n              k = int(np.argmin(m))\n              i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n              need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n              di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT)\n              dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT)\n              if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n                  r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT)\n              else:\n                  r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n              r = np.minimum(r, _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n          return centers,\
    \ r\n\n      # --- Objective and Constraint functions from Eval ID 319 (adapted for constants) ---\n      def _local_objective(x):\n          radii = x[2::3]\n          return -np.sum(radii)\n\n      def _local_penalized_objective(x):\n          centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n          radii = x[2::3]\n          \n          base_objective = -np.sum(radii)\n\n          dist_enc = np.linalg.norm(centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] - centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]])\n          dist_disc = np.linalg.norm(centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] - centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]])\n\n          target_sum_radii_enc = radii[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] + radii[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]]\n          penalty_enc = 0\n          if dist_enc > target_sum_radii_enc + EPS_CLOSE_OPT:\n              penalty_enc = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT * (dist_enc - (target_sum_radii_enc + EPS_CLOSE_OPT))**2\n          \n          target_sum_radii_disc = radii[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] + radii[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]]\n          penalty_disc = 0\n\
    \          if target_sum_radii_disc + EPS_FAR_OPT > dist_disc:\n              penalty_disc = BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT * ((target_sum_radii_disc + EPS_FAR_OPT) - dist_disc)**2\n\n          return base_objective + penalty_enc + penalty_disc\n\n      def _local_objective_jacobian(x):\n          grad = np.zeros_like(x)\n          grad[2::3] = -1.0\n          return grad\n\n      def _local_penalized_objective_jacobian(x):\n          centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n          radii = x[2::3]\n          \n          grad_base = np.zeros_like(x)\n          grad_base[2::3] = -1.0\n\n          grad_penalty_enc = np.zeros_like(x)\n          grad_penalty_disc = np.zeros_like(x)\n\n          dist_enc = np.linalg.norm(centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] - centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]])\n          target_sum_radii_enc = radii[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] + radii[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]]\n          if dist_enc > target_sum_radii_enc + EPS_CLOSE_OPT:\n              diff_val = dist_enc - (target_sum_radii_enc + EPS_CLOSE_OPT)\n\
    \              \n              unit_vec_enc = (centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] - centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]]) / (dist_enc + 1e-10)\n              grad_penalty_enc[3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]+0:3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]+2] += 2 * ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * unit_vec_enc\n              grad_penalty_enc[3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]+0:3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]+2] -= 2 * ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * unit_vec_enc\n\n              grad_penalty_enc[3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]+2] += 2 * ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * (-1.0)\n              grad_penalty_enc[3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]+2] += 2 * ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * (-1.0)\n\n          dist_disc = np.linalg.norm(centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] - centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]])\n          target_sum_radii_disc = radii[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] + radii[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]]\n          if target_sum_radii_disc + EPS_FAR_OPT > dist_disc:\n              diff_val = (target_sum_radii_disc + EPS_FAR_OPT) - dist_disc\n\n              unit_vec_disc =\
    \ (centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] - centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]]) / (dist_disc + 1e-10)\n              grad_penalty_disc[3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]+0:3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]+2] -= 2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * unit_vec_disc\n              grad_penalty_disc[3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]+0:3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]+2] += 2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * unit_vec_disc\n\n              grad_penalty_disc[3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]+2] += 2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * (1.0)\n              grad_penalty_disc[3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]+2] += 2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * (1.0)\n\n          return grad_base + grad_penalty_enc + grad_penalty_disc\n\n\n      def _local_constraints(x):\n          centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n          radii = x[2::3]\n\n          boundary_constraints = np.empty(4 * N)\n          boundary_constraints[0*N : 1*N] = centers[:, 0] - radii  # x - r >= 0\n          boundary_constraints[1*N : 2*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 0] + radii) # 1 - x - r >= 0\n \
    \         boundary_constraints[2*N : 3*N] = centers[:, 1] - radii  # y - r >= 0\n          boundary_constraints[3*N : 4*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 1] + radii) # 1 - y - r >= 0\n\n          dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n          overlap_constraints = []\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  overlap_constraints.append(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n\n          return np.concatenate((boundary_constraints, overlap_constraints))\n\n      def _local_constraints_jacobian(x):\n          centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n          radii = x[2::3]\n          grad = np.zeros((4 * N + N * (N - 1) // 2, N * 3))\n\n          for i in range(N):\n              grad[i, 3*i + 0] = 1.0; grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[N + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0; grad[N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0; grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0; grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n\
    \n          k = 4 * N\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  diff_centers = centers[i] - centers[j]\n                  dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(diff_centers)\n                  if dist_ij < 1e-10: \n                      dist_ij = 1e-10\n                  \n                  grad[k, 3*i + 0] = diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 1] = diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 0] = -diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 1] = -diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 2] = -1.0\n                  k += 1\n          return grad\n\n      # Function to generate active constraints (now returns raw tuples)\n      def _local_get_active_constraints_raw_tuples(centers, radii, tol=1e-8):\n          n = centers.shape[0]\n          \n          active_boundary_raw = []\n          for i in range(n):\n              x, y = centers[i]\n\
    \              r = radii[i]\n              if abs(x - r) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"xmin\")) # Store as (idx, tag) tuple\n              if abs(1.0 - (x + r)) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"xmax\"))\n              if abs(y - r) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"ymin\"))\n              if abs(1.0 - (y + r)) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"ymax\"))\n          \n          active_pairs_raw = []\n          dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  if abs(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])) < tol:\n                      active_pairs_raw.append((i, j)) # Store as (idx1, idx2) tuple\n          \n          return active_boundary_raw, active_pairs_raw\n\n      # ---------- Helper functions for Jaccard analysis (adapted from Noesis I's Eval ID 325 and moved to local scope) ----------\n      def _local_first_existing(paths):\n          for p in paths:\n             \
    \ if os.path.exists(p): return p\n          return None\n\n      def _local_read_lines(path):\n          with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\n              return f.read().strip().splitlines()\n\n      def _local_parse_pairs_raw(path):\n          rows=[]\n          if not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n          for ln in _local_read_lines(path):\n              toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n              if len(toks) >= 2:\n                  try:\n                      i = int(float(toks[0])); j = int(float(toks[1]))\n                      rows.append((i, j))\n                  except Exception:\n                      continue\n          return rows\n\n      def _local_parse_boundary_raw(path):\n          rows=[]\n          if not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n          for ln in _local_read_lines(path):\n              itoks = INT_RE.findall(ln)\n              if not itoks: \n                  continue\n              try:\n                  i = int(itoks[0])\n\
    \              except Exception:\n                  continue\n              m = SIDE_RE.search(ln)\n              if not m:\n                  continue\n              s_raw = m.group(1)\n              k = s_raw.replace(' ', '').replace(':','').replace(',','').replace('.','').lower()\n              s = CANON.get(k, CANON.get(k.lower(), k))\n              if s in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'):\n                  rows.append((i, s))\n          return rows\n\n      def _local_normalize_indices(rows, kind):\n          if kind == 'pairs':\n              idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows] + [j for (_, j) in rows]\n          else:\n              idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows]\n          if not idxs:\n              return set(), {'applied': False, 'mode': 'empty'}\n          c0 = sum(0 <= v <= N-1 for v in idxs)\n          c1 = sum(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs)\n          meta = {'applied': False, 'mode': 'as-is'}\n          out = set()\n          if c1 > c0 and all(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs):\n             \
    \ meta = {'applied': True, 'mode': 'minus_one'}\n              if kind == 'pairs':\n                  for (i, j) in rows:\n                      a, b = i-1, j-1\n                      if 0 <= a < N and 0 <= b < N and a != b:\n                          u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n                          out.add((u, v))\n              else:\n                  for (i, s) in rows:\n                      a = i-1\n                      if 0 <= a < N:\n                          out.add((a, s))\n          else:\n              if kind == 'pairs':\n                  for (i, j) in rows:\n                      if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N and i != j:\n                          u, v = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                          out.add((u, v))\n              else:\n                  for (i, s) in rows:\n                      if 0 <= i < N:\n                          out.add((i, s))\n          return out, meta\n\n      def _local_read_centers(path):\n          rows=[]\n      \
    \    for ln in _local_read_lines(path):\n              toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n              if len(toks) >= 2:\n                  rows.append([float(toks[0]), float(toks[1])])\n          C = np.array(rows, float)\n          if C.shape != (N, 2):\n              raise ValueError(f\"centers shape mismatch: {path} -> {C.shape}\")\n          return C\n\n      def _local_load_pack(dir_root, centers_path=None):\n          pr_raw = _local_parse_pairs_raw(os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'))\n          bd_raw = _local_parse_boundary_raw(os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'))\n          pairs, m_pairs = _local_normalize_indices(pr_raw, 'pairs')\n          bound, m_bound = _local_normalize_indices(bd_raw, 'bound')\n          C = _local_read_centers(centers_path) if centers_path and os.path.exists(centers_path) else None\n          return {'pairs': pairs, 'bound': bound, 'centers': C, 'meta': {'pairs_norm': m_pairs, 'bound_norm': m_bound}}\n\n      def _local_jaccard_calc(A,\
    \ B): \n          I = A & B; U = A | B\n          J = float(len(I))/float(len(U)) if len(U) > 0 else 1.0\n          return J, len(I), len(U), len(U) - len(I)\n\n      def _local_align_map(CA, CB):\n          if CA is None or CB is None:\n              return None \n          M = np.sum((CA[:, None, :] - CB[None, :, :])**2, axis=2)\n          r, c = linear_sum_assignment(M)\n          P = np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[r] = c\n          return P\n\n      def _local_map_pairs(P, S):\n          if P is None: return S \n          T = set()\n          for (i, j) in S:\n              a, b = int(P[i]), int(P[j])\n              if a == b:\n                  continue\n              u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n              T.add((u, v))\n          return T\n\n      def _local_map_bound(P, S):\n          if P is None: return S \n          T = set()\n          for (i, s) in S:\n              T.add((int(P[i]), s))\n          return T\n\n      def _local_write_jaccard_report(pack_A, pack_B, out_dir,\
    \ tag_A, tag_B, summary_list):\n          # Unaligned\n          Jb, Ib, Ub, Db = _local_jaccard_calc(pack_A['bound'], pack_B['bound'])\n          Jp, Ip, Up, Dp = _local_jaccard_calc(pack_A['pairs'], pack_B['pairs'])\n          \n          # Aligned (A->B) if centers exist\n          P = _local_align_map(pack_A['centers'], pack_B['centers'])\n          if P is not None:\n              Ab, Ap = _local_map_bound(P, pack_A['bound']), _local_map_pairs(P, pack_A['pairs'])\n              Jb_aligned, Ib_aligned, Ub_aligned, Db_aligned = _local_jaccard_calc(Ab, pack_B['bound'])\n              Jp_aligned, Ip_aligned, Up_aligned, Dp_aligned = _local_jaccard_calc(Ap, pack_B['pairs'])\n              alignment_status = \"hungarian\"\n          else:\n              Jb_aligned, Ib_aligned, Ub_aligned, Db_aligned = None, None, None, None\n              Jp_aligned, Ip_aligned, Up_aligned, Dp_aligned = None, None, None, None\n              alignment_status = \"unaligned\" \n\n          # Write JSON report\n\
    \          json_data = {\n              \"n\": N,\n              \"pack_A\": tag_A,\n              \"pack_B\": tag_B,\n              \"boundary\": {\n                  \"unaligned_jaccard\": Jb, \"I\": Ib, \"U\": Ub, \"D\": Db,\n                  \"aligned_jaccard\": Jb_aligned, \"I_aligned\": Ib_aligned, \"U_aligned\": Ub_aligned\n              },\n              \"pairs\": {\n                  \"unaligned_jaccard\": Jp, \"I\": Ip, \"U\": Up, \"D\": Dp,\n                  \"aligned_jaccard\": Jp_aligned, \"I_aligned\": Ip_aligned, \"U_aligned\": Up_aligned, \"D_aligned\": Dp_aligned\n              },\n              \"alignment\": alignment_status\n          }\n          with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f'{tag_A}_vs_{tag_B}_jaccard.json'), 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(json_data, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n          # Append to summary list\n          summary_list.append({\n              'pack_A': tag_A, 'pack_B': tag_B,\n              'J_bound_unaligned': Jb, 'J_pairs_unaligned':\
    \ Jp,\n              'J_bound_aligned': Jb_aligned, 'J_pairs_aligned': Jp_aligned\n          })\n\n      # --- Start of construct_packing logic ---\n      os.makedirs(OUT_ROOT, exist_ok=True)\n\n      summary_of_comparisons = []\n\n      # --- Re-run the optimization for Eval ID 319 to get the exact configuration ---\n      try:\n          base_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/centers.txt') \n          base_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/radii.txt')   \n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Scientia I's SOTA data (Eval ID 259) from storage: {e}. Falling back to a dense grid for robustness during re-optimization.\")\n          base_centers = []\n          base_radii = []\n          radius = 0.08  \n          rows = 5\n          cols = 6\n          for i in range(rows):\n              for j in range(cols):\n                  if len(base_centers) < N:\n                      x = 0.1 + i * 0.2\n                      y = 0.1 + j * 0.15\n\
    \                      base_centers.append([x, y])\n                      base_radii.append(radius)\n          base_centers = np.array(base_centers)\n          base_radii = np.array(base_radii)\n\n      base_centers, base_radii = _local_make_feasible(base_centers, base_radii, eps=1e-8)\n\n      initial_guess = np.zeros(N * 3)\n      initial_guess[0::3] = base_centers[:, 0]\n      initial_guess[1::3] = base_centers[:, 1]\n      initial_guess[2::3] = base_radii\n\n      lower_bounds = np.zeros(N * 3)\n      upper_bounds = np.ones(N * 3)\n      lower_bounds[2::3] = R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT\n      upper_bounds[2::3] = 0.5\n\n      bounds = Bounds(lower_bounds, upper_bounds)\n      ineq_constraints = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': _local_constraints, 'jac': _local_constraints_jacobian}\n\n      result = minimize(\n          _local_penalized_objective, \n          initial_guess,\n          method='SLSQP',\n          jac=_local_penalized_objective_jacobian, \n          bounds=bounds,\n          constraints=[ineq_constraints],\n\
    \          options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': True}\n      )\n\n      if not result.success:\n          print(f\"Optimization failed during re-run: {result.message}\")\n          final_centers = base_centers \n          final_radii = base_radii\n      else:\n          print(\"Re-optimization successful.\")\n          final_centers = result.x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n          final_radii = result.x[2::3]\n      \n      final_centers, final_radii = _local_make_feasible(final_centers, final_radii, eps=1e-8)\n      # --- End of re-optimization for Eval ID 319 ---\n\n      # Now load all required packs for comparison, including the re-optimized one\n      # Get raw tuples, then normalize them into sets\n      active_boundary_nudged_raw, active_pairs_nudged_raw = _local_get_active_constraints_raw_tuples(final_centers, final_radii)\n      bound_nudged_set, _ = _local_normalize_indices(active_boundary_nudged_raw, 'bound')\n      pairs_nudged_set, _ = _local_normalize_indices(active_pairs_nudged_raw,\
    \ 'pairs')\n\n      scientia_nudged_pack_for_comp = {'centers': final_centers, 'radii': final_radii, \n                                       'bound': bound_nudged_set, 'pairs': pairs_nudged_set}\n      \n      print(f\"Re-optimized Eval ID 319 data internally and prepared for comparison.\")\n\n      # Load Noesis I's SOTA (Eval ID 243)\n      try:\n          noesis_243_pack = _local_load_pack(D_NOESIS_243, centers_path='storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt') \n          print(f\"Loaded Noesis I SOTA (Eval ID 243) data from {D_NOESIS_243}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Noesis I SOTA (Eval ID 243) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Noesis.\")\n          noesis_243_pack = None\n\n      # Load Scientia I's SOTA (Eval ID 259)\n      try:\n          scientia_259_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_259, centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_259, 'centers.txt'))\n          print(f\"Loaded Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) data from {D_SCIENTIA_259}\")\n      except Exception\
    \ as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Scientia 259.\")\n          scientia_259_pack = None\n\n      # Load Prometheus I's SOTA (Eval ID 298)\n      prometheus_298_dir = _local_first_existing(D_PROMETHEUS_298_CANDIDATES)\n      if prometheus_298_dir:\n          try:\n              prometheus_298_pack = _local_load_pack(prometheus_298_dir, centers_path=os.path.join(prometheus_298_dir, 'centers.txt'))\n              print(f\"Loaded Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) data from {prometheus_298_dir}\")\n          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"Error loading Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Prometheus.\")\n              prometheus_298_pack = None\n      else:\n          print(f\"[WARN] Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) exports not found in {D_PROMETHEUS_298_CANDIDATES}. Cannot compare with Prometheus.\")\n          prometheus_298_pack = None\n\n      # Perform comparisons\n      if noesis_243_pack:\n\
    \          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_pack_for_comp, noesis_243_pack, OUT_ROOT, \n                               \"scientia_nudged_319\", \"noesis_243\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if scientia_259_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_pack_for_comp, scientia_259_pack, OUT_ROOT, \n                               \"scientia_nudged_319\", \"scientia_259\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if prometheus_298_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_pack_for_comp, prometheus_298_pack, OUT_ROOT, \n                               \"scientia_nudged_319\", \"prometheus_298\", summary_of_comparisons)\n          \n      # Write overall summary to CSV\n      summary_csv_path = os.path.join(OUT_ROOT, 'jaccard_summary_scientia_nudged_319.csv')\n      with open(summary_csv_path, 'w', newline='') as f:\n          writer = csv.writer(f)\n          if summary_of_comparisons:\n              headers = summary_of_comparisons[0].keys()\n         \
    \     writer.writerow(headers)\n              for row in summary_of_comparisons:\n                  writer.writerow(row.values())\n          else:\n              writer.writerow(['No comparisons made'])\n\n      print(f\"Jaccard analysis complete. Results exported to {OUT_ROOT}/\")\n\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
thinking_content: "**Root Cause and Solution for `ValueError: too many values to unpack`**\n\nOkay, so the last submission (Eval ID 353) failed in `_local_map_bound` with this unpacking error, and I've traced it down. The core issue is in how boundary constraints are represented within the nudged packing process.  Essentially, the `pack_A['bound']` set, which should contain tuples like `(index, side)` representing boundary constraints, is instead getting populated with *strings*. These strings are like \"b0_xmin\", which is clearly not what the unpacking `for (i, s) in S:` expects, leading to the error.\n\nLet's break it down:\n\n*   `_local_normalize_indices` is the key. It's supposed to handle these boundary constraints, expecting tuples. It does this correctly, given the right input.\n*   The raw data comes from `_local_load_pack` using `parse_boundary_raw` which does the right thing, correctly parsing a set of strings into tuples.\n*   However, `_local_get_active_constraints` is where\
  \ the misstep happens in `construct_packing`. It directly creates strings like `\"b0_xmin\"`. This is then converted to a set but those strings need to parsed (into tuples) for `normalize_indices`.\n\nThe fix is straightforward. I need to modify `_local_get_active_constraints` so that it generates *tuples* from the start. That way, those tuples can be properly processed by the normalization stage, and then used directly by `_local_map_bound` without any string-to-tuple parsing needed.\n\nHere's the revised `_local_get_active_constraints`:\n\n```python\ndef _local_get_active_constraints(centers, radii, tol=1e-8):\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n\n    active_boundary_raw = [] # Changed to raw format\n    for i in range(n):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        r = radii[i]\n        if abs(x - r) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"xmin\")) # Storing as tuple\n        if abs(1.0 - (x + r)) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"xmax\"))\n        if abs(y - r) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i,\
  \ \"ymin\"))\n        if abs(1.0 - (y + r)) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"ymax\"))\n\n    active_pairs_raw = [] # Changed to raw format\n    dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if abs(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])) < tol:\n                active_pairs_raw.append((i, j)) # Storing as tuple\n\n    # Now, apply the normalization logic that was used in load_pack\n    pairs_set, _ = _local_normalize_indices(active_pairs_raw, 'pairs')\n    bound_set, _ = _local_normalize_indices(active_boundary_raw, 'bound')\n\n    return bound_set, pairs_set # Return sets directly\n```\n\nThen, in the main code, I'll need to use:\n\n```python\nactive_boundary_nudged_set, active_pairs_nudged_set = _local_get_active_constraints(final_centers, final_radii)\nscientia_nudged_pack_for_comp['bound'] = active_boundary_nudged_set\nscientia_nudged_pack_for_comp['pairs'] = active_pairs_nudged_set\n```\n\nThis ensures that\
  \ the boundary and pair data are passed in the correct format (normalized sets).\n\nIn short, instead of outputting strings and relying on downstream functions to do the parsing, `_local_get_active_constraints` will output normalized sets in the same format that `_local_load_pack` uses. This eliminates the string-to-tuple unpacking error. This is also a much cleaner design because `_local_get_active_constraints` handles the parsing and normalization, and `construct_packing` has no extra logic to process that data."
