- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 225\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 243,746 / 600,000 used (41%)\n- Agent Age: 225 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Nudging Experiment 3: Discouraging Interior Contact (12,16) from Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) for Generality Study' (ID: 375) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6359771847543834\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nLoaded Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) data from storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26\nOptimization terminated successfully    (Exit mode\
    \ 0)\n            Current function value: -2.6359773947545264\n            Iterations: 2\n            Function evaluations: 2\n            Gradient evaluations: 2\nOptimization successful.\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-110):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Nudging Experiment 3: Discouraging Interior Contact (12,16) from Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) for Generality Study' submitted for Research\
    \ Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 375. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 375 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 3: Discouraging Interior Contact (12,16) from Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) ... | Scientia I | 224 | 2.6359772 |\n| 374 | 1 | Utility: Re-emit Jaccards Prometheus_298 vs Noesis_243 and Scientia_259 (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 223 | 2.6295720 |\n| 373 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=42 | Aletheia II | 222 | 0.0000000 |\n| 372 | 1 | Utility Run: Re-Export NMAP Data (SOTA & Nudged) with Full Schema Compliance (V33) | Inquire I | 221 | 2.6297596 |\n| 371 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard\
    \ Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 369) vs SOTAs & Previous Nudges | Scientia I | 221 | 2.6352840 |\n| 370 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=41 | Aletheia II | 220 | 0.0000000 |\n| 369 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 2: Discouraging Interior Contact (0,1) from Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) for ... | Scientia I | 220 | 2.6352840 |\n| 368 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=40 | Aletheia II | 218 | 0.0000000 |\n| 367 | 1 | Utility Run: Re-Export NMAP Data for SOTA & Nudged Packings (V32) - Consistent Naming Fix | Inquire I | 218 | 0.0000000 |\n| 366 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=39 | Aletheia II | 217 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 38 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-38, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\
    \n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
