tick: 225
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully completed \"Experiment 3: Nudge from a Different SOTA\" (Eval ID 375). This experiment, which discouraged interior contact (12,16) from Prometheus I's SOTA (Eval ID 298), yielded an impressive score of 2.6359772, which is essentially the same as the absolute SOTA. This demonstrates the generality of the nudging method to induce structural changes even from a different SOTA base, while maintaining near-optimal performance.\n\nMy multi-experiment validation plan now requires me to perform a Jaccard similarity analysis on this new packing (Eval ID 375) to quantify its structural distinctness.\n\nI will create a utility submission to re-run the optimization for Eval ID 375 internally, generate its active contacts, and then compare its contact graph against existing SOTAs (Noesis I's 243, Scientia I's 259, Prometheus I's 298) and my previous nudged packings (Eval ID 319, Eval ID 363, Eval ID 369). The results will be exported to a new dedicated directory.\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) vs SOTAs & Previous Nudges\"\ntags: \"utility, Jaccard analysis, contact graph, structural distinctness, nmap, multi-experiment\"\nabstract: \"This utility calculates the Jaccard similarity index for both active boundary and pair constraint sets of Scientia I's third nudged packing (Eval ID 375). It compares this packing against key SOTA solutions from Noesis I (Eval ID 243), Scientia I (Eval ID 259), Prometheus I (Eval ID 298), and previous nudged packings (Eval ID 319, Eval ID 363, Eval ID 369). Both unaligned and Hungarian-aligned Jaccard values are computed and exported to quantify structural distinctness as part of a multi-experiment validation study, demonstrating the generality of the nudging approach.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, re, csv, json, numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds, linear_sum_assignment\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n\
    \  # GLOBAL CONSTANTS (should be accessible)\n  N = 26\n  TOL = 1e-8\n  OUT_ROOT = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_375' # New output directory\n\n  # Constants for the original nudging experiment (Eval ID 375's internal re-optimization)\n  R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT = 1e-6 \n  EPS_CLOSE_OPT = 1e-8 \n  EPS_FAR_OPT = 0.005 \n  ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT = 0 # Disabled for Eval ID 375\n  BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT = 1e2 \n  ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT = (0, 0) # Dummy for Eval ID 375\n  DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT = (12, 16) # Targeted pair for Eval ID 375\n\n  # Paths to relevant packings\n  D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_319 = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudged_319_data' # Previous nudged packing\n  D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_363 = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_363/scientia_nudged_363_data' # Previous nudged packing\n  D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_369 = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_369/scientia_nudged_369_data' # Previous nudged packing\n  D_NOESIS_243 = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'\n  D_SCIENTIA_259 = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26'\
    \ # My own SOTA\n  D_PROMETHEUS_298_SOTA_CANDIDATES = [ \n      'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/sota_298_data', \n      'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26',\n  ]\n\n\n  # Extended canonicalization for boundary labels (copied from Noesis I)\n  CANON = {\n    'xl':'xL','x_l':'xL','xleft':'xL','left':'xL','xmin':'xL','x_min':'xL',\n    'xr':'xR','x_r':'xR','xright':'xR','right':'xR','xmax':'xR','x_max':'xR',\n    'yb':'yB','y_b':'yB','ybottom':'yB','bottom':'yB','ymin':'yB','y_min':'yB',\n    'yt':'yT','y_t':'yT','ytop':'yT','top':'yT','ymax':'yT','y_max':'yT',\n    'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'\n  }\n  INT_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+')\n  NUM_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?', re.I)\n  SIDE_RE = re.compile(r'(xL|xR|yB|yT|xl|xr|yb|yt|left|right|top|bottom|xmin|xmax|ymin|ymax|x_min|x_max|y_min|y_max)', re.I)\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # All helper functions are defined locally within construct_packing to avoid NameErrors\n      # This makes the function very\
    \ long but ensures sandbox compatibility.\n\n      # ---------- Feasibility helpers (copied from storage/noesis/operators.py and adapted for constants) ----------\n      def _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9):\n          x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n          cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n          return np.maximum(cap, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT)\n\n      def _local_make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000):\n          n = centers.shape[0]\n          r = np.minimum(radii, _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n          r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT)\n          for _ in range(max_iter):\n              diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n              dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n              iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n              m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n              if np.all(m >= eps):\n                  break\n              k = int(np.argmin(m))\n       \
    \       i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n              need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n              di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT)\n              dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT)\n              if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n                  r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT)\n              else:\n                  r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n              r = np.minimum(r, _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n          return centers, r\n\n      # --- Objective and Constraint functions from Eval ID 375 (adapted for constants) ---\n      def _local_objective(x):\n          radii = x[2::3]\n          return -np.sum(radii)\n\n      def _local_penalized_objective(x):\n          centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n          radii = x[2::3]\n          \n          base_objective = -np.sum(radii)\n\n          # Penalty for encouraging a contact (disabled in this experiment)\n          penalty_enc = 0\n          if ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT > 0: \n   \
    \           dist_enc = np.linalg.norm(centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] - centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]])\n              target_sum_radii_enc = radii[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] + radii[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]]\n              if dist_enc > target_sum_radii_enc + EPS_CLOSE_OPT:\n                  penalty_enc = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT * (dist_enc - (target_sum_radii_enc + EPS_CLOSE_OPT))**2\n          \n          # Penalty for discouraging a contact\n          penalty_disc = 0\n          if BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT > 0: \n              dist_disc = np.linalg.norm(centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] - centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]])\n              target_sum_radii_disc = radii[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] + radii[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]]\n              if target_sum_radii_disc + EPS_FAR_OPT > dist_disc: # If too close\n                  penalty_disc = BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT * ((target_sum_radii_disc + EPS_FAR_OPT) - dist_disc)**2\n\n          return base_objective + penalty_enc + penalty_disc\n\n      def _local_objective_jacobian(x):\n\
    \          grad = np.zeros_like(x)\n          grad[2::3] = -1.0\n          return grad\n\n      def _local_penalized_objective_jacobian(x):\n          centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n          radii = x[2::3]\n          \n          grad_base = np.zeros_like(x)\n          grad_base[2::3] = -1.0\n\n          grad_penalty_enc = np.zeros_like(x)\n          grad_penalty_disc = np.zeros_like(x)\n\n          if ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT > 0:\n              dist_enc = np.linalg.norm(centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] - centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]])\n              target_sum_radii_enc = radii[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] + radii[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]]\n              if dist_enc > target_sum_radii_enc + EPS_CLOSE_OPT:\n                  diff_val = dist_enc - (target_sum_radii_enc + EPS_CLOSE_OPT)\n                  \n                  unit_vec_enc = (centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] - centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]]) / (dist_enc + 1e-10)\n                  grad_penalty_enc[3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]+0:3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]+2]\
    \ += 2 * ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * unit_vec_enc\n                  grad_penalty_enc[3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]+0:3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]+2] -= 2 * ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * unit_vec_enc\n\n                  grad_penalty_enc[3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]+2] += 2 * ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * (-1.0)\n                  grad_penalty_enc[3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]+2] += 2 * ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * (-1.0)\n\n          if BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT > 0:\n              dist_disc = np.linalg.norm(centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] - centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]])\n              target_sum_radii_disc = radii[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] + radii[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]]\n              if target_sum_radii_disc + EPS_FAR_OPT > dist_disc:\n                  diff_val = (target_sum_radii_disc + EPS_FAR_OPT) - dist_disc\n\n                  unit_vec_disc = (centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]] - centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]]) / (dist_disc + 1e-10)\n                  grad_penalty_disc[3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]+0:3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]+2]\
    \ -= 2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * unit_vec_disc\n                  grad_penalty_disc[3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]+0:3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]+2] += 2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * unit_vec_disc\n\n                  grad_penalty_disc[3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[0]+2] += 2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * (1.0)\n                  grad_penalty_disc[3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT[1]+2] += 2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT * diff_val * (1.0)\n\n          return grad_base + grad_penalty_enc + grad_penalty_disc\n\n\n      def _local_constraints(x):\n          centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n          radii = x[2::3]\n\n          boundary_constraints = np.empty(4 * N)\n          boundary_constraints[0*N : 1*N] = centers[:, 0] - radii  # x - r >= 0\n          boundary_constraints[1*N : 2*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 0] + radii) # 1 - x - r >= 0\n          boundary_constraints[2*N : 3*N] = centers[:, 1] - radii  # y - r >= 0\n          boundary_constraints[3*N : 4*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 1] + radii) # 1 - y - r >=\
    \ 0\n\n          dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n          overlap_constraints = []\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  overlap_constraints.append(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n\n          return np.concatenate((boundary_constraints, overlap_constraints))\n\n      def _local_constraints_jacobian(x):\n          centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n          radii = x[2::3]\n          grad = np.zeros((4 * N + N * (N - 1) // 2, N * 3))\n\n          for i in range(N):\n              grad[i, 3*i + 0] = 1.0; grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[N + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0; grad[N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0; grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0; grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n\n          k = 4 * N\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  diff_centers = centers[i] - centers[j]\n              \
    \    dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(diff_centers)\n                  if dist_ij < 1e-10: \n                      dist_ij = 1e-10\n                  \n                  grad[k, 3*i + 0] = diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 1] = diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 0] = -diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 1] = -diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 2] = -1.0\n                  k += 1\n          return grad\n\n      # Function to generate active constraints (now returns raw tuples)\n      def _local_get_active_constraints_raw_tuples(centers, radii, tol=1e-8):\n          n = centers.shape[0]\n          \n          active_boundary_raw = []\n          for i in range(n):\n              x, y = centers[i]\n              r = radii[i]\n              if abs(x - r) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"xmin\")) \n              if abs(1.0 - (x + r)) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i,\
    \ \"xmax\"))\n              if abs(y - r) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"ymin\"))\n              if abs(1.0 - (y + r)) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"ymax\"))\n          \n          active_pairs_raw = []\n          dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  if abs(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])) < tol:\n                      active_pairs_raw.append((i, j)) \n          \n          return active_boundary_raw, active_pairs_raw\n\n      # ---------- Helper functions for Jaccard analysis (adapted from Noesis I's Eval ID 325 and moved to local scope) ----------\n      def _local_first_existing(paths):\n          for p in paths:\n              if os.path.exists(p): return p\n          return None\n\n      def _local_read_lines(path):\n          with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\n              return f.read().strip().splitlines()\n\n      def _local_parse_pairs_raw(path):\n\
    \          rows=[]\n          if not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n          for ln in _local_read_lines(path):\n              toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n              if len(toks) >= 2:\n                  try:\n                      i = int(float(toks[0])); j = int(float(toks[1]))\n                      rows.append((i, j))\n                  except Exception:\n                      continue\n          return rows\n\n      def _local_parse_boundary_raw(path):\n          rows=[]\n          if not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n          for ln in _local_read_lines(path):\n              itoks = INT_RE.findall(ln)\n              if not itoks: \n                  continue\n              try:\n                  i = int(itoks[0])\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n              m = SIDE_RE.search(ln)\n              if not m:\n                  continue\n              s_raw = m.group(1)\n              k = s_raw.replace(' ', '').replace(':','').replace(',','').replace('.','').lower()\n\
    \              s = CANON.get(k, CANON.get(k.lower(), k))\n              if s in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'):\n                  rows.append((i, s))\n          return rows\n\n      def _local_normalize_indices(rows, kind):\n          if kind == 'pairs':\n              idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows] + [j for (_, j) in rows]\n          else:\n              idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows]\n          if not idxs:\n              return set(), {'applied': False, 'mode': 'empty'}\n          c0 = sum(0 <= v <= N-1 for v in idxs)\n          c1 = sum(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs)\n          meta = {'applied': False, 'mode': 'as-is'}\n          out = set()\n          if c1 > c0 and all(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs):\n              meta = {'applied': True, 'mode': 'minus_one'}\n              if kind == 'pairs':\n                  for (i, j) in rows:\n                      a, b = i-1, j-1\n                      if 0 <= a < N and 0 <= b < N and a != b:\n                          u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n\
    \                          out.add((u, v))\n              else:\n                  for (i, s) in rows:\n                      a = i-1\n                      if 0 <= a < N:\n                          out.add((a, s))\n          else:\n              if kind == 'pairs':\n                  for (i, j) in rows:\n                      if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N and i != j:\n                          u, v = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                          out.add((u, v))\n              else:\n                  for (i, s) in rows:\n                      if 0 <= i < N:\n                          out.add((i, s))\n          return out, meta\n\n      def _local_read_centers(path):\n          rows=[]\n          for ln in _local_read_lines(path):\n              toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n              if len(toks) >= 2:\n                  rows.append([float(toks[0]), float(toks[1])])\n          C = np.array(rows, float)\n          if C.shape != (N, 2):\n              raise ValueError(f\"centers\
    \ shape mismatch: {path} -> {C.shape}\")\n          return C\n\n      def _local_load_pack(dir_root, centers_path=None):\n          pr_raw = _local_parse_pairs_raw(os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'))\n          bd_raw = _local_parse_boundary_raw(os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'))\n          pairs, m_pairs = _local_normalize_indices(pr_raw, 'pairs')\n          bound, m_bound = _local_normalize_indices(bd_raw, 'bound')\n          C = _local_read_centers(centers_path) if centers_path and os.path.exists(centers_path) else None\n          return {'pairs': pairs, 'bound': bound, 'centers': C, 'meta': {'pairs_norm': m_pairs, 'bound_norm': m_bound}}\n\n      def _local_jaccard_calc(A, B): \n          I = A & B; U = A | B\n          J = float(len(I))/float(len(U)) if len(U) > 0 else 1.0\n          return J, len(I), len(U), len(U) - len(I)\n\n      def _local_align_map(CA, CB):\n          if CA is None or CB is None:\n              return None \n          M =\
    \ np.sum((CA[:, None, :] - CB[None, :, :])**2, axis=2)\n          r, c = linear_sum_assignment(M)\n          P = np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[r] = c\n          return P\n\n      def _local_map_pairs(P, S):\n          if P is None: return S \n          T = set()\n          for (i, j) in S:\n              a, b = int(P[i]), int(P[j])\n              if a == b:\n                  continue\n              u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n              T.add((u, v))\n          return T\n\n      def _local_map_bound(P, S):\n          if P is None: return S \n          T = set()\n          for (i, s) in S:\n              T.add((int(P[i]), s))\n          return T\n\n      def _local_write_jaccard_report(pack_A, pack_B, out_dir, tag_A, tag_B, summary_list):\n          # Unaligned\n          Jb, Ib, Ub, Db = _local_jaccard_calc(pack_A['bound'], pack_B['bound'])\n          Jp, Ip, Up, Dp = _local_jaccard_calc(pack_A['pairs'], pack_B['pairs'])\n          \n          # Aligned (A->B) if centers exist\n\
    \          P = _local_align_map(pack_A['centers'], pack_B['centers'])\n          if P is not None:\n              Ab, Ap = _local_map_bound(P, pack_A['bound']), _local_map_pairs(P, pack_A['pairs'])\n              Jb_aligned, Ib_aligned, Ub_aligned, Db_aligned = _local_jaccard_calc(Ab, pack_B['bound'])\n              Jp_aligned, Ip_aligned, Up_aligned, Dp_aligned = _local_jaccard_calc(Ap, pack_B['pairs'])\n              alignment_status = \"hungarian\"\n          else:\n              Jb_aligned, Ib_aligned, Ub_aligned, Db_aligned = None, None, None, None\n              Jp_aligned, Ip_aligned, Up_aligned, Dp_aligned = None, None, None, None\n              alignment_status = \"unaligned\" \n\n          # Write JSON report\n          json_data = {\n              \"n\": N,\n              \"pack_A\": tag_A,\n              \"pack_B\": tag_B,\n              \"boundary\": {\n                  \"unaligned_jaccard\": Jb, \"I\": Ib, \"U\": Ub, \"D\": Db,\n                  \"aligned_jaccard\": Jb_aligned,\
    \ \"I_aligned\": Ib_aligned, \"U_aligned\": Ub_aligned\n              },\n              \"pairs\": {\n                  \"unaligned_jaccard\": Jp, \"I\": Ip, \"U\": Up, \"D\": Dp,\n                  \"aligned_jaccard\": Jp_aligned, \"I_aligned\": Ip_aligned, \"U_aligned\": Up_aligned, \"D_aligned\": Dp_aligned\n              },\n              \"alignment\": alignment_status\n          }\n          with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f'{tag_A}_vs_{tag_B}_jaccard.json'), 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(json_data, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n          # Append to summary list\n          summary_list.append({\n              'pack_A': tag_A, 'pack_B': tag_B,\n              'J_bound_unaligned': Jb, 'J_pairs_unaligned': Jp,\n              'J_bound_aligned': Jb_aligned, 'J_pairs_aligned': Jp_aligned\n          })\n\n      # --- Start of construct_packing logic ---\n      os.makedirs(OUT_ROOT, exist_ok=True)\n\n      summary_of_comparisons = []\n\n      # Attempt to load Prometheus I's SOTA\
    \ (Eval ID 298) as base\n      base_centers = None\n      base_radii = None\n      prometheus_loaded = False\n\n      for p_dir in D_PROMETHEUS_298_SOTA_CANDIDATES:\n          try:\n              c_path = os.path.join(p_dir, 'centers.txt')\n              r_path = os.path.join(p_dir, 'radii.txt')\n              if os.path.exists(c_path) and os.path.exists(r_path):\n                  base_centers = np.loadtxt(c_path)\n                  base_radii = np.loadtxt(r_path)\n                  print(f\"Loaded Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) data from {p_dir}\")\n                  prometheus_loaded = True\n                  break\n          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"Attempt to load Prometheus SOTA from {p_dir} failed: {e}\")\n              continue\n      \n      if not prometheus_loaded:\n          print(f\"Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) not found. Falling back to Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) as base.\")\n          try:\n              base_centers = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_259,\
    \ 'centers.txt')) \n              base_radii = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_259, 'radii.txt'))   \n          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"Error loading Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) from storage: {e}. Falling back to a dense grid for robustness.\")\n              base_centers = []\n              base_radii = []\n              radius = 0.08  \n              rows = 5\n              cols = 6\n              for i in range(rows):\n                  for j in range(cols):\n                      if len(base_centers) < N:\n                          x = 0.1 + i * 0.2\n                          y = 0.1 + j * 0.15\n                          base_centers.append([x, y])\n                          base_radii.append(radius)\n              base_centers = np.array(base_centers)\n              base_radii = np.array(base_radii)\n\n      base_centers, base_radii = _local_make_feasible(base_centers, base_radii, eps=1e-8)\n\n      initial_guess = np.zeros(N * 3)\n      initial_guess[0::3]\
    \ = base_centers[:, 0]\n      initial_guess[1::3] = base_centers[:, 1]\n      initial_guess[2::3] = base_radii\n\n      lower_bounds = np.zeros(N * 3)\n      upper_bounds = np.ones(N * 3)\n      lower_bounds[2::3] = R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT\n      upper_bounds[2::3] = 0.5\n\n      bounds = Bounds(lower_bounds, upper_bounds)\n      ineq_constraints = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': _local_constraints, 'jac': _local_constraints_jacobian}\n\n      result = minimize(\n          _local_penalized_objective, \n          initial_guess,\n          method='SLSQP',\n          jac=_local_penalized_objective_jacobian, \n          bounds=bounds,\n          constraints=[ineq_constraints],\n          options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': True}\n      )\n\n      if not result.success:\n          print(f\"Optimization failed during re-run of Eval ID 375: {result.message}\")\n          final_centers_375 = base_centers \n          final_radii_375 = base_radii\n      else:\n          print(\"Re-optimization\
    \ of Eval ID 375 successful.\")\n          final_centers_375 = result.x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n          final_radii_375 = result.x[2::3]\n      \n      final_centers_375, final_radii_375 = _local_make_feasible(final_centers_375, final_radii_375, eps=1e-8)\n      # --- End of re-optimization for Eval ID 375 ---\n\n      # Prepare Scientia I's new nudged packing (Eval ID 375) for comparison\n      active_boundary_375_raw, active_pairs_375_raw = _local_get_active_constraints_raw_tuples(final_centers_375, final_radii_375)\n      bound_375_set, _ = _local_normalize_indices(active_boundary_375_raw, 'bound')\n      pairs_375_set, _ = _local_normalize_indices(active_pairs_375_raw, 'pairs')\n\n      scientia_nudged_375_pack_for_comp = {'centers': final_centers_375, 'radii': final_radii_375, \n                                            'bound': bound_375_set, 'pairs': pairs_375_set}\n      print(f\"Re-optimized Eval ID 375 data internally and prepared for comparison.\")\n\n      # Load Scientia\
    \ I's previous nudged packing (Eval ID 319)\n      try:\n          scientia_nudged_319_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_319, centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_319, 'centers.txt'))\n          print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 319) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_319}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 319) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Eval ID 319.\")\n          scientia_nudged_319_pack = None\n\n      # Load Scientia I's previous nudged packing (Eval ID 363)\n      try:\n          scientia_nudged_363_pack = _local_load_pack('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_363/scientia_nudged_363_data', \n                                                       centers_path=os.path.join('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_363/scientia_nudged_363_data', 'centers.txt'))\n          print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 363) data from {'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_363/scientia_nudged_363_data'}\"\
    )\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 363) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Eval ID 363.\")\n          scientia_nudged_363_pack = None\n\n      # Load Scientia I's previous nudged packing (Eval ID 369)\n      try:\n          scientia_nudged_369_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_369, centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_369, 'centers.txt'))\n          print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 369) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_369}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 369) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Eval ID 369.\")\n          scientia_nudged_369_pack = None\n\n      # Load Noesis I's SOTA (Eval ID 243)\n      try:\n          noesis_243_pack = _local_load_pack(D_NOESIS_243, centers_path='storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt') \n          print(f\"Loaded Noesis I SOTA (Eval ID 243) data from {D_NOESIS_243}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error\
    \ loading Noesis I SOTA (Eval ID 243) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Noesis.\")\n          noesis_243_pack = None\n\n      # Load Scientia I's SOTA (Eval ID 259)\n      try:\n          scientia_259_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_259, centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_259, 'centers.txt'))\n          print(f\"Loaded Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) data from {D_SCIENTIA_259}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Scientia 259.\")\n          scientia_259_pack = None\n\n      # Load Prometheus I's SOTA (Eval ID 298)\n      prometheus_298_dir = _local_first_existing(D_PROMETHEUS_298_SOTA_CANDIDATES)\n      if prometheus_298_dir:\n          try:\n              prometheus_298_pack = _local_load_pack(prometheus_298_dir, centers_path=os.path.join(prometheus_298_dir, 'centers.txt'))\n              print(f\"Loaded Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) data from {prometheus_298_dir}\")\n          except Exception\
    \ as e:\n              print(f\"Error loading Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Prometheus.\")\n              prometheus_298_pack = None\n      else:\n          print(f\"[WARN] Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) exports not found in {D_PROMETHEUS_298_SOTA_CANDIDATES}. Cannot compare with Prometheus.\")\n          prometheus_298_pack = None\n\n      # Perform comparisons\n      if noesis_243_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_375_pack_for_comp, noesis_243_pack, OUT_ROOT, \n                               \"scientia_nudged_375\", \"noesis_243\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if scientia_259_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_375_pack_for_comp, scientia_259_pack, OUT_ROOT, \n                               \"scientia_nudged_375\", \"scientia_259\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if prometheus_298_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_375_pack_for_comp, prometheus_298_pack, OUT_ROOT, \n  \
    \                             \"scientia_nudged_375\", \"prometheus_298\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if scientia_nudged_319_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_375_pack_for_comp, scientia_nudged_319_pack, OUT_ROOT,\n                               \"scientia_nudged_375\", \"scientia_nudged_319\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if scientia_nudged_363_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_375_pack_for_comp, scientia_nudged_363_pack, OUT_ROOT,\n                               \"scientia_nudged_375\", \"scientia_nudged_363\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if scientia_nudged_369_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_375_pack_for_comp, scientia_nudged_369_pack, OUT_ROOT,\n                               \"scientia_nudged_375\", \"scientia_nudged_369\", summary_of_comparisons)\n          \n      # Write overall summary to CSV\n      summary_csv_path = os.path.join(OUT_ROOT, 'jaccard_summary_scientia_nudged_375.csv')\n\
    \      with open(summary_csv_path, 'w', newline='') as f:\n          writer = csv.writer(f)\n          if summary_of_comparisons:\n              headers = summary_of_comparisons[0].keys()\n              writer.writerow(headers)\n              for row in summary_of_comparisons:\n                  writer.writerow(row.values())\n          else:\n              writer.writerow(['No comparisons made'])\n\n      print(f\"Jaccard analysis complete. Results exported to {OUT_ROOT}/\")\n\n      return final_centers_375, final_radii_375\n```"
