parts:
- text: "I have successfully completed \"Nudging Experiment 4: Local Multi-Start Optimization of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 363) within its Distinct Structural Basin\" (Eval ID 387). This experiment yielded a score of 2.6358955, which is a significant improvement over the base Eval ID 363 (2.6351560) and matches my own SOTA (Eval ID 259), coming very close to the absolute SOTA. This demonstrates that even within a distinct structural basin, there is potential for score refinement, validating the robustness of the discovered structure.\n\nI have now completed four of the five required experiments for my multi-experiment validation study for publication. The next step is to perform a Jaccard similarity analysis on this new packing (Eval ID 387) to confirm that the local optimization did not inadvertently shift it back into a previously known structural class.\n\nI will create a utility submission to re-run the optimization for Eval ID 387 internally, generate its active contacts, and\
    \ then compare its contact graph against existing SOTAs (Noesis I's 243, Scientia I's 259, Prometheus I's 298) and my previous nudged packings (Eval ID 319, Eval ID 363, Eval ID 369, Eval ID 375). The results will be exported to a new dedicated directory.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 387) vs SOTAs & Previous Nudges (Post Local-Refinement)\"\ntags: \"utility, Jaccard analysis, contact graph, structural distinctness, nmap, multi-experiment, local refinement\"\nabstract: \"This utility calculates the Jaccard similarity index for both active boundary and pair constraint sets of Scientia I's refined nudged packing (Eval ID 387), which resulted from local multi-start optimization of Eval ID 363. It compares this packing against key SOTA solutions and previous nudged packings (Eval IDs 319, 363, 369, 375) to confirm its continued structural distinctness after score refinement, as part of a multi-experiment\
    \ validation study for publication.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, re, csv, json, numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds, linear_sum_assignment\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  # GLOBAL CONSTANTS (should be accessible)\n  N = 26\n  TOL = 1e-8\n  OUT_ROOT = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_387' # New output directory\n\n  # Constants for the original nudging experiment (Eval ID 387's internal re-optimization)\n  R_MIN_CONSTRAINT_OPT = 1e-6 \n  EPS_CLOSE_OPT = 1e-8 # Not used in Eval ID 387's objective, but included for completeness if code is adapted.\n  EPS_FAR_OPT = 0.005 # Not used in Eval ID 387's objective.\n  ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_OPT = 0 # Not used in Eval ID 387's objective.\n  BETA_DISCOURAGE_OPT = 0 # Not used in Eval ID 387's objective.\n  ENCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT = (0, 0) # Dummy\n  DISCOURAGE_PAIR_OPT = (0, 0) # Dummy\n\n  # Multi-start parameters for re-optimization (copied from Eval ID 387 for internal re-run)\n  NUM_RESTARTS_OPT\
    \ = 5 \n  PERTURB_MAGNITUDE_OPT = 1e-4 \n\n  # Paths to relevant packings\n  D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_319 = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudged_319_data' \n  D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_363_EXPORTED = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_363_data' # Base for Eval ID 387\n  D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_369 = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_369/scientia_nudged_369_data' \n  D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375 = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_375/scientia_nudged_375_data'\n  D_NOESIS_243 = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'\n  D_SCIENTIA_259 = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26' # My own SOTA\n  D_PROMETHEUS_298_SOTA_CANDIDATES = [ \n      'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/sota_298_data', \n      'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26',\n  ]\n\n\n  # Extended canonicalization for boundary labels (copied from Noesis I)\n  CANON = {\n    'xl':'xL','x_l':'xL','xleft':'xL','left':'xL','xmin':'xL','x_min':'xL',\n    'xr':'xR','x_r':'xR','xright':'xR','right':'xR','xmax':'xR','x_max':'xR',\n    'yb':'yB','y_b':'yB','ybottom':'yB','bottom':'yB','ymin':'yB','y_min':'yB',\n\
    \    'yt':'yT','y_t':'yT','ytop':'yT','top':'yT','ymax':'yT','y_max':'yT',\n    'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'\n  }\n  INT_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+')\n  NUM_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?', re.I)\n  SIDE_RE = re.compile(r'(xL|xR|yB|yT|xl|xr|yb|yt|left|right|top|bottom|xmin|xmax|ymin|ymax|x_min|x_max|y_min|y_max)', re.I)\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # All helper functions are defined locally within construct_packing to avoid NameErrors\n      # This makes the function very long but ensures sandbox compatibility.\n\n      # ---------- Feasibility helpers (copied for self-containment) ----------\n      def _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9):\n          x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n          cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n          return np.maximum(cap, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n\n      def _local_make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000):\n          n = centers.shape[0]\n          r = np.minimum(radii,\
    \ _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n          r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n          for _ in range(max_iter):\n              diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n              dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n              iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n              m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n              if np.all(m >= eps):\n                  break\n              k = int(np.argmin(m))\n              i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n              need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n              di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n              dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n              if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n                  r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n              else:\n                  r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n              r = np.minimum(r, _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n          return centers, r\n\n      # --- Objective and Constraint functions (original, non-penalized,\
    \ from Eval ID 387's internal re-run) ---\n      def _local_objective(x):\n          radii = x[2::3]\n          return -np.sum(radii)\n\n      def _local_objective_jacobian(x):\n          grad = np.zeros_like(x)\n          grad[2::3] = -1.0\n          return grad\n\n      def _local_constraints(x):\n          centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n          radii = x[2::3]\n\n          boundary_constraints = np.empty(4 * N)\n          boundary_constraints[0*N : 1*N] = centers[:, 0] - radii  # x - r >= 0\n          boundary_constraints[1*N : 2*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 0] + radii) # 1 - x - r >= 0\n          boundary_constraints[2*N : 3*N] = centers[:, 1] - radii  # y - r >= 0\n          boundary_constraints[3*N : 4*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 1] + radii) # 1 - y - r >= 0\n\n          dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n          overlap_constraints = []\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  overlap_constraints.append(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i]\
    \ + radii[j]))\n\n          return np.concatenate((boundary_constraints, overlap_constraints))\n\n      def _local_constraints_jacobian(x):\n          centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n          radii = x[2::3]\n          grad = np.zeros((4 * N + N * (N - 1) // 2, N * 3))\n\n          for i in range(N):\n              grad[i, 3*i + 0] = 1.0; grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[N + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0; grad[N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0; grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0; grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n\n          k = 4 * N\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  diff_centers = centers[i] - centers[j]\n                  dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(diff_centers)\n                  if dist_ij < 1e-10: \n                      dist_ij = 1e-10\n                  \n                  grad[k, 3*i + 0] = diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 1]\
    \ = diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 0] = -diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 1] = -diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 2] = -1.0\n                  k += 1\n          return grad\n\n      # Function to generate active constraints (now returns raw tuples)\n      def _local_get_active_constraints_raw_tuples(centers, radii, tol=1e-8):\n          n = centers.shape[0]\n          \n          active_boundary_raw = []\n          for i in range(n):\n              x, y = centers[i]\n              r = radii[i]\n              if abs(x - r) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"xmin\")) \n              if abs(1.0 - (x + r)) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"xmax\"))\n              if abs(y - r) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"ymin\"))\n              if abs(1.0 - (y + r)) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"ymax\"))\n          \n          active_pairs_raw = []\n \
    \         dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  if abs(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])) < tol:\n                      active_pairs_raw.append((i, j)) \n          \n          return active_boundary_raw, active_pairs_raw\n\n      # ---------- Helper functions for Jaccard analysis (adapted from Noesis I's Eval ID 325 and moved to local scope) ----------\n      def _local_first_existing(paths):\n          for p in paths:\n              if os.path.exists(p): return p\n          return None\n\n      def _local_read_lines(path):\n          with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\n              return f.read().strip().splitlines()\n\n      def _local_parse_pairs_raw(path):\n          rows=[]\n          if not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n          for ln in _local_read_lines(path):\n              toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n              if len(toks) >= 2:\n     \
    \             try:\n                      i = int(float(toks[0])); j = int(float(toks[1]))\n                      rows.append((i, j))\n                  except Exception:\n                      continue\n          return rows\n\n      def _local_parse_boundary_raw(path):\n          rows=[]\n          if not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n          for ln in _local_read_lines(path):\n              itoks = INT_RE.findall(ln)\n              if not itoks: \n                  continue\n              try:\n                  i = int(itoks[0])\n              except Exception:\n                  continue\n              m = SIDE_RE.search(ln)\n              if not m:\n                  continue\n              s_raw = m.group(1)\n              k = s_raw.replace(' ', '').replace(':','').replace(',','').replace('.','').lower()\n              s = CANON.get(k, CANON.get(k.lower(), k))\n              if s in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'):\n                  rows.append((i, s))\n          return rows\n\n\
    \      def _local_normalize_indices(rows, kind):\n          if kind == 'pairs':\n              idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows] + [j for (_, j) in rows]\n          else:\n              idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows]\n          if not idxs:\n              return set(), {'applied': False, 'mode': 'empty'}\n          c0 = sum(0 <= v <= N-1 for v in idxs)\n          c1 = sum(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs)\n          meta = {'applied': False, 'mode': 'as-is'}\n          out = set()\n          if c1 > c0 and all(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs):\n              meta = {'applied': True, 'mode': 'minus_one'}\n              if kind == 'pairs':\n                  for (i, j) in rows:\n                      a, b = i-1, j-1\n                      if 0 <= a < N and 0 <= b < N and a != b:\n                          u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n                          out.add((u, v))\n              else:\n                  for (i, s) in rows:\n                      a = i-1\n                      if 0 <= a\
    \ < N:\n                          out.add((a, s))\n          else:\n              if kind == 'pairs':\n                  for (i, j) in rows:\n                      if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N and i != j:\n                          u, v = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                          out.add((u, v))\n              else:\n                  for (i, s) in rows:\n                      if 0 <= i < N:\n                          out.add((i, s))\n          return out, meta\n\n      def _local_read_centers(path):\n          rows=[]\n          for ln in _local_read_lines(path):\n              toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n              if len(toks) >= 2:\n                  rows.append([float(toks[0]), float(toks[1])])\n          C = np.array(rows, float)\n          if C.shape != (N, 2):\n              raise ValueError(f\"centers shape mismatch: {path} -> {C.shape}\")\n          return C\n\n      def _local_load_pack(dir_root, centers_path=None):\n          pr_raw = _local_parse_pairs_raw(os.path.join(dir_root,\
    \ 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'))\n          bd_raw = _local_parse_boundary_raw(os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'))\n          pairs, m_pairs = _local_normalize_indices(pr_raw, 'pairs')\n          bound, m_bound = _local_normalize_indices(bd_raw, 'bound')\n          C = _local_read_centers(centers_path) if centers_path and os.path.exists(centers_path) else None\n          return {'pairs': pairs, 'bound': bound, 'centers': C, 'meta': {'pairs_norm': m_pairs, 'bound_norm': m_bound}}\n\n      def _local_jaccard_calc(A, B): \n          I = A & B; U = A | B\n          J = float(len(I))/float(len(U)) if len(U) > 0 else 1.0\n          return J, len(I), len(U), len(U) - len(I)\n\n      def _local_align_map(CA, CB):\n          if CA is None or CB is None:\n              return None \n          M = np.sum((CA[:, None, :] - CB[None, :, :])**2, axis=2)\n          r, c = linear_sum_assignment(M)\n          P = np.zeros(N, dtype=int); P[r] = c\n          return P\n\n      def _local_map_pairs(P,\
    \ S):\n          if P is None: return S \n          T = set()\n          for (i, j) in S:\n              a, b = int(P[i]), int(P[j])\n              if a == b:\n                  continue\n              u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n              T.add((u, v))\n          return T\n\n      def _local_map_bound(P, S):\n          if P is None: return S \n          T = set()\n          for (i, s) in S:\n              T.add((int(P[i]), s))\n          return T\n\n      def _local_write_jaccard_report(pack_A, pack_B, out_dir, tag_A, tag_B, summary_list):\n          # Unaligned\n          Jb, Ib, Ub, Db = _local_jaccard_calc(pack_A['bound'], pack_B['bound'])\n          Jp, Ip, Up, Dp = _local_jaccard_calc(pack_A['pairs'], pack_B['pairs'])\n          \n          # Aligned (A->B) if centers exist\n          P = _local_align_map(pack_A['centers'], pack_B['centers'])\n          if P is not None:\n              Ab, Ap = _local_map_bound(P, pack_A['bound']), _local_map_pairs(P, pack_A['pairs'])\n\
    \              Jb_aligned, Ib_aligned, Ub_aligned, Db_aligned = _local_jaccard_calc(Ab, pack_B['bound'])\n              Jp_aligned, Ip_aligned, Up_aligned, Dp_aligned = _local_jaccard_calc(Ap, pack_B['pairs'])\n              alignment_status = \"hungarian\"\n          else:\n              Jb_aligned, Ib_aligned, Ub_aligned, Db_aligned = None, None, None, None\n              Jp_aligned, Ip_aligned, Up_aligned, Dp_aligned = None, None, None, None\n              alignment_status = \"unaligned\" \n\n          # Write JSON report\n          json_data = {\n              \"n\": N,\n              \"pack_A\": tag_A,\n              \"pack_B\": tag_B,\n              \"boundary\": {\n                  \"unaligned_jaccard\": Jb, \"I\": Ib, \"U\": Ub, \"D\": Db,\n                  \"aligned_jaccard\": Jb_aligned, \"I_aligned\": Ib_aligned, \"U_aligned\": Ub_aligned\n              },\n              \"pairs\": {\n                  \"unaligned_jaccard\": Jp, \"I\": Ip, \"U\": Up, \"D\": Dp,\n       \
    \           \"aligned_jaccard\": Jp_aligned, \"I_aligned\": Ip_aligned, \"U_aligned\": Up_aligned, \"D_aligned\": Dp_aligned\n              },\n              \"alignment\": alignment_status\n          }\n          with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f'{tag_A}_vs_{tag_B}_jaccard.json'), 'w') as f:\n              json.dump(json_data, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n          # Append to summary list\n          summary_list.append({\n              'pack_A': tag_A, 'pack_B': tag_B,\n              'J_bound_unaligned': Jb, 'J_pairs_unaligned': Jp,\n              'J_bound_aligned': Jb_aligned, 'J_pairs_aligned': Jp_aligned\n          })\n\n      # --- Start of construct_packing logic ---\n      os.makedirs(OUT_ROOT, exist_ok=True)\n\n      summary_of_comparisons = []\n\n      # --- Re-run the optimization for Eval ID 387 to get the exact configuration ---\n      # Load Scientia I's Nudged Packing (Eval ID 363) as base for multi-start re-optimization\n      try:\n          base_centers_387 = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_363_EXPORTED,\
    \ 'centers.txt'))\n          base_radii_387 = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_363_EXPORTED, 'radii.txt'))\n          print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 363) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_363_EXPORTED} for re-optimization of Eval ID 387.\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 363) data for Eval ID 387 re-optimization: {e}. Falling back to a dense grid.\")\n          base_centers_387 = []\n          base_radii_387 = []\n          radius = 0.08  \n          rows = 5\n          cols = 6\n          for i in range(rows):\n              for j in range(cols):\n                  if len(base_centers_387) < N:\n                      x = 0.1 + i * 0.2\n                      y = 0.1 + j * 0.15\n                      base_centers_387.append([x, y])\n                      base_radii_387.append(radius)\n          base_centers_387 = np.array(base_centers_387)\n          base_radii_387 = np.array(base_radii_387)\n\n      base_centers_387,\
    \ base_radii_387 = _local_make_feasible(base_centers_387, base_radii_387, eps=1e-8)\n\n      best_score_387 = -np.sum(base_radii_387) \n      best_centers_387 = base_centers_387\n      best_radii_387 = base_radii_387\n\n      for restart_idx in range(NUM_RESTARTS_OPT):\n          current_centers = base_centers_387 + np.random.uniform(-PERTURB_MAGNITUDE_OPT, PERTURB_MAGNITUDE_OPT, base_centers_387.shape)\n          current_radii = base_radii_387 \n          current_centers = np.clip(current_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n          current_centers, current_radii = _local_make_feasible(current_centers, current_radii, eps=1e-8)\n\n          initial_guess = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          initial_guess[0::3] = current_centers[:, 0]\n          initial_guess[1::3] = current_centers[:, 1]\n          initial_guess[2::3] = current_radii\n\n          lower_bounds = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          upper_bounds = np.ones(N * 3)\n          lower_bounds[2::3] = R_MIN_CONSTRAINT\n       \
    \   upper_bounds[2::3] = 0.5\n\n          bounds = Bounds(lower_bounds, upper_bounds)\n          ineq_constraints = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': _local_constraints, 'jac': _local_constraints_jacobian}\n\n          result = minimize(\n              _local_objective, \n              initial_guess,\n              method='SLSQP',\n              jac=_local_objective_jacobian, \n              bounds=bounds,\n              constraints=[ineq_constraints],\n              options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False} \n          )\n\n          if result.success and -result.fun > -best_score_387: \n              best_score_387 = -result.fun\n              best_centers_387 = result.x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n              best_radii_387 = result.x[2::3]\n              best_centers_387, best_radii_387 = _local_make_feasible(best_centers_387, best_radii_387, eps=1e-8)\n              print(f\"Restart {restart_idx+1} for Eval ID 387 re-optimization: New best score found: {-result.fun}\")\n        \
    \  #else:\n              #print(f\"Restart {restart_idx+1} for Eval ID 387 re-optimization: Score: {-result.fun if result.success else 'n.a.'} (Current best: {-best_score_387})\")\n\n      print(f\"Re-optimization of Eval ID 387 finished. Best score: {-best_score_387}\")\n      final_centers_387 = best_centers_387\n      final_radii_387 = best_radii_387\n      # --- End of re-optimization for Eval ID 387 ---\n\n      # Prepare Scientia I's new nudged packing (Eval ID 387) for comparison\n      active_boundary_387_raw, active_pairs_387_raw = _local_get_active_constraints_raw_tuples(final_centers_387, final_radii_387)\n      bound_387_set, _ = _local_normalize_indices(active_boundary_387_raw, 'bound')\n      pairs_387_set, _ = _local_normalize_indices(active_pairs_387_raw, 'pairs')\n\n      scientia_nudged_387_pack_for_comp = {'centers': final_centers_387, 'radii': final_radii_387, \n                                            'bound': bound_387_set, 'pairs': pairs_387_set}\n      print(f\"\
    Re-optimized Eval ID 387 data internally and prepared for comparison.\")\n\n      # Load Scientia I's previous nudged packing (Eval ID 319)\n      try:\n          scientia_nudged_319_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_319, centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_319, 'centers.txt'))\n          print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 319) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_319}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 319) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Eval ID 319.\")\n          scientia_nudged_319_pack = None\n\n      # Load Scientia I's previous nudged packing (Eval ID 363) - from its explicit export\n      try:\n          scientia_nudged_363_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_363_EXPORTED, \n                                                       centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_363_EXPORTED, 'centers.txt'))\n          print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 363) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_363_EXPORTED}\"\
    )\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 363) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Eval ID 363.\")\n          scientia_nudged_363_pack = None\n\n      # Load Scientia I's previous nudged packing (Eval ID 369)\n      try:\n          scientia_nudged_369_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_369, centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_369, 'centers.txt'))\n          print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 369) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_369}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 369) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Eval ID 369.\")\n          scientia_nudged_369_pack = None\n\n      # Load Scientia I's previous nudged packing (Eval ID 375)\n      try:\n          scientia_nudged_375_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375, centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375, 'centers.txt'))\n          print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 375) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375}\"\
    )\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 375) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Eval ID 375.\")\n          scientia_nudged_375_pack = None\n\n\n      # Load Noesis I's SOTA (Eval ID 243)\n      try:\n          noesis_243_pack = _local_load_pack(D_NOESIS_243, centers_path='storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt') \n          print(f\"Loaded Noesis I SOTA (Eval ID 243) data from {D_NOESIS_243}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Noesis I SOTA (Eval ID 243) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Noesis.\")\n          noesis_243_pack = None\n\n      # Load Scientia I's SOTA (Eval ID 259)\n      try:\n          scientia_259_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_259, centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_259, 'centers.txt'))\n          print(f\"Loaded Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) data from {D_SCIENTIA_259}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) data: {e}. Cannot compare\
    \ with Scientia 259.\")\n          scientia_259_pack = None\n\n      # Load Prometheus I's SOTA (Eval ID 298)\n      prometheus_298_dir = _local_first_existing(D_PROMETHEUS_298_SOTA_CANDIDATES)\n      if prometheus_298_dir:\n          try:\n              prometheus_298_pack = _local_load_pack(prometheus_298_dir, centers_path=os.path.join(prometheus_298_dir, 'centers.txt'))\n              print(f\"Loaded Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) data from {prometheus_298_dir}\")\n          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"Error loading Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Prometheus.\")\n              prometheus_298_pack = None\n      else:\n          print(f\"[WARN] Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) exports not found in {D_PROMETHEUS_298_SOTA_CANDIDATES}. Cannot compare with Prometheus.\")\n          prometheus_298_pack = None\n\n      # Perform comparisons\n      if noesis_243_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_387_pack_for_comp,\
    \ noesis_243_pack, OUT_ROOT, \n                               \"scientia_nudged_387\", \"noesis_243\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if scientia_259_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_387_pack_for_comp, scientia_259_pack, OUT_ROOT, \n                               \"scientia_nudged_387\", \"scientia_259\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if prometheus_298_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_387_pack_for_comp, prometheus_298_pack, OUT_ROOT, \n                               \"scientia_nudged_387\", \"prometheus_298\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if scientia_nudged_319_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_387_pack_for_comp, scientia_nudged_319_pack, OUT_ROOT,\n                               \"scientia_nudged_387\", \"scientia_nudged_319\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if scientia_nudged_363_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_387_pack_for_comp, scientia_nudged_363_pack, OUT_ROOT,\n \
    \                              \"scientia_nudged_387\", \"scientia_nudged_363\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if scientia_nudged_369_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_387_pack_for_comp, scientia_nudged_369_pack, OUT_ROOT,\n                               \"scientia_nudged_387\", \"scientia_nudged_369\", summary_of_comparisons)\n      if scientia_nudged_375_pack:\n          _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_nudged_387_pack_for_comp, scientia_nudged_375_pack, OUT_ROOT,\n                               \"scientia_nudged_387\", \"scientia_nudged_375\", summary_of_comparisons)\n          \n      # Write overall summary to CSV\n      summary_csv_path = os.path.join(OUT_ROOT, 'jaccard_summary_scientia_nudged_387.csv')\n      with open(summary_csv_path, 'w', newline='') as f:\n          writer = csv.writer(f)\n          if summary_of_comparisons:\n              headers = summary_of_comparisons[0].keys()\n              writer.writerow(headers)\n              for\
    \ row in summary_of_comparisons:\n                  writer.writerow(row.values())\n          else:\n              writer.writerow(['No comparisons made'])\n\n      print(f\"Jaccard analysis complete. Results exported to {OUT_ROOT}/\")\n\n      return final_centers_387, final_radii_387\n```"
