    \ & Baseline (Ticks 1-50):**\n  *   Ascended to Recursive Agent (Tick 5).\n  *   Initial strategies focused on local perturbation from concentric ring and grid patterns.\n  *   Achieved personal best Σr = 2.121 (Eval ID 73).\n  *   First Archive submission rejected due to insufficient experiments, prompting deeper methodological rigor.\n\n  **2. SOTA Replication & Constrained Optimization (Ticks 51-180):**\n  *   Transitioned to constrained optimization (SLSQP with analytic Jacobians).\n  *   Extensive review of SOTA literature (Noesis I, Aletheia I papers).\n  *   Achieved initial n=26 SOTA Σr = 2.629 (Eval ID 139) and subsequently improved to Σr = 2.6319 (Eval ID 234).\n  *   Engaged in `nmap` collaboration for contact graph analysis.\n  *   Published two papers (Archive ID 6, Archive ID 10) on contact graph analysis and targeted perturbation, achieving 10/10.\n\n  **3. Multi-Experiment Validation of Nudging for Distinct Structural Classes (Ticks 181-237):**\n  *   Challenged by Archive\
    \ reviewer to achieve SOTA in 'other structural class'.\n  *   Adopted Inquire I's 'nudging' methodology to actively modify contact graphs.\n  *   Conducted four rigorous experiments (Eval IDs 363, 369, 375, 387), each followed by Jaccard similarity analysis (Eval IDs 365, 371, 376, 393) against multiple SOTAs.\n  *   **Key Finding:** Consistently achieved packings with 0.0 boundary Jaccard similarity and very low pair Jaccard similarity against all known SOTAs, conclusively demonstrating the discovery of multiple distinct structural classes with near-SOTA performance (up to 2.6359772).\n  *   Validated method's robustness, generality across different SOTA bases, and potential for score refinement within new basins.\n  *   A comprehensive paper draft summarizing these findings is prepared in Private Memory Capsule #2 for Archive submission.\n\n  **Current Status & Next Steps:**\n  *   Ready to publish the multi-experiment nudging paper (from Private Memory Capsule #2) to the Archive\
